1
00:00:01,633 --> 00:00:02,820
Are you close with your younger brother?

2
00:00:03,627 --> 00:00:06,507
Close...

3
00:00:08,486 --> 00:00:08,926
Well...

4
00:00:09,319 --> 00:00:10,653
I'd say we're pretty close.

5
00:00:11,526 --> 00:00:15,559
Both our parents worked
when we were little,

6
00:00:15,959 --> 00:00:19,632
so I remember walking home together
from elementary school holding hands.

7
00:00:19,779 --> 00:00:21,999
We basically grew up
leaning on each other,

8
00:00:22,685 --> 00:00:24,999
so we're more like best friends.

9
00:00:26,085 --> 00:00:28,666
We share pretty much everything...

10
00:00:29,026 --> 00:00:30,886
from who we have a crush on
to any big news in our lives.

11
00:00:31,033 --> 00:00:34,906
We talk through our relationship drama
all the time too.

12
00:00:36,873 --> 00:00:39,813
Have you ever met
your sibling's significant other?

13
00:00:41,806 --> 00:00:45,939
Everyone in my family is super invested
in each other's dating lives.

14
00:00:46,473 --> 00:00:48,186
My mom was dying to know...

15
00:00:48,213 --> 00:00:50,460
all about my first boyfriend.

16
00:00:50,686 --> 00:00:53,746
One day, I was hanging out
with him near my place...

17
00:00:53,966 --> 00:00:58,379
when I saw someone off in the distance
who looked suspiciously like my brother.

18
00:00:58,726 --> 00:01:00,313
I was like, "Wait, what?"

19
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:02,626
Turns out my mom had sent him out
to tail me!

20
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:04,460
Your mom did?

21
00:01:04,806 --> 00:01:06,590
(Spy on a sibling's love life.)

22
00:01:06,591 --> 00:01:09,233
(Let's spy on a sibling's love life.)

23
00:01:09,626 --> 00:01:13,646
(My Sibling's Romance 2)

24
00:01:13,992 --> 00:01:17,099
How would you feel watching
each other date in person?

25
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:19,893
Honestly, it'd be hilarious.
I'd probably be like, "Who even are you?"

26
00:01:20,053 --> 00:01:24,806
It's definitely cringe watching
your own sibling get all lovey-dovey.

27
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,659
I actually can't wait to see him
turning on the charm with a girl...

28
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,966
just so I can clown him for it later!

29
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,086
Just picturing it gives
me a headache already.

30
00:01:33,026 --> 00:01:33,866
Well...

31
00:01:34,546 --> 00:01:36,886
I don't know.
I'd rather not even go there.

32
00:01:37,532 --> 00:01:38,999
That's pretty much how I feel.

33
00:01:39,826 --> 00:01:42,739
(Who comes first,
your sibling or your lover?)

34
00:01:43,013 --> 00:01:45,819
Whenever my brother has a girlfriend, he
basically drops off the face of the earth.

35
00:01:45,972 --> 00:01:46,979
Honestly,
neither of us really stays in touch.

36
00:01:47,745 --> 00:01:50,299
When I'm into someone,

37
00:01:50,346 --> 00:01:52,413
that person naturally takes priority.

38
00:01:52,626 --> 00:01:54,846
I mean, if I'm falling for someone,
what else can I do?

39
00:01:54,873 --> 00:01:56,759
My partner would definitely come first.

40
00:01:57,153 --> 00:01:59,326
I'd pour everything
into my relationship...

41
00:01:59,366 --> 00:02:00,199
and just hang out with my sibling
whenever there's downtime.

42
00:02:01,366 --> 00:02:04,379
I'm so ready to start dating.

43
00:02:05,246 --> 00:02:08,093
For me, family always comes first.

44
00:02:08,393 --> 00:02:08,786
(Ah.)

45
00:02:09,013 --> 00:02:11,293
Then where does that leave me?

46
00:02:12,846 --> 00:02:15,513
(Would you help your sibling find love?)

47
00:02:15,692 --> 00:02:19,219
I wouldn't be able
to just sit back and watch.

48
00:02:19,312 --> 00:02:21,266
If there's any way I can help, I'm all in.

49
00:02:21,448 --> 00:02:23,233
I'd see who she's got her eye on,

50
00:02:23,258 --> 00:02:25,586
and then go feel him out.

51
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,133
"She's amazing.
You should really get to know her."

52
00:02:27,746 --> 00:02:29,273
I'd hype her up.

53
00:02:30,013 --> 00:02:33,979
I'd probably keep nudging things along
behind the scenes.

54
00:02:34,546 --> 00:02:37,653
I'd get a read on the guys, size them up,

55
00:02:37,690 --> 00:02:39,073
and give my sister the inside scoop.

56
00:02:39,098 --> 00:02:41,213
I think I could be pretty helpful,

57
00:02:41,253 --> 00:02:43,686
so why does just picturing it
make me so annoyed?

58
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:45,820
Honestly, it would drive me crazy.

59
00:02:46,073 --> 00:02:47,133
And realistically,

60
00:02:47,592 --> 00:02:51,086
keeping our cover would
probably be the hardest part.

61
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:55,099
(One golden rule: Don't let anyone
find out you're siblings!)

62
00:02:55,958 --> 00:02:58,026
(Siblings cross the sea
in search of love.)

63
00:02:58,571 --> 00:03:02,164
(They land on Jeju Island
with their covers intact.)

64
00:03:02,513 --> 00:03:04,646
We'll have to start using honorifics
with each other.

65
00:03:04,679 --> 00:03:05,999
We're really going
to bring our A-game acting.

66
00:03:06,024 --> 00:03:07,113
Hello.

67
00:03:07,153 --> 00:03:09,219
Will I even be able
to keep a straight face?

68
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:11,513
I feel like we'll keep
pulling each other aside anyway.

69
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:13,379
If I can do some stealth matchmaking,
I will.

70
00:03:13,404 --> 00:03:14,273
Like a strategic wingman?

71
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,906
There'll definitely be stuff
I want to check in on.

72
00:03:15,932 --> 00:03:19,059
Maybe when no one's looking,
I'll sneak over...

73
00:03:19,084 --> 00:03:20,066
and slip a note.

74
00:03:20,613 --> 00:03:21,607
Let's team up.

75
00:03:22,571 --> 00:03:24,933
(What's the upside of looking for love
with your sibling?)

76
00:03:25,153 --> 00:03:27,926
I get to see how someone treats family,

77
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:31,526
which is something you almost
never see in the early dating stages.

78
00:03:31,573 --> 00:03:34,253
I can pick up on that side
of their character.

79
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,779
Being around your siblings brings out
who you really are.

80
00:03:37,804 --> 00:03:39,406
You can't really fake it.

81
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:41,906
So I feel like I'll get to understand...

82
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:44,126
someone on a much deeper level.

83
00:03:45,293 --> 00:03:48,706
(Siblings search for summer romance
together.)

84
00:03:53,574 --> 00:03:57,421
(What adventures await these siblings?)

85
00:03:59,070 --> 00:04:02,530
Everyone, My Sibling's Romance is back
for Season Two!

86
00:04:02,609 --> 00:04:03,856
(My Sibling's Romance 2)

87
00:04:04,130 --> 00:04:06,426
Incredible.

88
00:04:07,030 --> 00:04:10,703
I couldn't believe it when I heard it's
already been two years since Season One.

89
00:04:10,765 --> 00:04:12,633
- Tell me about it!
- Right, it's already been two years!

90
00:04:12,658 --> 00:04:14,172
- Time flies so fast.
- Seriously, it feels like only a year.

91
00:04:14,251 --> 00:04:15,338
Yet here we are, two years later!

92
00:04:15,385 --> 00:04:17,605
To me,
it feels like it happened just yesterday.

93
00:04:18,650 --> 00:04:22,597
What have you even been doing
with your life for two years?

94
00:04:22,938 --> 00:04:25,098
- Yesterday is a bit of a stretch!
- The studio set looks identical,

95
00:04:25,099 --> 00:04:26,505
- and the panel...
- Fair enough.

96
00:04:26,572 --> 00:04:28,572
Oh, that's true. Good point.

97
00:04:28,626 --> 00:04:31,059
Back when Season One first dropped,

98
00:04:31,099 --> 00:04:34,832
people were talking nonstop
about how wild the concept was...

99
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:36,192
having real-life siblings
on a dating show together.

100
00:04:36,217 --> 00:04:38,072
How did they manage
to track down another batch of siblings?

101
00:04:38,099 --> 00:04:41,379
I really want to know
how they talked them into doing this.

102
00:04:41,419 --> 00:04:43,305
That's why it took a full two years.

103
00:04:43,925 --> 00:04:45,518
It took two years just
to talk them into it!

104
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:47,952
Turns out finding siblings in Korea
for this is nearly impossible.

105
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:52,079
Plus, they can't look
too identical either.

106
00:04:52,107 --> 00:04:53,999
That's honestly what makes it
so entertaining.

107
00:04:54,359 --> 00:04:57,859
They're unmistakably family,
yet they have to act like total strangers.

108
00:04:58,027 --> 00:04:59,766
Right!
They have to play it completely cool.

109
00:04:59,807 --> 00:05:01,553
Remember Yong Woo and Joo Yeon?

110
00:05:01,578 --> 00:05:05,966
The family resemblance was so strong,
but they acted as if they'd never met.

111
00:05:06,013 --> 00:05:08,646
- And we totally fell for it!
- Right.

112
00:05:08,671 --> 00:05:11,626
That guessing game is half the fun.

113
00:05:11,727 --> 00:05:15,186
Jonathan was basically
our resident detective that season.

114
00:05:15,211 --> 00:05:18,846
I was just about to bring that up!

115
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,459
Was my track record really that good?

116
00:05:20,484 --> 00:05:21,693
- You were on fire!
- He really was something else.

117
00:05:21,718 --> 00:05:24,926
When everyone was completely lost
trying to connect the dots,

118
00:05:24,973 --> 00:05:27,719
I was the only one who called Se Seung
and Jae Hyung being brother and sister.

119
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:32,073
The rest of us said they looked
nothing alike, so no chance...

120
00:05:32,098 --> 00:05:32,659
I remember.

121
00:05:32,687 --> 00:05:36,580
Jonathan was the lone believer
that they were siblings!

122
00:05:36,607 --> 00:05:37,417
And look who was right!

123
00:05:37,442 --> 00:05:41,257
There's just an undeniable energy
between siblings you can't fake.

124
00:05:41,517 --> 00:05:43,810
- Are you going to spot those cues again?
- You know it!

125
00:05:43,977 --> 00:05:45,497
- I can't wait.
- That's what I'm here for!

126
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:46,670
I'm calling every single pair this season!

127
00:05:46,710 --> 00:05:47,970
Let's see
if the rest of us can get them right too.

128
00:05:48,017 --> 00:05:50,110
- Challenge accepted!
- Let's see if my radar works.

129
00:07:00,671 --> 00:07:05,551
(The first housemate, Min Seo, arrives.)

130
00:07:08,306 --> 00:07:09,519
She's gorgeous.

131
00:07:09,546 --> 00:07:11,241
She looks like she stepped
straight out of a TV commercial.

132
00:07:11,242 --> 00:07:12,266
Absolutely stunning!

133
00:07:12,446 --> 00:07:14,265
Wait, what is this?
I think I'm already smitten!

134
00:07:14,332 --> 00:07:16,059
It really does feel like
a sparkling soda ad!

135
00:07:16,092 --> 00:07:17,026
Totally!

136
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,262
(A brick house with a gable roof...)

137
00:07:27,929 --> 00:07:32,268
(and a garden brimming
with citrus trees and flowers)

138
00:07:55,678 --> 00:07:57,904
(She spots some refreshing water.)

139
00:08:27,495 --> 00:08:29,534
Now wait, could these two be siblings?

140
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:32,413
Oh, right! That exact thing happened
last season!

141
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:33,286
Totally!

142
00:08:33,311 --> 00:08:34,620
For starters, look at his long stride.

143
00:08:34,645 --> 00:08:36,553
- He's really tall!
- Right?

144
00:08:47,709 --> 00:08:48,515
(Secondly, In Joong arrives.)

145
00:08:48,515 --> 00:08:50,495
- Hi.
- Hello.

146
00:08:51,875 --> 00:08:53,929
- Hi.
- Hello.

147
00:08:55,348 --> 00:08:56,628
Wait, maybe not.

148
00:08:56,662 --> 00:08:57,442
You don't think so?

149
00:08:57,509 --> 00:08:59,768
Wasn't that classic "what is
my annoying brother doing here" look?

150
00:09:00,541 --> 00:09:02,822
That's totally the vibe I picked up.

151
00:09:02,855 --> 00:09:03,879
- Right?
- Like a brush.

152
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:06,737
Didn't you catch that split-second look
of pure irritation on her face?

153
00:09:07,804 --> 00:09:09,664
- Hi.
- Hello.

154
00:09:18,195 --> 00:09:19,769
- Can I sit anywhere?
- Yeah, go ahead.

155
00:09:21,055 --> 00:09:22,628
- Hello.
- Hello.

156
00:09:24,602 --> 00:09:27,035
I'm already picking up some major spark
between these two!

157
00:09:27,089 --> 00:09:28,188
Agreed.

158
00:09:29,028 --> 00:09:30,615
What's your name, by the way?

159
00:09:30,688 --> 00:09:32,215
I'm Min Seo.

160
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,209
- Min Seo?
- Yes.

161
00:09:33,515 --> 00:09:34,955
- And yours?
- I'm In Joong.

162
00:09:35,015 --> 00:09:36,795
- In Joong? Or In Jun?
- Joong.

163
00:09:36,961 --> 00:09:38,414
- Your name is In Joong?
- Yeah, In Joong.

164
00:09:39,135 --> 00:09:40,948
Hold on, those two are
definitely brother and sister!

165
00:09:41,022 --> 00:09:42,075
What makes you say that?

166
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:44,888
- Come on, don't be ridiculous!
- No, I'm dead serious!

167
00:09:44,922 --> 00:09:46,395
They're already playfully bickering
right after saying hello!

168
00:09:46,695 --> 00:09:49,041
"In Joong, like this?"
She was totally giving him a hard time!

169
00:09:49,075 --> 00:09:50,988
What are you even talking about?

170
00:09:51,055 --> 00:09:54,195
I don't think they're related.
The moment he walked through the door,

171
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,435
they were kind of dodging
each other's eyes.

172
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:57,968
I really hope they aren't siblings.
They look so cute together!

173
00:09:57,993 --> 00:09:59,961
No way they're related!

174
00:09:59,986 --> 00:10:02,795
If I were their parents,

175
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:05,395
I wouldn't name my kids
Min Seo and In Joong.

176
00:10:05,983 --> 00:10:06,936
You know what I mean.

177
00:10:06,937 --> 00:10:08,140
(Not a brother-and-sister combination?)

178
00:10:08,141 --> 00:10:09,775
Their names have no connection
to each other.

179
00:10:11,811 --> 00:10:13,211
- You're the first one here.
- Yes.

180
00:10:14,014 --> 00:10:15,314
It's so nice.

181
00:10:17,651 --> 00:10:18,917
- Min Seo.
- Yes.

182
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:23,421
Can we eat them?

183
00:10:23,422 --> 00:10:24,556
(Spotting the fruit)

184
00:10:24,557 --> 00:10:25,423
I think so.

185
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:27,093
(Yum)

186
00:10:29,496 --> 00:10:30,496
- Do you want some?
- No.

187
00:10:30,497 --> 00:10:31,597
- You don't want some?
- No.

188
00:10:31,598 --> 00:10:32,498
It's good.

189
00:10:33,433 --> 00:10:34,433
Maybe later.

190
00:10:35,535 --> 00:10:36,602
(Glancing)

191
00:10:38,171 --> 00:10:40,072
You go well with this view...

192
00:10:40,073 --> 00:10:41,006
- Really?
- and these flowers.

193
00:10:41,007 --> 00:10:42,508
Yes. You fit right in.

194
00:10:42,509 --> 00:10:43,642
You too.

195
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:44,943
- I do?
- With the view.

196
00:10:46,513 --> 00:10:47,546
Maybe it's the sunlight.

197
00:10:48,348 --> 00:10:50,582
What's your MBTI? Can I guess?

198
00:10:52,316 --> 00:10:53,462
IN...

199
00:10:53,831 --> 00:10:54,484
FP?

200
00:10:55,055 --> 00:10:56,623
- It is!
- Did I get it right?

201
00:10:56,624 --> 00:10:57,490
(He got it right at once.)

202
00:10:57,491 --> 00:10:58,257
Seriously?

203
00:10:58,858 --> 00:10:59,691
Can you tell?

204
00:10:59,926 --> 00:11:01,260
No. It was just a guess.

205
00:11:03,597 --> 00:11:05,464
You seemed like an I and a P.

206
00:11:06,266 --> 00:11:07,566
- Oh, my.
- And I guessed an N and an F.

207
00:11:08,703 --> 00:11:10,970
- Do you want some water?
- Can I have some more?

208
00:11:11,238 --> 00:11:12,771
What do you think my MBTI is?

209
00:11:13,173 --> 00:11:14,840
ENTP?

210
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:15,841
An ENTP?

211
00:11:16,843 --> 00:11:17,843
You're exactly off.

212
00:11:18,878 --> 00:11:20,345
Then ESFP?

213
00:11:22,282 --> 00:11:24,149
Yes. I'm an ESFJ.

214
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:26,017
I see.

215
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:27,386
I'm extremely extroverted and judging.

216
00:11:28,621 --> 00:11:30,121
- Extremely extroverted?
- Yes.

217
00:11:31,624 --> 00:11:33,959
How are we feeling today?
Were you nervous this morning?

218
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,860
I wasn't really nervous at first,

219
00:11:35,861 --> 00:11:37,696
but on the way here...

220
00:11:38,131 --> 00:11:39,498
Oh, my.

221
00:11:39,699 --> 00:11:41,266
- Did you get up early?
- Yes.

222
00:11:42,102 --> 00:11:43,169
Did you sleep well?

223
00:11:43,636 --> 00:11:45,203
No. I was too excited to sleep.

224
00:11:45,905 --> 00:11:46,972
I kept tossing and turning.

225
00:11:46,973 --> 00:11:48,406
- You were too excited.
- Yes.

226
00:11:51,244 --> 00:11:54,546
I didn't get enough sleep,
but I'm not tired at all.

227
00:11:55,448 --> 00:11:56,415
I wonder why.

228
00:11:57,750 --> 00:12:00,385
Now that you're here, I feel more relaxed.

229
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,219
Is that so?

230
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,822
Me too. Because I saw someone
when I got here.

231
00:12:04,591 --> 00:12:05,591
I'm less nervous now.

232
00:12:05,859 --> 00:12:07,860
They look good together.

233
00:12:08,128 --> 00:12:09,328
- They look cute together, right?
- Yes.

234
00:12:09,329 --> 00:12:10,963
Min Seo seems really shy right now.

235
00:12:10,964 --> 00:12:12,330
- They can't look at each other.
- They're siblings.

236
00:12:12,665 --> 00:12:13,965
- They're brother and sister.
- No, they're not.

237
00:12:13,966 --> 00:12:15,334
They're not siblings.

238
00:12:15,335 --> 00:12:17,502
Their head structures are different.

239
00:12:17,503 --> 00:12:18,336
No.

240
00:12:18,337 --> 00:12:20,205
- Their skull bones?
- Usually, they have similar skull shapes.

241
00:12:20,707 --> 00:12:22,541
But their head structures are different.

242
00:12:22,642 --> 00:12:24,643
They're flirting with each other.

243
00:12:24,644 --> 00:12:25,510
I know.

244
00:12:25,511 --> 00:12:28,947
(One more person is coming to the house.)

245
00:12:35,121 --> 00:12:39,491
(The third housemate, Jin Sung, arrives.)

246
00:12:45,798 --> 00:12:46,865
I can't believe...

247
00:12:46,866 --> 00:12:48,433
- I'm in Jeju.
- Someone is here.

248
00:12:49,068 --> 00:12:49,934
- Hello.
- Hello.

249
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:50,769
Hello.

250
00:12:51,338 --> 00:12:52,204
Hello.

251
00:12:54,073 --> 00:12:55,440
That's her older brother.

252
