00:24:32,842 --> 00:24:34,340
I'll sit over there.

522
00:24:34,742 --> 00:24:37,682
(She takes a seat
between Dong Su and Jin Sung.)

523
00:24:37,889 --> 00:24:40,212
I didn't expect
so many people to be here already.

524
00:24:41,046 --> 00:24:42,348
What's your name?

525
00:24:42,389 --> 00:24:44,016
I'm Yu Ra.

526
00:24:44,416 --> 00:24:45,369
- Yu Ra.
- Yu Ra?

527
00:24:45,396 --> 00:24:46,485
- Yu Ra?
- Yu Ra.

528
00:24:46,669 --> 00:24:48,520
Weren't you nervous when you came here?

529
00:24:48,582 --> 00:24:49,489
I was so nervous.

530
00:24:49,491 --> 00:24:50,456
I was really nervous.

531
00:24:50,736 --> 00:24:52,149
I thought my heart was going to burst.

532
00:24:52,151 --> 00:24:53,425
- Really?
- Seriously?

533
00:24:54,026 --> 00:24:56,393
What do you do for fun, Yu Ra?

534
00:24:56,682 --> 00:24:58,731
If I had to pick one thing,
it'd be exercising.

535
00:24:58,841 --> 00:24:59,865
- Exercising?
- Yes.

536
00:24:59,934 --> 00:25:01,467
I just go running by myself.

537
00:25:01,694 --> 00:25:03,235
- Do you like running?
- Right.

538
00:25:03,635 --> 00:25:06,805
I also do a lot of walking
under the guise of window-shopping.

539
00:25:07,627 --> 00:25:09,208
Oh, shopping!

540
00:25:09,394 --> 00:25:10,376
Like shopping for exercise?

541
00:25:10,642 --> 00:25:11,510
Something like that.

542
00:25:14,421 --> 00:25:16,382
What's your MBTI?

543
00:25:16,761 --> 00:25:18,817
I'm an ISFJ.

544
00:25:19,815 --> 00:25:21,322
Another different MBTI type.

545
00:25:21,322 --> 00:25:22,488
Are there any other ISFJs here?

546
00:25:22,615 --> 00:25:24,923
- We all have different MBTI types.
- We're all different.

547
00:25:24,923 --> 00:25:26,925
So are all seven of us different?

548
00:25:27,002 --> 00:25:28,594
But Min Seo is the only introvert.

549
00:25:29,441 --> 00:25:30,662
We're fellow introverts.

550
00:25:31,175 --> 00:25:32,965
You two must be able
to lean on each other a lot.

551
00:25:32,967 --> 00:25:33,899
Good.

552
00:25:34,406 --> 00:25:35,834
In Joong and Yu Ra look like siblings.

553
00:25:36,115 --> 00:25:37,162
They even smile alike.

554
00:25:37,164 --> 00:25:37,903
You're right.

555
00:25:38,270 --> 00:25:40,439
The corners of their mouths
seem to turn down a little.

556
00:25:41,006 --> 00:25:43,006
Their eyes look similar too.

557
00:25:44,030 --> 00:25:45,878
Can you tell me your name once again?

558
00:25:46,250 --> 00:25:47,513
I'm Dong Su.

559
00:25:47,515 --> 00:25:48,514
Dong Su, I see.

560
00:25:49,723 --> 00:25:52,818
Min Seo, In Joong, Ye In, and Jwa Hyeon.

561
00:25:54,668 --> 00:25:55,821
And Jun Sung.

562
00:25:56,088 --> 00:25:57,856
- I'm Jin Sung.
- Oh, Jin Sung.

563
00:25:59,268 --> 00:26:00,994
You sure are good at remembering names.

564
00:26:01,521 --> 00:26:02,528
See?

565
00:26:02,894 --> 00:26:04,594
You know what I'm saying, right?

566
00:26:04,763 --> 00:26:05,731
You already figured it out?

567
00:26:05,748 --> 00:26:06,899
I'll find them all today.

568
00:26:28,079 --> 00:26:33,086
(The eighth housemate, Ji Hwan, arrives.)

569
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:36,195
He's handsome.

570
00:26:37,062 --> 00:26:39,731
I have absolutely no idea.
Could he be Min Seo's brother?

571
00:26:40,199 --> 00:26:41,066
Wait a minute.

572
00:26:41,066 --> 00:26:42,301
I'm completely stumped.

573
00:26:57,939 --> 00:26:59,193
- Hello.
- Hi.

574
00:26:59,193 --> 00:27:01,086
- Hi.
- Nice to meet you.

575
00:27:01,753 --> 00:27:03,222
My name is Ji Hwan.

576
00:27:03,856 --> 00:27:05,457
My name is Ji Hwan.

577
00:27:05,659 --> 00:27:07,911
(An introduction
faster than anyone else's)

578
00:27:07,913 --> 00:27:09,279
That was a quick introduction.

579
00:27:11,771 --> 00:27:14,624
(While waiting to enter a moment ago)

580
00:27:14,923 --> 00:27:18,064
(Practicing his introduction
without his last name)

581
00:27:18,085 --> 00:27:19,238
I'm Ji Hwan.

582
00:27:19,365 --> 00:27:20,672
- I'm Ji Hwan.
- Good.

583
00:27:20,672 --> 00:27:22,499
(He practiced so hard that...)

584
00:27:23,199 --> 00:27:25,392
(he blurted out his name
the moment he arrived.)

585
00:27:25,393 --> 00:27:26,345
Nice to meet you all.

586
00:27:26,452 --> 00:27:30,349
When he walked in,
he just blurted out, "My name is Ji Hwan."

587
00:27:31,083 --> 00:27:34,319
Ji Hwan made
the strongest first impression on me.

588
00:27:34,430 --> 00:27:36,121
He walked in, saying his name.

589
00:27:36,722 --> 00:27:37,990
It was pretty unusual.

590
00:27:39,455 --> 00:27:42,302
(He made a strong impression
the moment he walked in.)

591
00:27:42,508 --> 00:27:44,008
What was his name again?

592
00:27:44,008 --> 00:27:45,564
I'm Ji Hwan.

593
00:27:45,582 --> 00:27:46,732
- Ji Hwan?
- Ji Hwan.

594
00:27:47,389 --> 00:27:50,002
Ji Hwan and Jwa Hyeon sound
kind of similar.

595
00:27:50,969 --> 00:27:52,533
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

596
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:56,808
When Ji Hwan came in,

597
00:27:57,075 --> 00:28:01,086
my eyes went straight to him.

598
00:28:01,293 --> 00:28:03,782
He's really tall, for one thing.

599
00:28:03,820 --> 00:28:06,118
And he was sitting right across from me,

600
00:28:06,193 --> 00:28:07,653
so I kept noticing him.

601
00:28:08,506 --> 00:28:11,684
My MBTI is INTJ.

602
00:28:12,264 --> 00:28:14,960
I enjoy cooking,

603
00:28:15,578 --> 00:28:18,697
listening to music, and singing.

604
00:28:19,691 --> 00:28:21,533
I also watch a lot of movies...

605
00:28:21,642 --> 00:28:24,469
and like analyzing them
and figuring things out.

606
00:28:25,003 --> 00:28:26,705
What kind of movies do you like?

607
00:28:26,842 --> 00:28:28,916
I really like movies
with ambiguous endings.

608
00:28:31,182 --> 00:28:36,020
I also like movies
based on mystery novels...

609
00:28:36,313 --> 00:28:38,617
and horror movies.

610
00:28:39,140 --> 00:28:41,853
I found Ji Hwan's vibe really attractive.

611
00:28:41,913 --> 00:28:43,989
He spoke slowly...

612
00:28:44,067 --> 00:28:47,226
and talked about himself in depth.

613
00:28:47,353 --> 00:28:51,430
He seemed very laid-back.

614
00:28:51,627 --> 00:28:54,333
He has a relaxed vibe.

615
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:56,368
He speaks calmly,

616
00:28:56,368 --> 00:28:57,810
but he still gets everything
he wants to say across...

617
00:28:57,834 --> 00:28:59,071
without raising his voice.

618
00:28:59,100 --> 00:29:00,973
I'm in the middle
between E and I and F and T.

619
00:29:01,007 --> 00:29:03,208
I like cooking...

620
00:29:03,394 --> 00:29:06,511
and singing, so I go to karaoke a lot.

621
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:08,247
(The two share similar hobbies.)

622
00:29:08,260 --> 00:29:09,314
We have a lot in common.

623
00:29:09,347 --> 00:29:11,383
Yes, we like a lot of the same things.

624
00:29:11,466 --> 00:29:13,619
So now we have a running group...

625
00:29:13,619 --> 00:29:15,354
- and a karaoke group.
- Yes.

626
00:29:16,279 --> 00:29:18,033
(Q. What was your sibling like?)

627
00:29:18,133 --> 00:29:19,091
She looked the best.

628
00:29:20,926 --> 00:29:22,094
She had a different aura.

629
00:29:22,424 --> 00:29:25,197
My brother was impressive, as expected.

630
00:29:27,165 --> 00:29:28,634
She was even worse.

631
00:29:30,564 --> 00:29:31,870
"What's wrong with him?"

632
00:29:32,738 --> 00:29:33,705
Gosh.

633
00:29:34,002 --> 00:29:35,607
"Why is he trying so hard
to look handsome?"

634
00:29:36,942 --> 00:29:37,895
Goodness!

635
00:29:39,202 --> 00:29:41,513
They were actually thinking that
about their siblings?

636
00:29:41,675 --> 00:29:43,862
So they're all actually siblings, then.

637
00:29:44,329 --> 00:29:45,900
That means everyone's here now.

638
00:29:46,033 --> 00:29:47,520
"Why is he trying so hard
to look handsome?"

639
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:49,560
I couldn't stand...

640
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:51,760
how he was trying so hard to look
handsome.

641
00:29:53,825 --> 00:29:55,213
(Q. Did you manage to act like strangers
with your sibling?)

642
00:29:55,214 --> 00:29:57,262
Yes. I think we nailed it.

643
00:29:57,632 --> 00:30:00,465
We don't really look alike.

644
00:30:00,623 --> 00:30:01,627
Or do we?

645
00:30:02,250 --> 00:30:03,502
I don't think they caught on.

646
00:30:04,495 --> 00:30:07,106
We just sold it, honestly.

647
00:30:08,038 --> 00:30:09,141
I'm in trouble.

648
00:30:09,549 --> 00:30:12,311
The guys are all so good-looking.

649
00:30:13,001 --> 00:30:15,748
Like, all of them. Seriously.

650
00:30:16,110 --> 00:30:17,945
All the guys here...

651
00:30:17,946 --> 00:30:20,385
are tall and good-looking.

652
00:30:20,834 --> 00:30:22,211
That's just unfair.

653
00:30:22,212 --> 00:30:23,289
In Joong.

654
00:30:23,669 --> 00:30:25,366
He looked tall even sitting down.

655
00:30:25,367 --> 00:30:28,627
And he's got that idol face.

656
00:30:29,313 --> 00:30:31,329
So I was like,
"Okay, he's tough competition."

657
00:30:31,330 --> 00:30:32,664
That's what went through my head.

658
00:30:33,193 --> 00:30:35,792
There are two people I'm curious about.

659
00:30:35,793 --> 00:30:36,961
But...

660
00:30:36,962 --> 00:30:39,938
they're totally different types.

661
00:30:40,330 --> 00:30:43,041
So I want to talk to both of them more.

662
00:30:43,108 --> 00:30:46,144
(Eight siblings have moved in.)

663
00:30:46,231 --> 00:30:48,231
Compared to Season One,

664
00:30:48,233 --> 00:30:50,233
everyone was way more nervous...

665
00:30:50,235 --> 00:30:51,638
and awkward back then.

666
00:30:51,639 --> 00:30:54,217
This time, the vibe is bright and bold.

667
00:30:54,219 --> 00:30:56,093
And everyone's more chill.

668
00:30:56,094 --> 00:30:57,321
- If that makes sense.
- Yeah.

669
00:30:57,813 --> 00:30:59,510
I'm thinking Min Seo and In Joong.

670
00:30:59,511 --> 00:31:02,809
Ye In and Ji Hwan.
They're definitely siblings.

671
00:31:03,138 --> 00:31:04,896
They couldn't fool me.

672
00:31:05,921 --> 00:31:06,865
Nice try.

673
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:08,667
I see.

674
00:31:08,827 --> 00:31:10,001
That makes zero sense.

675
00:31:10,302 --> 00:31:11,804
What about you, CODE KUNST?

676
00:31:11,806 --> 00:31:13,997
I say Ye In and Dong Su.

677
00:31:14,210 --> 00:31:15,165
Ye In and Dong Su.

678
00:31:15,166 --> 00:31:17,643
In Joong and Yu Ra.

679
00:31:17,964 --> 00:31:19,311
I think they're siblings.

680
00:31:19,702 --> 00:31:21,697
Same. Ye In and Dong Su.

681
00:31:21,698 --> 00:31:23,546
Jwa Hyeon and Ji Hwan.

682
00:31:23,547 --> 00:31:25,016
In Joong and Yu Ra.

683
00:31:25,805 --> 00:31:28,019
And Min Seo and Jin Sung.

684
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:30,576
- Min Seo and Jin Sung?
- I'm thinking...

685
00:31:30,577 --> 00:31:33,792
Jin Sung and Ye In.

686
00:31:34,261 --> 00:31:35,588
Did you even watch?

687
00:31:35,589 --> 00:31:37,131
Yes, I did!

688
00:31:37,132 --> 00:31:38,519
- Jwa Hyeon and Ji Hwan?
- Yes.

689
00:31:38,520 --> 00:31:40,506
Ji Hwan and Jwa Hyeon.

690
00:31:40,508 --> 00:31:42,164
- Were you dozing off?
- No way.

691
00:31:42,165 --> 00:31:44,068
Dong Su and Min Seo give sibling vibes.

692
00:31:45,444 --> 00:31:46,371
No?

693
00:31:46,604 --> 00:31:47,606
Is my radar just trash?

694
00:31:47,612 --> 00:31:48,962
Dong Su and Ye In.

695
00:31:48,963 --> 00:31:51,644
- I swear it's Min Seo and In Joong.
- Wrong.

696
00:31:51,645 --> 00:31:54,712
Your radar is looking shaky this time.

697
00:31:54,713 --> 00:31:57,082
(Trash radar alert)

698
00:32:04,456 --> 00:32:06,658
(In Joong)

699
00:32:09,961 --> 00:32:11,830
(Min Seo)

700
00:32:14,232 --> 00:32:16,000
(Yu Ra)

701
00:32:19,104 --> 00:32:20,806
(Ji Hwan)

702
00:32:23,942 --> 00:32:25,677
(Ye In)

703
00:32:27,712 --> 00:32:29,647
(Jwa Hyeon)

704
00:32:32,984 --> 00:32:34,552
(Dong Su)

705
00:32:37,289 --> 00:32:39,324
(Jin Sung)

706
00:32:47,899 --> 00:32:52,771
(My Sibling's Romance 2)

707
00:32:59,059 --> 00:33:00,812
Shall we look around?

708
00:33:00,814 --> 00:33:02,180
- Shall we?
- Sure.

709
00:33:03,250 --> 00:33:05,250
- Finally.
- I'm so hyped.

710
00:33:06,225 --> 00:33:09,087
I thought the path was so pretty.

711
00:33:09,297 --> 00:33:11,456
- This path?
- Yeah, this one.

712
00:33:11,808 --> 00:33:13,598
I love all the flowers.

713
00:33:15,596 --> 00:33:16,454
A hut.

714
00:33:17,127 --> 00:33:18,162
So cute.

715
00:33:19,939 --> 00:33:21,939
The vibe here is so good.

716
00:33:22,068 --> 00:33:23,841
- If we hang out here...
- Right?

717
00:33:23,842 --> 00:33:25,571
- over a beer.
- Heart-to-heart.

718
00:33:26,273 --> 00:33:27,839
It's literally for that deep talk.

719
00:33:29,016 --> 00:33:29,936
Aren't you hungry?

720
00:33:30,198 --> 00:33:31,277
I'm getting hungry.

721
00:33:31,278 --> 00:33:32,544
- Right?
- Yeah.

722
00:33:33,099 --> 00:33:34,246
Nice.

723
00:33:35,046 --> 00:33:37,129
Oh, nice. There are yoga mats.

724
00:33:37,130 --> 00:33:39,050
We can play catch too.

725
00:33:46,926 --> 00:33:48,158
Which way do we go?

726
00:33:48,159 --> 00:33:49,861
(Lost at the front door)

727
00:33:49,982 --> 00:33:50,962
I think it's this way.

728
00:33:59,237 --> 00:34:03,775
(First floor living room)

729
00:34:05,032 --> 00:34:06,144
This is so nice.

730
00:34:06,797 --> 00:34:08,079
It's so cute and cozy.

731
00:34:15,353 --> 00:34:18,433
(They head to the second floor.)

732
00:34:18,434 --> 00:34:19,391
It's nice.

733
00:34:22,544 --> 00:34:24,211
- No way.
- Wow.

734
00:34:24,663 --> 00:34:26,107
(Second floor living room)

735
00:34:26,108 --> 00:34:28,333
The second floor is amazing.

736
00:34:28,658 --> 00:34:30,502
I'm lying here every single day.

737
00:34:30,800 --> 00:34:31,836
It's so pretty.

738
00:34:32,779 --> 00:34:34,205
The view is gorgeous too.

739
00:34:34,207 --> 00:34:35,642
Doesn't this feel like Jeju Island?

740
00:34:35,643 --> 00:34:36,841
I love it.

741
00:34:37,554 --> 00:34:38,977
There's a coffee machine.

742
00:34:39,438 --> 00:34:41,241
- Board games too.
- Ooh, fun.

743
00:34:41,242 --> 00:34:43,915
We can all hang here in the evening.

744
00:34:44,841 --> 00:34:45,951
Is this a room?

745
00:34:46,987 --> 00:34:47,919
Wow.

746
00:34:48,361 --> 00:34:49,947
It's a dressing room.

747
00:34:49,948 --> 00:34:52,190
- I'm obsessed.
- It's so pretty.

748
00:34:53,126 --> 00:34:54,426
Third floor next?

749
00:34:57,699 --> 00:34:59,598
Are all the rooms up here?

750
00:34:59,600 --> 00:35:01,066
(Two attics on the third floor)

751
00:35:01,955 --> 00:35:03,835
Oh, this must be the women's room.

752
00:35:03,837 --> 00:35:06,037
It's giving college trip vibes.

753
00:35:06,039 --> 00:35:08,339
- A group trip.
- It's so cute.

754
00:35:10,642 --> 00:35:12,730
The guys' room is right across.

755
00:35:12,731 --> 00:35:15,080
Oh, that's the guys' room.

756
00:35:15,147 --> 00:35:16,462
(Third floor men's room)

757
00:35:16,463 --> 00:35:18,082
- It's bigger.
- Right?

758
00:35:19,756 --> 00:35:20,718
Wow.

759
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:22,453
It's so cute.

760
00:35:24,058 --> 00:35:25,732
Let's all get along.

761
00:35:25,733 --> 00:35:26,925
Yeah, let's get along.

762
00:35:31,037 --> 00:35:32,912
Isn't the house gorgeous?

763
00:35:32,913 --> 00:35:34,681
Total aesthetic stay.

764
00:35:34,682 --> 00:35:36,187
- That's right.
- Peak Jeju vibes.

765
00:35:36,188 --> 00:35:38,492
When you travel as a group,

766
00:35:38,494 --> 00:35:40,879
- an Airbnb beats a hotel.
- So true.

767
00:35:40,881 --> 00:35:42,351
- Definitely.
- And it feels cozy.

768
00:35:42,353 --> 00:35:44,909
Plus you can all cook together,
so it's more comfortable.

769
00:35:45,028 --> 00:35:47,713
- You could really bond in there.
- Yeah.

770
00:35:48,532 --> 00:35:50,647
Someone's going to sit there
and cry their eyes out.

771
00:35:50,649 --> 00:35:51,883
Oh, no.

772
00:35:54,085 --> 00:35:56,855
- Let's eat.
- Enjoy.

773
00:35:57,254 --> 00:35:59,013
- Shall we say cheers?
- Our very first one.

774
00:35:59,014 --> 00:36:00,091
Yes, of course.

775
00:36:00,881 --> 00:36:03,528
- Cheers.
- Nice to meet you all.

776
00:36:07,080 --> 00:36:08,466
I'll try some hijiki.

777
00:36:08,938 --> 00:36:11,103
Is this hijiki?

778
00:36:11,755 --> 00:36:13,104
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

779
00:36:22,384 --> 00:36:25,566
I wish we could take group pictures.

780
00:36:25,568 --> 00:36:26,768
That would be so nice.

781
00:36:26,770 --> 00:36:28,587
I saw a Polaroid camera upstairs.

782
00:36:28,588 --> 00:36:30,530
- Really?
- Yes.

783
00:36:30,532 --> 00:36:31,917
I'm really good at taking photos.

784
00:36:31,918 --> 00:36:32,990
I'll take them for you.

785
00:36:33,641 --> 00:36:35,494
- But then you won't be in any.
- Yeah.

786
00:36:35,496 --> 00:36:38,063
Oh, me? Good point.

787
00:36:38,838 --> 00:36:40,838
I'll try a selfie.

788
00:36:41,294 --> 00:36:43,267
Polaroid selfies aren't easy.

789
00:36:45,273 --> 00:36:47,272
Don't you guys want meat?

790
00:36:47,500 --> 00:36:48,940
There's meat?

791
00:36:50,211 --> 00:36:51,209
Yeah.

792
00:36:51,713 --> 00:36:53,545
We only had fish over here.

793
00:36:54,060 --> 00:36:55,247
We have meat too.

794
00:36:55,637 --> 00:36:56,432
Would you like some?

795
00:36:56,433 --> 00:36:58,583
All the meat ended up over here.

796
00:36:58,984 --> 00:36:59,918
Pork?

797
00:37:02,910 --> 00:37:04,252
Is this beef?

798
00:37:04,253 --> 00:37:05,536
I can't really tell.

799
00:37:05,537 --> 00:37:06,624
I think it's beef.

800
00:37:08,727 --> 00:37:09,928
Mmm.

801
00:37:10,831 --> 00:37:12,171
It's like a cooking show.

802
00:37:12,172 --> 00:37:13,631
Like a total meat expert.

803
00:37:14,136 --> 00:37:15,166
Yeah? Then I'm a judge.

804
00:37:19,976 --> 00:37:21,528
Ye In and Dong Su...

805
00:37:21,529 --> 00:37:23,529
were super chatty.

806
00:37:23,854 --> 00:37:27,179
And I think their outfits
were similar colors too.

807
00:37:28,628 --> 00:37:29,814
Yep, it's beef.

808
00:37:30,570 --> 00:37:32,050
How could you tell?

809
00:37:32,684 --> 00:37:35,920
You were just poking at the greens.

810
00:37:36,284 --> 00:37:38,990
They just bounced off each other
so naturally.

811
00:37:39,710 --> 00:37:41,760
I thought maybe they're siblings.

812
00:37:42,092 --> 00:37:46,131
Dong Su is kind of funny.

813
00:37:46,926 --> 00:37:49,167
My type is Ji Hwan, but...

814
00:37:54,112 --> 00:37:56,574
Dong Su might be the best-looking.

815
00:38:00,424 --> 00:38:01,346
Wait, what?

816
00:38:01,540 --> 00:38:02,703
She keeps flip-flopping.

817
00:38:02,704 --> 00:38:04,048
She's blushing.

818
00:38:04,732 --> 00:38:07,452
Don't those two kind of look alike?

819
00:38:07,816 --> 00:38:10,288
Dong Su and Ji Hwan.

820
00:38:11,968 --> 00:38:14,993
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

821
00:38:15,884 --> 00:38:19,130
This one's Mafia,
and there are a lot of roles.

822
00:38:19,340 --> 00:38:21,805
This "Image cards game" looks fun.

823
00:38:21,806 --> 00:38:22,901
And simple.

824
00:38:23,664 --> 00:38:26,792
Oh, this is perfect for...

825
00:38:26,793 --> 00:38:27,845
first impressions.

826
00:38:27,846 --> 00:38:29,240
Intuitive.

827
00:38:29,549 --> 00:38:30,976
Nice and easy.

828
00:38:31,574 --> 00:38:32,744
No getting mad.

829
00:38:33,476 --> 00:38:34,782
Already?

830
00:38:34,783 --> 00:38:36,246
Then I'll go first.

831
00:38:36,247 --> 00:38:37,849
(Min Seo goes first.)

832
00:38:39,384 --> 00:38:41,107
(Who seems like
they had their first kiss the latest?)

833
00:38:41,108 --> 00:38:43,434
- Whoa, that's the question?
- That's on there?

834
00:38:43,435 --> 00:38:44,224
Oh, wow.

835
00:38:44,225 --> 00:38:46,227
Season Two is going bold.

836
00:38:46,228 --> 00:38:47,947
So bold.

837
00:38:47,948 --> 00:38:48,893
Right off the bat.

838
00:38:49,891 --> 00:38:53,598
To think you have to sit with your sibling
and talk about stuff like that.

839
00:38:54,193 --> 00:38:55,699
- I know, right?
- It's insane!

840
00:38:55,700 --> 00:38:57,435
- It'll be so hard.
- And so uncomfortable.

841
00:38:57,437 --> 00:39:00,833
I pictured having that talk
with my own sibling.

842
00:39:01,859 --> 00:39:03,320
It'd be brutal.

843
00:39:03,321 --> 00:39:04,909
What do you even do?

844
00:39:05,093 --> 00:39:06,613
Just pick your brother.

845
00:39:06,615 --> 00:39:07,803
Ooh, this could give it away.

846
00:39:07,804 --> 00:39:09,347
It would show!

847
00:39:10,849 --> 00:39:22,928
(Who seems like
they had their first kiss the latest?)

848
00:39:28,915 --> 00:39:30,011
- Here.
- Me?

849
00:39:30,012 --> 00:39:30,785
What's the question?

850
00:39:30,786 --> 00:39:32,367
- Do I read it out loud?
- Yes.

851
00:39:32,368 --> 00:39:33,604
It's a bit embarrassing.

852
00:39:35,513 --> 00:39:36,400
Huh?

853
00:39:36,401 --> 00:39:37,683
Wow, this is harsh.

854
00:39:37,686 --> 00:39:38,710
Sorry.

855
00:39:39,064 --> 00:39:43,561
"Who seems like they had
their first kiss the latest?"

856
00:39:45,029 --> 00:39:46,317
Ouch, that one hurts.

857
00:39:46,815 --> 00:39:50,456
Defend yourself or explain the pick.

858
00:39:50,458 --> 00:39:52,824
But any reason would make it weirder.

859
00:39:53,378 --> 00:39:55,969
There are tons of questions like this.

860
00:39:55,970 --> 00:39:57,094
- Really?
- Wow.

861
00:39:57,095 --> 00:39:58,719
There's a whole category.

862
00:39:58,744 --> 00:40:00,521
I think you should just take it.

863
00:40:01,165 --> 00:40:02,551
I'll take it as mine, then.

864
00:40:03,531 --> 00:40:04,764
Are you agreeing with that?

865
00:40:04,824 --> 00:40:06,258
I'm not saying I agree, but...

866
00:40:06,925 --> 00:40:08,004
I disagree, but...

867
00:40:09,051 --> 00:40:10,064
It's the first question, so sure.

868
00:40:10,298 --> 00:40:11,738
(He coolly takes the first card.)

869
00:40:12,278 --> 00:40:14,131
(Ye In's turn)

870
00:40:16,110 --> 00:40:18,317
I feel like this one's
going to hurt someone's feelings.

871
00:40:19,270 --> 00:40:20,970
- What is it?
- What is it?

872
00:40:20,994 --> 00:40:23,069
If she gives it to Dong Su,
those two are siblings.

873
00:40:24,053 --> 00:40:25,540
No offense.

874
00:40:25,668 --> 00:40:27,345
- Of course.
- No offense.

875
00:40:35,464 --> 00:40:36,797
(She chooses Dong Su.)

876
00:40:36,990 --> 00:40:38,137
See?

877
00:40:40,790 --> 00:40:42,863
- No offense.
- No getting upset.

878
00:40:42,888 --> 00:40:43,690
Okay.

879
00:40:43,715 --> 00:40:44,997
(He checks the card.)

880
00:40:45,057 --> 00:40:46,150
I'm sorry.

881
00:40:46,457 --> 00:40:47,833
I'll think about it one more time.

882
00:40:47,857 --> 00:40:48,743
(He returns the card.)

883
00:40:48,803 --> 00:40:49,976
Seriously, no offense.

884
00:40:50,244 --> 00:40:52,976
"The person most likely to have had
the most rebound relationships."

885
00:40:54,790 --> 00:40:55,799
I guess he's her older brother.

886
00:40:55,823 --> 00:40:57,930
Exactly. It's such a sensitive question.

887
00:40:57,955 --> 00:41:00,557
You couldn't give that
to someone you just met.

888
00:41:00,630 --> 00:41:03,183
They basically dropped
a bomb on the siblings.

889
00:41:03,317 --> 00:41:05,877
But giving that to your own brother
is a bit weird too, isn't it?

890
00:41:05,901 --> 00:41:07,270
No, I don't mind at all.

891
00:41:09,478 --> 00:41:09,944
(Glaring)

892
00:41:09,991 --> 00:41:11,451
Seriously, no offense.

893
00:41:11,485 --> 00:41:12,331
No getting upset.

894
00:41:12,356 --> 00:41:13,444
No getting upset.

895
00:41:13,468 --> 00:41:14,731
I should stop looking at her now.

896
00:41:15,745 --> 00:41:16,911
Maybe he won't come tomorrow.

897
00:41:18,165 --> 00:41:20,431
(In Joong's turn)

898
00:41:22,391 --> 00:41:30,464
(The person most likely to struggle
with eye contact around their crush)

899
00:41:34,183 --> 00:41:35,982
(He chooses Ye In.)

900
00:41:36,116 --> 00:41:37,162
What is it?

901
00:41:41,833 --> 00:41:43,560
I can't agree with that.

902
00:41:44,340 --> 00:41:47,253
"The person most likely to struggle
with eye contact around their crush."

903
00:41:47,473 --> 00:41:49,106
I see.

904
00:41:49,237 --> 00:41:50,640
I'm actually good 1-on-1.

905
00:41:53,348 --> 00:41:54,468
Really?

906
00:41:55,422 --> 00:41:59,075
There was a moment
when I tried to show that side of myself.

907
00:41:59,189 --> 00:42:01,068
I'm just shy around new people,

908
00:42:01,095 --> 00:42:04,075
but I think I'm pretty good 1-on-1.

909
00:42:04,142 --> 00:42:06,895
That's why I said
I couldn't agree with it,

910
00:42:06,955 --> 00:42:10,022
and said, "I'm actually good 1-on-1."

911
00:42:10,189 --> 00:42:12,175
When I first saw her,

912
00:42:12,222 --> 00:42:15,348
she seemed really shy and quiet.

913
00:42:15,662 --> 00:42:17,869
But then she said she was good 1-on-1.

914
00:42:18,249 --> 00:42:19,942
That really caught my attention.

915
00:42:20,549 --> 00:42:22,848
That's when I started
feeling drawn to Ye In.

916
00:42:23,515 --> 00:42:25,087
It made me even more curious about her.

917
00:42:26,223 --> 00:42:27,521
I'm the only one with two cards.

918
00:42:32,058 --> 00:42:34,244
(A letter arrives.)

919
00:42:34,637 --> 00:42:35,357
I'm curious.

920
00:42:37,560 --> 00:42:38,973
It's here.

921
00:42:40,069 --> 00:42:41,026
I'll read it.

922
00:42:41,086 --> 00:42:42,426
(The first letter for the siblings)

923
00:42:43,153 --> 00:42:43,760
Goodness.

924
00:42:44,553 --> 00:42:45,160
What?

925
00:42:47,808 --> 00:42:50,955
"The men's first-impression picks
will now begin."

926
00:42:50,979 --> 00:42:53,703
"Take the hand of the woman you were
most attracted to at first sight,"

927
00:42:53,727 --> 00:42:55,615
"and head to the hut
for a conversation."

928
00:42:58,120 --> 00:42:59,360
Hold hands?

929
00:42:59,606 --> 00:43:00,740
Hold hands?

930
00:43:01,260 --> 00:43:03,112
Guys, what's wrong with holding hands?

931
00:43:03,193 --> 00:43:05,287
- It feels like things just leveled up.
- Exactly.

932
00:43:05,312 --> 00:43:08,519
- Holding hands is...
- Isn't this a little sudden?

933
00:43:08,560 --> 00:43:09,860
That's so exciting.

934
00:43:09,893 --> 00:43:11,313
I don't think I could do it.

935
00:43:11,366 --> 00:43:13,079
You're so innocent.

936
00:43:13,104 --> 00:43:14,826
You guys are way too innocent.

937
00:43:14,886 --> 00:43:16,626
We'll get dirty soon enough too.

938
00:43:19,120 --> 00:43:21,080
(The men will hold hands...)

939
00:43:21,707 --> 00:43:24,001
(with the woman they're interested in
and have a chat.)

940
00:43:24,025 --> 00:43:25,699
Just like that?

941
00:43:27,488 --> 00:43:28,659
I was so surprised.

942
00:43:28,700 --> 00:43:31,439
Just out in the open?

943
00:43:33,008 --> 00:43:35,414
While we're sitting
right across from each other?

944
00:43:37,953 --> 00:43:39,506
I thought it was crazy.

945
00:43:40,053 --> 00:43:42,706
They suddenly told us
to hold hands and leave...

946
00:43:42,800 --> 00:43:45,573
This early on? Right from the start?

947
00:43:45,598 --> 00:43:47,380
Hold hands and talk for 10 minutes?

948
00:43:47,433 --> 00:43:48,846
We were all caught off guard.

949
00:43:49,432 --> 00:43:50,393
Just like that?

950
00:43:50,418 --> 00:43:51,693
Really?

951
00:43:53,006 --> 00:43:54,386
Like this? Right now?

952
00:43:54,473 --> 00:43:56,471
It was...

953
00:43:58,466 --> 00:43:59,693
fun, actually.

954
00:44:01,306 --> 00:44:04,279
"The 1-on-1 conversation ends
once you let go of each other's hands."

955
00:44:04,693 --> 00:44:06,253
"Each conversation can last
up to 10 minutes."

956
00:44:06,286 --> 00:44:07,753
"Please make your move now."

957
00:44:09,353 --> 00:44:11,706
"Only one couple can
have a conversation at a time."

958
00:44:14,107 --> 00:44:16,300
"The next selection
and conversation will begin..."

959
00:44:16,341 --> 00:44:19,154
"once the previous couple returns."

960
00:44:24,373 --> 00:44:26,276
(The first-impression picks
that will take place in the hut)

961
00:44:29,443 --> 00:44:32,102
(Who will the men choose?)

962
00:44:32,249 --> 00:44:33,422
Do you want to come with me?

963
00:44:33,483 --> 00:44:36,110
It had been a long time
since I'd held a woman's hand.

964
00:44:36,903 --> 00:44:37,956
I'm getting dizzy.

965
00:44:40,095 --> 00:44:41,668
Can we get an extension?

966
00:44:42,529 --> 00:44:43,341
Hurry.

967
00:44:43,378 --> 00:44:45,846
You need to go before someone else
grabs a hand and leaves.

968
00:44:45,870 --> 00:44:47,058
Exactly. You need to move fast.

969
00:44:47,082 --> 00:44:49,615
I'm curious who's going to be
the first to get up.

970
00:44:50,205 --> 00:44:50,838
Gosh.

971
00:44:51,478 --> 00:44:53,611
Do we have to go this far?

972
00:44:53,638 --> 00:44:54,578
This is intense.

973
00:44:54,638 --> 00:44:56,492
- Things are heating up.
- From the start...

974
00:44:56,865 --> 00:44:57,685
I know.

975
00:44:58,684 --> 00:45:01,132
(Who will be the first man
to take a woman's hand and leave?)

976
00:45:01,652 --> 00:45:02,644
Is it first come, first served?

977
00:45:04,038 --> 00:45:05,458
I'll go first.

978
00:45:07,711 --> 00:45:10,044
(In Joong is the first to get up.)

979
00:45:13,320 --> 00:45:14,619
I'm so nervous right now.

980
00:45:15,253 --> 00:45:17,060
That's the hut, right?

981
00:45:17,886 --> 00:45:19,852
Yes, near the entrance.

982
00:45:19,893 --> 00:45:21,089
- Is that the hut?
- Yes.

983
00:45:21,113 --> 00:45:22,140
That's the one.

984
00:45:39,866 --> 00:45:40,759
Ye In.

985
00:45:42,659 --> 00:45:43,533
Ye In.

986
00:45:46,439 --> 00:45:47,132
We'll be back.

987
00:45:47,157 --> 00:45:47,746
(In Joong and Ye In)

988
00:45:47,780 --> 00:45:48,753
Ten minutes...

989
00:45:49,526 --> 00:45:50,552
Ten minutes, right?

990
00:45:50,726 --> 00:45:52,039
It's up to 10 minutes.

991
00:45:55,482 --> 00:45:56,335
Goodness.

992
00:45:57,392 --> 00:45:58,748
They're not holding back from the start.

993
00:46:09,042 --> 00:46:10,209
Is your hand uncomfortable?

994
00:46:10,234 --> 00:46:11,115
It's fine.

995
00:46:11,140 --> 00:46:12,062
- Is it okay?
- Yes.

996
00:46:14,236 --> 00:46:15,342
Did you see this earlier?

997
00:46:15,642 --> 00:46:17,329
Yes, I thought it was a swimming pool.

998
00:46:17,354 --> 00:46:18,756
Apparently there are doctor fish in there.

999
00:46:18,780 --> 00:46:19,580
Really?

1000
00:46:20,036 --> 00:46:21,229
No, there aren't.

1001
00:46:21,322 --> 00:46:22,722
- There's one right here.
- Really?

1002
00:46:23,362 --> 00:46:24,842
No, there isn't!

1003
00:46:29,388 --> 00:46:31,375
This is nice.
Looks different at night, doesn't it?

1004
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:32,548
Yes, it does.

1005
00:46:32,615 --> 00:46:33,768
We first met here.

1006
00:46:34,452 --> 00:46:37,481
- We were right here earlier.
- Exactly.

1007
00:46:37,868 --> 00:46:39,428
(Six hours earlier)

1008
00:46:39,534 --> 00:46:40,334
Hello.

1009
00:46:41,796 --> 00:46:42,700
Hello.

1010
00:46:44,511 --> 00:46:47,111
(The corner of the yard
where the two first met)

1011
00:46:48,148 --> 00:46:50,591
(Now they've come to the hut together,
holding hands.)

1012
00:46:50,617 --> 00:46:51,475
You go in first.

1013
00:46:51,500 --> 00:46:52,819
(The hut)

1014
00:46:52,966 --> 00:46:57,207
(What will they talk about in the hut?)

1015
00:47:00,341 --> 00:47:02,028
What do I do? Like this?

1016
00:47:11,613 --> 00:47:12,966
I think it'll be awkward.

1017
00:47:12,991 --> 00:47:15,533
- It's shy.
- The more awkward it is,

1018
00:47:15,609 --> 00:47:17,593
- the more exciting it'll be.
- Exactly.

1019
00:47:18,133 --> 00:47:18,779
Oh, my.

1020
00:47:22,534 --> 00:47:23,117
This is nice.

1021
00:47:24,294 --> 00:47:25,070
Fascinating.

1022
00:47:26,691 --> 00:47:28,655
It had been a long time
since I held a woman's hand.

1023
00:47:29,833 --> 00:47:30,710
It was so exciting.

1024
00:47:31,317 --> 00:47:33,157
I have bigger hands than most people,

1025
00:47:33,731 --> 00:47:35,564
so I was confident I could make...

1026
00:47:35,771 --> 00:47:36,957
holding hands feel good.

1027
00:47:36,991 --> 00:47:38,117
His hands were really big.

1028
00:47:38,484 --> 00:47:39,544
Really big.

1029
00:47:39,944 --> 00:47:41,830
My hands are pretty big too,

1030
00:47:42,011 --> 00:47:44,807
but his were much bigger than mine.

1031
00:47:44,832 --> 00:47:45,857
I liked that.

1032
00:47:49,002 --> 00:47:50,355
You're so confident.

1033
00:47:51,155 --> 00:47:52,803
You said you were good 1-on-1.

1034
00:47:54,389 --> 00:47:55,495
- Right.
- So I was curious.

1035
00:47:55,775 --> 00:47:57,742
I feel like I express myself...

1036
00:47:57,895 --> 00:48:00,392
- more easily 1-on-1.
- Really?

1037
00:48:01,969 --> 00:48:03,948
- You seem that way right now too.
- Do I?

1038
00:48:04,595 --> 00:48:05,969
Are you good 1-on-1?

1039
00:48:06,375 --> 00:48:09,461
I'm the same. And I prefer to take
my time getting to know someone.

1040
00:48:10,335 --> 00:48:12,222
By talking a lot?

1041
00:48:12,289 --> 00:48:13,555
Exactly.

1042
00:48:14,675 --> 00:48:17,615
When I like someone,
I have trouble looking them in the eyes.

1043
00:48:17,682 --> 00:48:19,295
I wanted to look at her,

1044
00:48:19,522 --> 00:48:21,243
but I could only
glance at her from the side.

1045
00:48:21,267 --> 00:48:22,942
I couldn't look at her directly.

1046
00:48:23,635 --> 00:48:27,875
He couldn't really look me in the eyes,

1047
00:48:28,669 --> 00:48:31,742
so I started feeling the same way.

1048
00:48:31,769 --> 00:48:34,689
I think I ended up sneaking
glances at him.

1049
00:48:36,715 --> 00:48:37,958
A while earlier,

1050
00:48:37,985 --> 00:48:39,851
you said good chemistry was
part of your ideal type, right?

1051
00:48:39,878 --> 00:48:42,257
- Right, someone I can click with.
- Someone you can talk to.

1052
00:48:42,698 --> 00:48:43,931
What's your ideal type?

1053
00:48:44,151 --> 00:48:46,704
I like girls with a puppy-like look.

1054
00:48:46,738 --> 00:48:48,571
- Puppy-like?
- Yes, I like that.

1055
00:48:49,145 --> 00:48:50,305
And I like a natural look.

1056
00:48:51,695 --> 00:48:54,098
I'm kind of into...

1057
00:48:54,382 --> 00:48:55,532
tall guys.

1058
00:48:56,426 --> 00:48:58,061
They're talking about each other.

1059
00:48:58,086 --> 00:48:59,541
That's how it goes.

1060
00:49:00,202 --> 00:49:02,408
One's ideal type is the person sitting
right in front of them.

1061
00:49:03,945 --> 00:49:06,480
I'm kind of into...

1062
00:49:06,681 --> 00:49:07,845
tall guys.

1063
00:49:08,504 --> 00:49:09,450
Really?

1064
00:49:11,063 --> 00:49:13,303
(In Joong is over 190 cm tall.)

1065
00:49:13,857 --> 00:49:16,203
I like good proportions, really.
It's more than just height.

1066
00:49:16,770 --> 00:49:17,910
How tall are you?

1067
00:49:18,070 --> 00:49:19,130
You seem really tall.

1068
00:49:19,163 --> 00:49:21,003
- I'm a little over 190 cm.
- Really?

1069
00:49:21,077 --> 00:49:21,850
Just a little over.

1070
00:49:21,890 --> 00:49:23,077
Seriously?

1071
00:49:24,321 --> 00:49:26,963
You're even taller than I thought.

1072
00:49:30,855 --> 00:49:32,902
Now that we're actually here,
I'm even more nervous.

1073
00:49:33,343 --> 00:49:35,943
I thought we'd be able to talk more easily
when it was just the two of us.

1074
00:49:44,693 --> 00:49:45,460
What?

1075
00:49:45,506 --> 00:49:47,574
They can see the whole yard
from the house.

1076
00:49:47,599 --> 00:49:48,646
Is that even allowed?

1077
00:49:48,867 --> 00:49:50,739
That means their siblings
can watch everything.

1078
00:49:50,767 --> 00:49:52,154
I wonder what that feels like.

1079
00:49:52,594 --> 00:49:54,986
How would you feel if your sibling was...

1080
00:49:55,020 --> 00:49:57,806
in the hut doing that?

1081
00:49:57,879 --> 00:50:00,066
But just like in Season One,

1082
00:50:00,091 --> 00:50:03,326
the hardest part must be
when no one chooses you.

1083
00:50:03,367 --> 00:50:04,947
- Exactly.
- Exactly.

1084
00:50:05,005 --> 00:50:06,805
Your sibling watching that is a bit weird.

1085
00:50:06,806 --> 00:50:08,340
Right, it's crushing.

1086
00:50:08,341 --> 00:50:09,808
They try to comfort you, too.

1087
00:50:09,809 --> 00:50:12,144
I think I would rather be chosen.

1088
00:50:12,145 --> 00:50:13,846
I remember them trying to help
one another.

1089
00:50:13,847 --> 00:50:14,914
Right.

1090
00:50:18,752 --> 00:50:21,887
(Deafening silence)

1091
00:50:24,459 --> 00:50:25,459
This is so awkward.

1092
00:50:26,761 --> 00:50:27,794
Everyone fell silent...

1093
00:50:28,129 --> 00:50:30,096
in just a second.

1094
00:50:30,497 --> 00:50:31,430
Ten minutes?

1095
00:50:32,966 --> 00:50:34,066
So are we staying like this?

1096
00:50:34,902 --> 00:50:36,669
We'll be waiting forever.

1097
00:50:37,071 --> 00:50:38,071
Forever.

1098
00:50:38,539 --> 00:50:41,641
Does that mean all four people get
to participate in the end?

1099
00:50:42,075 --> 00:50:45,445
No, it could be a landslide vote.

1100
00:50:45,446 --> 00:50:47,947
For example, Ye In could be picked
all four times.

1101
00:50:51,652 --> 00:50:54,320
I felt strange and slightly nervous.

1102
00:50:55,422 --> 00:50:58,524
The guys seemed like they were
weighing their options.

1103
00:50:59,860 --> 00:51:01,060
I don't know what to do.

1104
00:51:01,795 --> 00:51:02,895
I have two in mind.

1105
00:51:04,898 --> 00:51:07,800
The one I want to get to know is...

1106
00:51:14,908 --> 00:51:17,409
Can I go next?

1107
00:51:18,679 --> 00:51:20,145
- Yes.
- Sure.

1108
00:51:21,248 --> 00:51:23,816
(Dong Su volunteers to go second.)

1109
00:51:24,452 --> 00:51:26,152
Ten minutes feel like a long time.

1110
00:51:26,153 --> 00:51:27,587
That's so true.

1111
00:51:28,822 --> 00:51:30,422
It's just a second for the one choosing...

1112
00:51:30,757 --> 00:51:32,324
and forever for the one waiting.

1113
00:51:38,265 --> 00:51:40,200
- That was a good reaction.
- Really?

1114
00:51:40,201 --> 00:51:41,434
I like your reactions.

1115
00:51:42,503 --> 00:51:45,072
- So you enjoy running?
- Yes.

1116
00:51:45,073 --> 00:51:47,006
How about 5 km?
For a short and impactful workout.

1117
00:51:47,007 --> 00:51:48,241
- Right.
- Short and sweet.

1118
00:51:49,076 --> 00:51:51,211
- Let's run a 5K together next time.
- Okay.

1119
00:51:51,212 --> 00:51:52,511
They have some nice paths here.

1120
00:51:52,713 --> 00:51:54,413
Right. Wait, really?

1121
00:51:55,115 --> 00:51:56,148
- There's gravel.
- That slipped out.

1122
00:51:56,149 --> 00:51:57,316
Okay.

1123
00:51:57,317 --> 00:51:58,150
(Gravel roads for running?)

1124
00:51:58,151 --> 00:52:00,319
The trails here aren't great.

1125
00:52:00,654 --> 00:52:02,121
I'll take that back.

1126
00:52:03,924 --> 00:52:06,158
I must have been super nervous
to say that.

1127
00:52:09,029 --> 00:52:10,296
This is nice though.

1128
00:52:11,532 --> 00:52:12,699
During our time together,

1129
00:52:13,133 --> 00:52:15,367
he said "This is nice" about five times.

1130
00:52:16,169 --> 00:52:18,137
This is nice.
It looks so different at night.

1131
00:52:18,239 --> 00:52:19,705
This is nice.

1132
00:52:19,975 --> 00:52:21,040
This is nice.

1133
00:52:22,877 --> 00:52:26,078
It was both funny and endearing.

1134
00:52:27,080 --> 00:52:28,614
Having Ye In by my side...

1135
00:52:30,584 --> 00:52:31,551
made my heart flutter.

1136
00:52:35,255 --> 00:52:36,822
I left my phone.

1137
00:52:36,823 --> 00:52:39,225
(The ten-minute conversation is over.)

1138
00:52:39,660 --> 00:52:40,793
Should we go back?

1139
00:52:41,328 --> 00:52:43,929
(The hut)

1140
00:52:43,930 --> 00:52:45,264
- Mind your shoes.
- Okay.

1141
00:52:48,068 --> 00:52:50,436
- Ten minutes is over, right?
- Yes.

1142
00:52:52,039 --> 00:52:53,439
Holding hands...

1143
00:52:53,640 --> 00:52:56,875
made time go faster.

1144
00:52:57,311 --> 00:52:59,745
He was such a gentleman.

1145
00:52:59,746 --> 00:53:01,714
I was wearing heels,

1146
00:53:02,082 --> 00:53:04,616
so he gripped my hand tightly...

1147
00:53:04,617 --> 00:53:06,986
and helped me down the stairs.

1148
00:53:08,155 --> 00:53:09,222
That was nice.

1149
00:53:10,991 --> 00:53:12,959
Ten minutes might not seem long,

1150
00:53:12,960 --> 00:53:15,061
but ten minutes in a place like that...

1151
00:53:15,062 --> 00:53:16,562
just with each other is quite meaningful.

1152
00:53:17,131 --> 00:53:19,198
I feel like I opened up the possibility.

1153
00:53:19,600 --> 00:53:20,800
I'm more curious...

1154
00:53:21,468 --> 00:53:23,669
and want to talk to Ye In more.

1155
00:53:25,205 --> 00:53:26,872
You're so tall.

1156
00:53:28,742 --> 00:53:29,909
So when they walked back...

1157
00:53:30,578 --> 00:53:31,544
Yes, until the last second.

1158
00:53:32,713 --> 00:53:35,214
Somebody could fall into that pool.

1159
00:53:35,215 --> 00:53:36,282
Maybe I should try.

1160
00:53:37,751 --> 00:53:39,351
- I will save you.
- Awesome.

1161
00:53:43,924 --> 00:53:45,524
Why is it so quiet?

1162
00:53:46,860 --> 00:53:48,227
Come on, hurry.

1163
00:53:48,228 --> 00:53:49,161
Finally.

1164
00:53:49,162 --> 00:53:50,262
That took 20 minutes.

1165
00:53:50,530 --> 00:53:51,430
Twenty?

1166
00:53:51,431 --> 00:53:52,798
I thought it was ten.

1167
00:53:53,433 --> 00:53:54,533
To us, it felt like 20.

1168
00:54:01,073 --> 00:54:01,840
Is it hot?

1169
00:54:01,841 --> 00:54:02,676
- Sorry?
- Is it hot?

1170
00:54:02,677 --> 00:54:03,576
No, it's pretty cool.

1171
00:54:03,577 --> 00:54:04,953
(Checking the hut's conditions)

1172
00:54:05,012 --> 00:54:06,746
- There is a breeze.
- It's windy.

1173
00:54:07,214 --> 00:54:09,081
I'm heading out now.

1174
00:54:12,753 --> 00:54:15,654
I think Dong Su might go for Min Seo.

1175
00:54:15,655 --> 00:54:16,522
I think Jwa Hyeon.

1176
00:54:17,626 --> 00:54:19,626
(Who will take...)

1177
00:54:19,627 --> 00:54:23,296
(Dong Su's heart?)

1178
00:54:25,265 --> 00:54:26,532
Yu Ra, will you come with me?

1179
00:54:28,635 --> 00:54:29,835
That was unexpected.

1180
00:54:29,836 --> 00:54:31,570
- Totally.
- Right? You had no idea.

1181
00:54:32,739 --> 00:54:35,140
Yu Ra, will you come with me?

1182
00:54:35,575 --> 00:54:36,441
Okay.

1183
00:54:36,710 --> 00:54:39,311
(Dong Su chooses Yu Ra.)

1184
00:54:47,688 --> 00:54:49,088
You have to hold hands.

1185
00:54:50,590 --> 00:54:51,590
It's over if you let it go.

1186
00:54:51,992 --> 00:54:53,292
(Advice from a 10-minute veteran)

1187
00:55:06,640 --> 00:55:07,607
Here.

1188
00:55:12,279 --> 00:55:13,946
I chose Yu Ra.

1189
00:55:15,683 --> 00:55:18,551
Yu Ra wore a sky-blue blouse.

1190
00:55:18,552 --> 00:55:21,187
She looked so fresh,

1191
00:55:21,555 --> 00:55:23,789
which is close to my ideal type.

1192
00:55:24,491 --> 00:55:27,226
I find her cute and fresh.

1193
00:55:27,527 --> 00:55:30,296
He asked, "Yu Ra, will you come with me?"

1194
00:55:30,564 --> 00:55:32,264
I said, "Okay," and got up,

1195
00:55:32,399 --> 00:55:34,266
but I was quite nervous.

1196
00:55:34,769 --> 00:55:37,302
Doesn't Yu Ra also like Dong Su?

1197
00:55:37,303 --> 00:55:38,370
Right.

1198
00:55:38,371 --> 00:55:39,972
- That must be so nerve-wracking.
- She must be nervous.

1199
00:55:40,574 --> 00:55:44,343
This took me by surprise.

1200
00:55:44,344 --> 00:55:45,845
- You mean, today?
- This activity.

1201
00:55:45,846 --> 00:55:46,979
- Yes.
- Oh, me too.

1202
00:55:47,981 --> 00:55:49,081
We can see them.

1203
00:55:49,916 --> 00:55:51,083
You can?

1204
00:55:51,451 --> 00:55:52,618
Not much.

1205
00:55:52,619 --> 00:55:53,519
Really?

1206
00:55:53,520 --> 00:55:55,621
I can see those two very clearly though.

1207
00:55:55,923 --> 00:55:58,123
- Right.
- Last time, I couldn't see anything.

1208
00:55:59,459 --> 00:56:00,259
This way.

1209
00:56:07,400 --> 00:56:08,367
This is a bit awkward.

1210
00:56:08,635 --> 00:56:09,568
Right.

1211
00:56:16,610 --> 00:56:18,978
How is it for you so far, Dong Su?

1212
00:56:19,513 --> 00:56:20,546
It's more...

1213
00:56:21,248 --> 00:56:22,215
exciting than I thought.

1214
00:56:23,984 --> 00:56:25,818
I thought I wouldn't be able to adjust.

1215
00:56:26,186 --> 00:56:27,086
Why?

1216
00:56:27,587 --> 00:56:28,854
I've never done
something like this before.

1217
00:56:29,289 --> 00:56:30,256
Right.

1218
00:56:31,158 --> 00:56:32,858
You're also meeting new people.

1219
00:56:34,061 --> 00:56:35,294
But I think it's fun.

1220
00:56:43,135 --> 00:56:44,303
Did he just rub her?

1221
00:56:44,304 --> 00:56:46,238
This is a bit different.

1222
00:56:46,239 --> 00:56:47,139
What's up with this?

1223
00:56:47,140 --> 00:56:48,474
His thumb looks like...

1224
00:56:48,475 --> 00:56:49,775
it's acting on its own.

1225
00:56:51,546 --> 00:56:52,879
It's alive.

1226
00:56:52,880 --> 00:56:54,480
The thumb is alive.

1227
00:56:54,481 --> 00:56:57,183
I think I'm going to crash
when I get home today.

1228
00:56:58,285 --> 00:56:59,218
Why?

1229
00:56:59,219 --> 00:57:00,586
- Because you're nervous?
- Yes.

1230
00:57:00,787 --> 00:57:03,288
I feel like I'm the one doing all that.

1231
00:57:04,625 --> 00:57:07,693
He kept my hand on his leg as we talked.

1232
00:57:08,562 --> 00:57:13,131
I tend to freeze easily.

1233
00:57:13,132 --> 00:57:14,266
So I was flustered,

1234
00:57:14,501 --> 00:57:15,468
but...

1235
00:57:15,868 --> 00:57:16,969
his hand felt so warm.

1236
00:57:18,505 --> 00:57:19,371
So why did you come over?

1237
00:57:19,372 --> 00:57:22,208
The food on our table was...

1238
00:57:22,609 --> 00:57:25,578
a bit lacking.

1239
00:57:25,579 --> 00:57:26,445
I think...

1240
00:57:29,449 --> 00:57:30,649
What do you think of that, MIYEON?

1241
00:57:30,650 --> 00:57:31,717
She took his hand to her side.

1242
00:57:31,718 --> 00:57:33,519
That really caught me off guard.

1243
00:57:34,421 --> 00:57:35,854
- More than before?
- Really?

1244
00:57:35,855 --> 00:57:37,189
I feel like...

1245
00:57:37,190 --> 00:57:38,890
she's trying her best...

1246
00:57:38,891 --> 00:57:40,626
to break the awkwardness.

1247
00:57:40,627 --> 00:57:43,695
Dong Su also seems lost,
since he feels awkward.

1248
00:57:43,696 --> 00:57:44,931
He looks so nervous.

1249
00:57:44,932 --> 00:57:46,933
He might be on auto-pilot.

1250
00:57:46,934 --> 00:57:48,367
I bet his hands don't feel anything.

1251
00:57:54,107 --> 00:57:55,474
The first day... The first night...

1252
00:58:03,917 --> 00:58:06,085
Did you know that we don't share
a single letter in our MBTIs?

1253
00:58:07,187 --> 00:58:08,220
You're an INFJ?

1254
00:58:09,356 --> 00:58:10,456
No, ISFJ?

1255
00:58:13,660 --> 00:58:14,927
You sat next to me,

1256
00:58:14,928 --> 00:58:16,962
and your MBTI was
completely different from mine.

1257
00:58:17,498 --> 00:58:18,764
So that was a surprise.

1258
00:58:21,034 --> 00:58:24,770
(Yu Ra and Dong Su have
completely different MBTIs.)

1259
00:58:27,007 --> 00:58:27,974
Not a single matching letter.

1260
00:58:30,617 --> 00:58:31,777
Different MBTIs mean...

1261
00:58:32,979 --> 00:58:34,012
we have what the other doesn't.

1262
00:58:35,048 --> 00:58:36,081
Right.

1263
00:58:40,487 --> 00:58:42,220
You seem to be lost in thought.

1264
00:58:44,925 --> 00:58:47,126
But I appreciate you picking me.

1265
00:58:49,362 --> 00:58:50,228
Thank you.

1266
00:58:52,733 --> 00:58:54,433
Thank you for staying with me.

1267
00:58:56,437 --> 00:58:58,504
This feels so romantic.
Why am I getting butterflies?

1268
00:58:58,505 --> 00:59:01,006
There were a lot of romantic moments.

1269
00:59:03,610 --> 00:59:05,578
He thanked me for being with him.

1270
00:59:06,012 --> 00:59:07,279
That comment...

1271
00:59:08,181 --> 00:59:11,350
took me by surprise.

1272
00:59:12,285 --> 00:59:13,418
I used to love it when...

1273
00:59:14,120 --> 00:59:15,821
What do you call it? Skill?

1274
00:59:16,257 --> 00:59:17,923
Is our time up?

1275
00:59:19,159 --> 00:59:20,259
I didn't bring my phone.

1276
00:59:20,260 --> 00:59:22,227
(Your ten-minute conversation is over.)

1277
00:59:22,495 --> 00:59:23,428
Are we out of time?

1278
00:59:24,731 --> 00:59:25,597
Yes.

1279
00:59:25,867 --> 00:59:27,033
Can't we ask for an extension?

1280
00:59:31,906 --> 00:59:33,539
Skill?

1281
00:59:34,574 --> 00:59:36,475
- Something with thread.
- Scooby Doo?

1282
00:59:36,476 --> 00:59:37,876
No?

1283
00:59:37,877 --> 00:59:39,745
- Scooby Doo?
- It's not Scooby Doo?

1284
00:59:39,746 --> 00:59:41,346
No, it was two syllables. Maybe skull?

1285
00:59:41,581 --> 00:59:42,814
Skull?

1286
00:59:43,049 --> 00:59:44,916
- Something with an S.
- S?

1287
00:59:46,510 --> 00:59:47,319
Oh, a fish.

1288
00:59:53,626 --> 00:59:56,728
We should fill that pool
with fish sometime.

1289
01:00:02,202 --> 01:00:03,369
It's so quiet.

1290
01:00:04,176 --> 01:00:05,180
So quiet.

1291
01:00:05,714 --> 01:00:08,083
Why is everyone coming in so quietly?

1292
01:00:09,818 --> 01:00:11,253
You can make some noise when you come in.

1293
01:00:12,821 --> 01:00:14,223
It feels like we were only out
for five minutes.

1294
01:00:14,326 --> 01:00:15,390
- Five minutes?
- Barely five minutes.

1295
01:00:15,392 --> 01:00:16,158
Sorry?

1296
01:00:16,920 --> 01:00:17,860
(He jumps to his feet.)

1297
01:00:18,547 --> 01:00:20,165
(Jin Sung is quick to stand up.)

1298
01:00:20,452 --> 01:00:21,196
Min Seo.

1299
01:00:23,078 --> 01:00:25,398
(Jin Sung chooses Min Seo.)

1300
01:00:31,375 --> 01:00:33,775
I wondered if I should've gotten up
a little faster.

1301
01:00:34,376 --> 01:00:35,611
I really regret it.

1302
01:00:36,243 --> 01:00:37,246
Shall we go?

1303
01:00:37,776 --> 01:00:39,848
Just so you know,
my hands get pretty sweaty.

1304
01:00:39,929 --> 01:00:41,349
Mine do too, actually.

1305
01:00:41,350 --> 01:00:42,217
- Really?
- Yes.

1306
01:00:45,067 --> 01:00:48,047
I didn't expect we'd be doing
something like this right away.

1307
01:00:48,067 --> 01:00:50,054
I didn't think we'd be
walking out holding hands either.

1308
01:00:50,141 --> 01:00:50,993
From the start.

1309
01:00:51,274 --> 01:00:52,461
I never imagined it.

1310
01:00:52,487 --> 01:00:53,662
- Watch your step.
- Okay.

1311
01:00:56,098 --> 01:00:59,001
At least it's not as humid,

1312
01:00:59,535 --> 01:01:00,636
thankfully.

1313
01:01:02,200 --> 01:01:05,741
Min Seo stood out to me the most at first.

1314
01:01:05,953 --> 01:01:08,043
She kept responding...

1315
01:01:08,045 --> 01:01:09,538
whenever other people spoke.

1316
01:01:09,579 --> 01:01:11,413
I thought she was really thoughtful.

1317
01:01:11,433 --> 01:01:13,215
And she had this cute charm,

1318
01:01:13,531 --> 01:01:15,150
so I chose to hold her hand.

1319
01:01:15,971 --> 01:01:17,971
I had a feeling Jin Sung might choose me.

1320
01:01:17,973 --> 01:01:19,054
Because...

1321
01:01:19,131 --> 01:01:20,521
even though I was looking
in another direction,

1322
01:01:20,522 --> 01:01:23,423
you know how you can
sometimes feel someone looking at you?

1323
01:01:23,771 --> 01:01:27,763
I felt like Jin Sung kept looking at me,

1324
01:01:27,978 --> 01:01:29,331
so I was pretty sure.

1325
01:01:30,144 --> 01:01:31,366
Oh, here it is.

1326
01:01:33,548 --> 01:01:35,003
- I think this is the place.
- This is really nice!

1327
01:01:40,881 --> 01:01:42,411
It feels like...

1328
01:01:42,701 --> 01:01:43,453
I know.

1329
01:01:43,454 --> 01:01:45,013
- we only just met.
- I know.

1330
01:01:45,255 --> 01:01:46,315
What's your ideal type?

1331
01:01:46,949 --> 01:01:48,317
- Me?
- What kind of guys do you like?

1332
01:01:48,422 --> 01:01:50,686
First of all, someone who takes
good care of himself.

1333
01:01:51,820 --> 01:01:53,355
We need to have good conversations...

1334
01:01:53,515 --> 01:01:55,515
and share a similar sense of humor.

1335
01:01:56,080 --> 01:01:57,226
That's important.

1336
01:01:57,327 --> 01:01:58,760
I'm actually...

1337
01:01:59,027 --> 01:02:00,362
- pretty playful.
- Are you?

1338
01:02:01,296 --> 01:02:02,605
I'm pretty playful too.

1339
01:02:02,607 --> 01:02:03,599
- Really?
- Yes.

1340
01:02:03,999 --> 01:02:07,135
Can I ask
what your first impression of me was?

1341
01:02:07,238 --> 01:02:08,337
Your first impression?

1342
01:02:08,478 --> 01:02:09,938
You kept reacting...

1343
01:02:10,472 --> 01:02:12,874
and chiming in
whenever someone else was talking.

1344
01:02:13,005 --> 01:02:13,976
Oh, right.

1345
01:02:15,185 --> 01:02:16,338
(When everyone was sitting together)

1346
01:02:16,358 --> 01:02:17,303
Oh, I see.

1347
01:02:17,305 --> 01:02:19,278
(A quick glance)

1348
01:02:19,871 --> 01:02:20,749
Oh, my.

1349
01:02:21,251 --> 01:02:21,950
Goodness.

1350
01:02:22,658 --> 01:02:23,585
I see.

1351
01:02:23,986 --> 01:02:25,412
Gosh.

1352
01:02:26,054 --> 01:02:26,989
Oh, my.

1353
01:02:27,645 --> 01:02:28,657
I see.

1354
01:02:29,858 --> 01:02:31,323
- I'm pretty good at reacting.
- Yes, your reactions...

1355
01:02:31,325 --> 01:02:32,865
were really nice.

1356
01:02:32,985 --> 01:02:33,996
I think it's just a habit.

1357
01:02:34,712 --> 01:02:36,064
I think it's a good habit.

1358
01:02:36,765 --> 01:02:38,800
Can I ask
what your first impression of me was?

1359
01:02:39,301 --> 01:02:42,571
Well, the sunlight was really bright...

1360
01:02:42,596 --> 01:02:43,605
when you walked in.

1361
01:02:44,506 --> 01:02:46,908
And you looked so fair and radiant.

1362
01:02:49,501 --> 01:02:51,813
You kind of reminded me of milk.

1363
01:02:52,547 --> 01:02:54,683
Do you like working out?

1364
01:02:54,781 --> 01:02:56,051
I absolutely love it.

1365
01:02:56,618 --> 01:02:58,520
Would you like to try
rock climbing sometime...

1366
01:02:58,920 --> 01:03:00,205
- if we get the chance?
- I'd love to!

1367
01:03:00,207 --> 01:03:02,424
- Really?
- I feel like I'd be really good at it.

1368
01:03:02,540 --> 01:03:05,661
I think you would be too.
You've got long limbs.

1369
01:03:05,700 --> 01:03:07,700
People also tell me I have a strong grip.

1370
01:03:08,630 --> 01:03:10,065
Then you'd definitely be good at it.

1371
01:03:11,770 --> 01:03:12,768
I'll look forward to it.

1372
01:03:15,630 --> 01:03:16,905
My hands are getting sweaty.

1373
01:03:17,272 --> 01:03:18,088
Are they getting sweaty?

1374
01:03:18,090 --> 01:03:19,450
- Yes.
- Should we loosen our grip a bit?

1375
01:03:19,784 --> 01:03:21,043
Would you like to wipe your hand here?

1376
01:03:21,677 --> 01:03:22,878
No, I'm okay.

1377
01:03:22,910 --> 01:03:23,645
Are you sure?

1378
01:03:25,544 --> 01:03:27,824
(Another man with sweaty palms)

1379
01:03:33,114 --> 01:03:34,222
This is taking a long time.

1380
01:03:37,227 --> 01:03:38,660
I should've gone first.

1381
01:03:39,728 --> 01:03:42,130
It feels like I've been
waiting for an hour.

1382
01:03:42,964 --> 01:03:44,066
I'm getting dizzy.

1383
01:03:44,900 --> 01:03:47,026
Because he has to sit there
feeling nervous...

1384
01:03:47,028 --> 01:03:48,403
- for a whole hour!
- Exactly.

1385
01:03:48,670 --> 01:03:52,274
Ji Hwan seems really nervous.
He has been for a while.

1386
01:03:52,473 --> 01:03:54,473
If you wait until the end to choose,

1387
01:03:54,873 --> 01:03:57,479
there'll be a woman
who hasn't been chosen yet, right?

1388
01:03:57,967 --> 01:03:59,381
Oh, that's true.

1389
01:03:59,440 --> 01:04:02,184
If you're not interested in her,

1390
01:04:02,186 --> 01:04:04,951
you'll have to choose someone
who's already gone out with another guy.

1391
01:04:04,952 --> 01:04:06,388
So he really should've made
his choice earlier.

1392
01:04:12,394 --> 01:04:14,596
I'm having such a hard time
deciding right now.

1393
01:04:21,903 --> 01:04:23,438
When I first saw everyone,

1394
01:04:23,560 --> 01:04:25,073
two women caught my eye.

1395
01:04:25,747 --> 01:04:27,376
Ye In...

1396
01:04:28,563 --> 01:04:29,845
and Min Seo.

1397
01:04:32,047 --> 01:04:35,484
They're both so...

1398
01:04:36,151 --> 01:04:37,619
There was something...

1399
01:04:38,220 --> 01:04:39,554
I'm much better in 1-on-1 situations.

1400
01:04:44,092 --> 01:04:46,294
about Ye In's way of speaking
and her mannerisms.

1401
01:04:47,057 --> 01:04:49,898
I love going to an LP bar
and listening to music when it rains.

1402
01:04:50,392 --> 01:04:53,668
I found those qualities...

1403
01:04:53,870 --> 01:04:55,701
really charming.

1404
01:04:55,777 --> 01:04:58,974
As for Min Seo,
her looks and style were...

1405
01:04:59,021 --> 01:05:02,728
very close to my ideal type.

1406
01:05:02,761 --> 01:05:04,579
And after spending a little time together,

1407
01:05:05,048 --> 01:05:06,980
I realized
how incredibly thoughtful she was.

1408
01:05:07,668 --> 01:05:08,817
Give me half.

1409
01:05:10,781 --> 01:05:11,720
Here you go.

1410
01:05:12,327 --> 01:05:14,382
- I'll wipe it up.
- No, I'll do it.

1411
01:05:15,460 --> 01:05:16,458
Give that to me.

1412
01:05:20,480 --> 01:05:21,663
It was a really difficult decision.

1413
01:05:24,399 --> 01:05:27,602
I'm still pretty torn, to be honest.

1414
01:05:31,038 --> 01:05:32,073
Are they finished?

1415
01:05:39,014 --> 01:05:40,282
I'll head back inside.

1416
01:05:40,882 --> 01:05:42,889
(Jin Sung and Min Seo return
from the hut.)

1417
01:05:43,585 --> 01:05:45,341
We could see everything from over there!

1418
01:05:45,342 --> 01:05:46,321
- You could?
- Yes.

1419
01:05:46,469 --> 01:05:48,089
We saw everything.

1420
01:05:48,642 --> 01:05:49,624
Is everyone back now?

1421
01:06:19,044 --> 01:06:20,322
Ye In, would you come with me?

1422
01:06:20,977 --> 01:06:22,055
Oh, my.

1423
01:06:22,057 --> 01:06:23,358
Ye In!

1424
01:06:24,264 --> 01:06:27,028
So Ye In has received two votes.

1425
01:06:27,362 --> 01:06:29,030
And Jwa Hyeon hasn't been chosen yet.

1426
01:06:29,508 --> 01:06:30,765
Poor Jwa Hyeon.

1427
01:06:31,967 --> 01:06:33,335
Ye In, would you come with me?

1428
01:06:34,549 --> 01:06:38,740
(Ji Hwan chooses Ye In.)

1429
01:06:39,709 --> 01:06:41,109
I'm not very good with conversation.

1430
01:06:45,576 --> 01:06:46,715
What?

1431
01:06:47,983 --> 01:06:51,052
I never would've guessed
it would be Ji Hwan.

1432
01:06:51,920 --> 01:06:53,188
Honestly, I was jealous.

1433
01:06:53,522 --> 01:06:54,623
Someone else was going to hold...

1434
01:06:55,056 --> 01:06:56,258
the hand I'd just held.

1435
01:06:57,706 --> 01:06:59,120
He was the first to choose her,

1436
01:06:59,140 --> 01:06:59,928
Ye In.

1437
01:07:00,248 --> 01:07:02,664
and he was the guy I was most wary of.

1438
01:07:03,638 --> 01:07:05,000
So that made me...

1439
01:07:05,178 --> 01:07:08,169
even more competitive.

1440
01:07:08,470 --> 01:07:09,804
I was thrilled, of course.

1441
01:07:10,739 --> 01:07:13,356
Actually, those were the two guys...

1442
01:07:13,358 --> 01:07:15,358
I was most interested in too,

1443
01:07:15,377 --> 01:07:16,778
so I was even happier.

1444
01:07:16,976 --> 01:07:19,314
But they're completely different types.

1445
01:07:19,848 --> 01:07:22,493
Those two guys are polar opposites.

1446
01:07:22,494 --> 01:07:23,385
Exactly!

1447
01:07:23,852 --> 01:07:24,753
Which way do we go?

1448
01:07:25,554 --> 01:07:27,374
Oh, you haven't been there yet.

1449
01:07:27,722 --> 01:07:28,857
Over there.

1450
01:07:29,756 --> 01:07:30,759
- Over there?
- Yes,

1451
01:07:30,902 --> 01:07:31,793
to the left.

1452
01:07:32,656 --> 01:07:33,795
Watch your step.

1453
01:07:35,062 --> 01:07:36,542
My hand is a little cold, isn't it?

1454
01:07:37,236 --> 01:07:39,167
Not at all. Mine's cold too.

1455
01:07:43,329 --> 01:07:45,173
Why do you think...

1456
01:07:45,269 --> 01:07:48,143
I chose you?

1457
01:07:49,340 --> 01:07:51,880
I'm not sure yet.

1458
01:07:52,103 --> 01:07:54,716
But since we haven't talked much,

1459
01:07:55,800 --> 01:07:59,087
maybe you chose someone
you wanted to get to know better?

1460
01:07:59,821 --> 01:08:00,889
Why did you choose me?

1461
01:08:02,973 --> 01:08:03,858
You're right.

1462
01:08:05,454 --> 01:08:07,796
Now you've left me with nothing to say.

1463
01:08:08,111 --> 01:08:10,063
I chose you because I wanted
to talk to you more.

1464
01:08:11,800 --> 01:08:14,551
I was attracted to you from the start,

1465
01:08:14,571 --> 01:08:17,005
so I wanted to get to know you better.

1466
01:08:18,573 --> 01:08:20,875
What were your hobbies again?

1467
01:08:21,022 --> 01:08:23,022
I think we had similar interests.

1468
01:08:23,511 --> 01:08:26,414
I like cooking,

1469
01:08:27,082 --> 01:08:30,140
listening to music, and singing.

1470
01:08:30,294 --> 01:08:32,487
I love cooking...

1471
01:08:32,594 --> 01:08:35,890
and singing too, so I go to karaoke a lot.

1472
01:08:36,034 --> 01:08:38,660
We have a lot in common.

1473
01:08:40,195 --> 01:08:42,330
I love karaoke.

1474
01:08:43,345 --> 01:08:44,833
I go pretty often.

1475
01:08:45,426 --> 01:08:47,068
What's your go-to song?

1476
01:08:47,112 --> 01:08:49,804
It's "0310" by Baek Ye Rin.

1477
01:08:51,339 --> 01:08:52,273
Oh, "0310."

1478
01:08:52,345 --> 01:08:55,310
It feels like the perfect song
to listen to on a day like this.

1479
01:08:55,977 --> 01:08:59,446
Have you ever done anything else
with your singing?

1480
01:08:59,447 --> 01:09:00,515
Or do you just go to karaoke?

1481
01:09:00,735 --> 01:09:02,083
I think I entered...

1482
01:09:02,751 --> 01:09:04,486
a singing competition
when I was in school.

1483
01:09:06,521 --> 01:09:08,056
What song did you sing?

1484
01:09:08,356 --> 01:09:12,060
This is a little embarrassing.
I wasn't that good,

1485
01:09:12,360 --> 01:09:15,530
but I sang IU's "Love Wins All."

1486
01:09:17,525 --> 01:09:19,279
You must be a really good singer.

1487
01:09:19,525 --> 01:09:22,370
I just try to imitate the original.

1488
01:09:22,665 --> 01:09:24,665
Are you a good singer?

1489
01:09:25,073 --> 01:09:27,175
I wish I could at least imitate!

1490
01:09:27,272 --> 01:09:28,710
I just really love music.

1491
01:09:29,477 --> 01:09:30,845
Do you sing too?

1492
01:09:31,746 --> 01:09:33,548
I love singing too.

1493
01:09:34,852 --> 01:09:38,019
But I don't think I'm good enough
to perform in front of people.

1494
01:09:40,670 --> 01:09:42,457
Ji Hwan seems really nervous.

1495
01:09:42,970 --> 01:09:44,858
Can't you hear how nervous he is?

1496
01:09:44,859 --> 01:09:46,859
- In his voice.
- There's a slight tremble.

1497
01:09:48,744 --> 01:09:50,532
There's something I wanted to ask you.

1498
01:09:50,965 --> 01:09:52,965
Didn't you say you like cooking too?

1499
01:09:53,048 --> 01:09:55,637
Yes, I've been cooking
for myself for a long time.

1500
01:09:56,244 --> 01:09:59,307
I can take pretty good care of myself.

1501
01:10:00,675 --> 01:10:02,409
I really enjoy cooking too.

1502
01:10:02,619 --> 01:10:04,220
What can you cook?

1503
01:10:04,535 --> 01:10:07,390
I've cooked all kinds of things
over the years.

1504
01:10:07,392 --> 01:10:10,422
I'm a little embarrassed, but even before
I took the college entrance exam...

1505
01:10:10,423 --> 01:10:11,628
The college entrance exam?

1506
01:10:12,013 --> 01:10:13,106
- Well...
- The college entrance exam?

1507
01:10:13,107 --> 01:10:15,532
There was a famous cookbook
about Western cuisine,

1508
01:10:15,665 --> 01:10:17,665
and I even read that the day before.

1509
01:10:17,900 --> 01:10:20,436
I dreamed of specializing in Western food.

1510
01:10:20,776 --> 01:10:23,740
I feel like you're a really good cook.

1511
01:10:24,888 --> 01:10:27,176
Not really.

1512
01:10:27,451 --> 01:10:30,509
- I'll try to be a good assistant.
- Okay.

1513
01:10:31,222 --> 01:10:33,688
I got so caught up in the conversation...

1514
01:10:33,689 --> 01:10:35,030
and looking at her...

1515
01:10:35,031 --> 01:10:37,520
that I forgot we were holding hands.

1516
01:10:37,716 --> 01:10:39,716
With Ji Hwan,

1517
01:10:39,718 --> 01:10:44,027
the conversation felt
completely different.

1518
01:10:44,028 --> 01:10:45,320
With In Joong,

1519
01:10:45,321 --> 01:10:46,814
the conversation was fast-paced,

1520
01:10:46,815 --> 01:10:48,858
and we talked about a lot of things.

1521
01:10:48,859 --> 01:10:50,160
But with Ji Hwan,

1522
01:10:50,161 --> 01:10:52,134
he was much slower...

1523
01:10:52,135 --> 01:10:55,207
and took his time going into the details.

1524
01:10:55,208 --> 01:10:57,372
And I found myself getting absorbed
in what he was saying.

1525
01:10:57,373 --> 01:10:59,239
I thought that was charming.

1526
01:10:59,241 --> 01:11:01,144
I want to get to know him better.

1527
01:11:01,921 --> 01:11:03,713
They're really different.

1528
01:11:04,200 --> 01:11:06,282
I think her conversation with him
stuck with her more.

1529
01:11:06,560 --> 01:11:08,503
I don't know if she was more nervous
with In Joong, though.

1530
01:11:08,504 --> 01:11:11,821
Ye In said she likes it
when the conversation just flows.

1531
01:11:12,384 --> 01:11:15,702
I think her conversation
with In Joong flowed better.

1532
01:11:15,703 --> 01:11:19,014
With Ji Hwan, there were some pauses...

1533
01:11:19,015 --> 01:11:20,630
in the conversation.

1534
01:11:20,632 --> 01:11:23,280
I feel like there were more things
that resonated with her...

1535
01:11:23,281 --> 01:11:26,741
when she talked to Ji Hwan.

1536
01:11:26,742 --> 01:11:28,825
She looked more tired, though.

1537
01:11:28,826 --> 01:11:29,521
Who?

1538
01:11:29,523 --> 01:11:32,074
Ye In. Because it was her second time
out there.

1539
01:11:32,265 --> 01:11:33,793
She'd been waiting for a while.

1540
01:11:33,794 --> 01:11:37,106
- And Ji Hwan talked really slowly.
- Right.

1541
01:11:37,107 --> 01:11:40,583
She has to do a lot of preparation
before talking to him.

1542
01:11:40,804 --> 01:11:42,136
- Things to talk about?
- Yes.

1543
01:11:42,137 --> 01:11:43,986
But she doesn't need to do that
with In Joong.

1544
01:11:43,988 --> 01:11:45,688
That's when you know
the conversation really flows.

1545
01:11:45,943 --> 01:11:48,144
Is that so? When she was talking to him,

1546
01:11:48,145 --> 01:11:50,704
it seemed like she was just responding.

1547
01:11:50,705 --> 01:11:52,628
But with Ji Hwan,
they actually had a back-and-forth.

1548
01:11:55,558 --> 01:11:56,666
It's over, right?

1549
01:11:56,970 --> 01:11:58,214
It seems like time's up.

1550
01:11:58,659 --> 01:12:00,436
- It's over.
- Shall we go?

1551
01:12:00,658 --> 01:12:02,476
- Be careful.
- Thanks.

1552
01:12:03,956 --> 01:12:06,175
The wait was so long,

1553
01:12:06,799 --> 01:12:09,712
but the conversation felt like it was
less than five minutes.

1554
01:12:09,714 --> 01:12:11,147
It was a shame.

1555
01:12:12,398 --> 01:12:14,605
Are there actually doctor fish in here?

1556
01:12:14,606 --> 01:12:16,606
You can see them in there.

1557
01:12:17,340 --> 01:12:19,255
Don't you see the water ripple?

1558
01:12:20,043 --> 01:12:21,424
Aren't those raindrops?

1559
01:12:23,123 --> 01:12:25,862
Is it true? Don't mess with me.

1560
01:12:26,397 --> 01:12:27,930
Dip your feet in there tomorrow.

1561
01:12:29,332 --> 01:12:32,836
(One person has been sitting
in the same spot for 40 minutes.)

1562
01:12:34,549 --> 01:12:36,549
Ten minutes is really long.

1563
01:12:37,133 --> 01:12:38,274
I know.

1564
01:12:38,875 --> 01:12:42,479
(Nobody chose Jwa Hyeon.)

1565
01:12:45,382 --> 01:12:48,317
Time was passing so slowly.

1566
01:12:49,445 --> 01:12:51,621
I started thinking
about all sorts of things.

1567
01:12:52,022 --> 01:12:52,818
Ye In.

1568
01:12:54,715 --> 01:12:56,659
- Yu Ra, do you want to come with me?
- Yes.

1569
01:12:57,416 --> 01:12:58,940
- Min Seo.
- Yes.

1570
01:12:58,942 --> 01:13:00,259
(Jwa Hyeon never left her seat.)

1571
01:13:00,260 --> 01:13:01,764
Ye In, shall we go?

1572
01:13:03,029 --> 01:13:05,301
I realized I was totally wrong.

1573
01:13:05,601 --> 01:13:08,836
I had a feeling I might not get picked...

1574
01:13:08,861 --> 01:13:10,561
based on first impressions,

1575
01:13:10,562 --> 01:13:12,410
but I never thought...

1576
01:13:12,411 --> 01:13:14,672
it'd be all out...

1577
01:13:14,673 --> 01:13:16,111
in the open.

1578
01:13:17,179 --> 01:13:19,209
After seeing that happen,

1579
01:13:19,210 --> 01:13:20,227
I realized something.

1580
01:13:20,229 --> 01:13:23,052
That I can't stay like this.

1581
01:13:23,622 --> 01:13:25,491
I need to stay on my toes...

1582
01:13:25,492 --> 01:13:28,791
and try to show different sides of me.

1583
01:13:28,891 --> 01:13:31,160
I need to put in more effort.

1584
01:13:33,496 --> 01:13:37,066
(The hut date is over.)

1585
01:13:37,332 --> 01:13:38,668
Oh, my.

1586
01:13:38,670 --> 01:13:40,670
I feel bad for Jwa Hyeon.

1587
01:13:40,672 --> 01:13:43,231
And her sibling was watching there.

1588
01:13:43,232 --> 01:13:44,179
It's a little embarrassing.

1589
01:13:44,180 --> 01:13:46,633
I know. He was there the whole time.

1590
01:13:47,354 --> 01:13:49,712
My Sibling's Romance 2 is off
to a spicy start.

1591
01:13:51,012 --> 01:13:53,616
- Shall we start cooking?
- Should we?

1592
01:13:54,550 --> 01:13:56,819
(Ji Hwan and Ye In come back
after finishing their conversation.)

1593
01:14:00,076 --> 01:14:02,329
Being here makes you quiet.

1594
01:14:02,330 --> 01:14:03,659
Naturally.

1595
01:14:05,201 --> 01:14:07,063
How was it? Was the weather okay?

1596
01:14:07,640 --> 01:14:08,510
Isn't it raining?

1597
01:14:08,511 --> 01:14:10,318
- The rain hit me straight in my face.
- Really?

1598
01:14:10,320 --> 01:14:11,335
- Really?
- Is that so?

1599
01:14:11,337 --> 01:14:12,244
It makes your skin moist.

1600
01:14:12,246 --> 01:14:13,669
- Like a facial mist.
- Facial mist.

1601
01:14:14,060 --> 01:14:15,305
It makes your skin moist.

1602
01:14:15,495 --> 01:14:16,772
I didn't know it was raining.

1603
01:14:17,794 --> 01:14:19,876
Are you cooking?

1604
01:14:19,979 --> 01:14:22,117
- We are.
- You're making a late-night snack.

1605
01:14:22,118 --> 01:14:22,912
Awesome.

1606
01:14:23,579 --> 01:14:25,967
(Today's late-night snack: pork bulgogi)

1607
01:14:25,968 --> 01:14:28,450
- Yu Ra, add the sauce now.
- Now?

1608
01:14:29,444 --> 01:14:30,853
It smells great.

1609
01:14:31,515 --> 01:14:32,516
That's good.

1610
01:14:32,517 --> 01:14:33,499
Shall we just add one for now?

1611
01:14:33,501 --> 01:14:35,396
Let's add one and grill this.

1612
01:14:35,397 --> 01:14:37,193
- You're a genius!
- All right.

1613
01:14:37,673 --> 01:14:38,694
Thirty seconds.

1614
01:14:39,144 --> 01:14:40,563
The sauce?

1615
01:14:40,565 --> 01:14:41,560
Okay.

1616
01:14:41,561 --> 01:14:43,599
What if we keep playing this game
until the last day?

1617
01:14:44,564 --> 01:14:46,235
Because we don't understand
the other games.

1618
01:14:47,440 --> 01:14:48,637
Look at that.

1619
01:14:49,084 --> 01:14:51,240
You made a Korean pancake.

1620
01:14:51,387 --> 01:14:52,581
It does look like a Korean pancake.

1621
01:14:52,583 --> 01:14:54,944
Is that a spicy pork pancake?
A pork bulgogi pancake?

1622
01:14:57,530 --> 01:14:59,530
If you look at this, there's no way...

1623
01:14:59,815 --> 01:15:00,850
this doesn't taste good.

1624
01:15:01,800 --> 01:15:04,187
Are you sure? It looks suspicious to me.

1625
01:15:05,819 --> 01:15:09,040
They were making a bulgogi meal,

1626
01:15:09,041 --> 01:15:11,227
and they really seemed to hit it off.

1627
01:15:11,553 --> 01:15:12,854
Because they're siblings.

1628
01:15:12,855 --> 01:15:13,829
These two?

1629
01:15:16,354 --> 01:15:18,468
It smells a little weird.

1630
01:15:19,083 --> 01:15:21,304
- Am I wrong?
- Not at all.

1631
01:15:21,909 --> 01:15:23,611
Let's say my nose is wrong.

1632
01:15:23,612 --> 01:15:25,193
They bounced off each other
so naturally...

1633
01:15:25,194 --> 01:15:28,149
for two people who had just met.

1634
01:15:28,150 --> 01:15:30,545
Also, they look alike.

1635
01:15:30,546 --> 01:15:32,915
They have the same eyes.

1636
01:15:34,200 --> 01:15:35,985
- Yes. They look alike.
- They do.

1637
01:15:36,560 --> 01:15:39,288
I'm pretty sure they're siblings.

1638
01:15:39,488 --> 01:15:40,800
(Who do you think are brother and sister?)

1639
01:15:40,801 --> 01:15:42,492
Yu Ra and In Joong.

1640
01:15:42,658 --> 01:15:45,520
Yu Ra and In Joong...

1641
01:15:45,521 --> 01:15:47,530
naturally seemed like siblings.

1642
01:15:48,164 --> 01:15:50,833
(They have no idea
everyone is getting suspicious of them.)

1643
01:15:52,096 --> 01:15:54,096
That looks better now.

1644
01:15:55,011 --> 01:15:56,425
It looked a little suspicious earlier.

1645
01:15:56,426 --> 01:15:57,940
I don't agree.

1646
01:15:58,022 --> 01:15:58,975
Really?

1647
01:15:59,191 --> 01:16:03,012
"The person who'd get back together
the minute they broke up."

1648
01:16:03,267 --> 01:16:04,630
Getting back together?

1649
01:16:04,631 --> 01:16:06,849
I've never gotten back together
with an ex.

1650
01:16:10,052 --> 01:16:12,288
(Ji Hwan's turn)

1651
01:16:12,822 --> 01:16:16,859
(The person who can't look
someone they like in the eye)

1652
01:16:23,132 --> 01:16:25,568
(He chooses Min Seo.)

1653
01:16:28,540 --> 01:16:29,539
It's correct.

1654
01:16:30,867 --> 01:16:32,684
"The person who can't look
someone they like in the eye."

1655
01:16:32,685 --> 01:16:33,768
I can't make eye contact with them.

1656
01:16:33,769 --> 01:16:35,144
- Really?
- Yes.

1657
01:16:35,566 --> 01:16:39,001
If you can make eye contact with them,
does that mean you're not into them?

1658
01:16:39,002 --> 01:16:40,416
That's not necessarily true either.

1659
01:16:40,544 --> 01:16:44,797
It only happens
when I'm super into someone.

1660
01:16:45,593 --> 01:16:47,890
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you for the food.

1661
01:16:48,423 --> 01:16:49,491
Enjoy.

1662
01:16:49,493 --> 01:16:50,559
Shall we toast?

1663
01:16:56,884 --> 01:16:58,617
I feel like we're wrapping up the day...

1664
01:16:58,618 --> 01:17:00,732
- with a drink.
- I know.

1665
01:17:00,734 --> 01:17:02,232
- Like we're winding down.
- Right?

1666
01:17:02,494 --> 01:17:04,494
I haven't had a good drink in a while.

1667
01:17:12,481 --> 01:17:14,817
(A letter has arrived.)

1668
01:17:16,199 --> 01:17:17,252
Is there something in there?

1669
01:17:17,253 --> 01:17:19,055
(The second letter came in right after.)

1670
01:17:19,244 --> 01:17:20,524
I'm so nervous.

1671
01:17:20,653 --> 01:17:22,525
- I'll open it.
- Okay.

1672
01:17:22,893 --> 01:17:23,977
What?

1673
01:17:23,978 --> 01:17:27,730
"The women will now make
their first-impression picks."

1674
01:17:27,732 --> 01:17:28,904
What? Right away?

1675
01:17:28,905 --> 01:17:30,666
Right after eating?

1676
01:17:30,870 --> 01:17:32,068
I hope none of them match!

1677
01:17:32,635 --> 01:17:36,393
"The women will now make
their first-impression picks."

1678
01:17:36,394 --> 01:17:39,629
"The women will each receive
a first-impression date ticket."

1679
01:17:39,630 --> 01:17:42,085
"They can use it to go on a date..."

1680
01:17:42,086 --> 01:17:45,616
"with their first-impression pick
at any time during the stay."

1681
01:17:45,618 --> 01:17:48,897
"Write a message you'd like to send..."

1682
01:17:48,898 --> 01:17:50,920
"on the enclosed card..."

1683
01:17:51,253 --> 01:17:53,989
"and personally deliver it to that person
by 11:11 p.m."

1684
01:17:54,718 --> 01:17:55,984
"At any time."

1685
01:17:56,961 --> 01:17:59,342
Does that mean
we can use that ticket later?

1686
01:17:59,344 --> 01:18:00,596
I think so.

1687
01:18:01,157 --> 01:18:02,631
This is really important.

1688
01:18:02,926 --> 01:18:04,800
They can keep it until later.

1689
01:18:05,260 --> 01:18:07,536
- That's huge.
- That's a big deal.

1690
01:18:08,029 --> 01:18:10,239
I can't wait to see who Ye In will choose.

1691
01:18:10,650 --> 01:18:12,441
We don't have much time.

1692
01:18:12,748 --> 01:18:14,200
Why don't you go upstairs to write?

1693
01:18:14,224 --> 01:18:15,745
- It'll be more comfortable.
- Shall we?

1694
01:18:15,897 --> 01:18:18,046
"Personally deliver it to that person."

1695
01:18:18,911 --> 01:18:20,883
- All of a sudden?
- Oh, dear.

1696
01:18:21,846 --> 01:18:23,028
I'll sit here.

1697
01:18:23,030 --> 01:18:25,888
(They all sit down with their cards.)

1698
01:18:25,890 --> 01:18:29,164
We have to deliver it by 11:11 p.m.

1699
01:18:29,165 --> 01:18:30,492
Yes, within today.

1700
01:18:31,511 --> 01:18:33,830
If it's by 11:11 p.m.,
we have to write our cards...

1701
01:18:33,831 --> 01:18:35,627
and deliver them right away.

1702
01:18:37,199 --> 01:18:39,268
(Deep in thought)

1703
01:18:43,806 --> 01:18:46,842
(Jwa Hyeon is the first one
to start writing her card.)

1704
01:18:48,177 --> 01:18:50,679
(Yu Ra gets started right after.)

1705
01:18:54,149 --> 01:18:56,063
(Meanwhile, it's quiet downstairs.)

1706
01:18:56,064 --> 01:18:57,420
It's suddenly quiet.

1707
01:18:59,049 --> 01:18:59,989
Gosh.

1708
01:19:00,462 --> 01:19:02,357
This is going to be
a long 20 minutes for us.

1709
01:19:02,959 --> 01:19:04,427
They make us do a lot of things
on the first day.

1710
01:19:05,243 --> 01:19:06,361
This is fun.

1711
01:19:08,068 --> 01:19:08,819
Right.

1712
01:19:08,820 --> 01:19:10,833
(Just staring at the clock)

1713
01:19:13,769 --> 01:19:15,638
(Current time: 10:52 p.m.)

1714
01:19:15,779 --> 01:19:17,105
I'll go downstairs.

1715
01:19:17,563 --> 01:19:18,877
Are you already done?

1716
01:19:18,878 --> 01:19:21,677
I didn't write much. I kept it short.

1717
01:19:22,111 --> 01:19:24,413
(Yu Ra finishes shortly after.)

1718
01:19:24,528 --> 01:19:26,415
I'll get going too.

1719
01:19:27,165 --> 01:19:28,618
Bye.

1720
01:19:30,853 --> 01:19:33,823
(The two are still thinking.)

1721
01:19:34,223 --> 01:19:36,158
(Jwa Hyeon and Yu Ra go downstairs.)

1722
01:19:36,607 --> 01:19:38,607
Let me read it again.

1723
01:19:45,167 --> 01:19:46,969
(Sliding)

1724
01:19:48,203 --> 01:19:53,408
(The women's first-impression picks:
Yu Ra chooses Ji Hwan.)

1725
01:19:55,366 --> 01:19:56,812
Really?

1726
01:19:56,997 --> 01:19:58,997
- Ji Hwan? Right in front of Dong Su?
- I thought she liked the date.

1727
01:19:59,612 --> 01:20:02,659
- That's kind of brutal, though.
- I know. Dong Su is right there.

1728
01:20:02,684 --> 01:20:03,940
What are you talking about?

1729
01:20:03,973 --> 01:20:05,066
This is so much fun!

1730
01:20:05,160 --> 01:20:06,766
They may not pick each other.

1731
01:20:06,820 --> 01:20:08,113
It's just a first-impression pick.

1732
01:20:09,789 --> 01:20:12,776
(Yu Ra chose Ji Hwan.)

1733
01:20:19,533 --> 01:20:21,333
When Ji Hwan first walked in,

1734
01:20:21,420 --> 01:20:22,907
he was so tall and handsome.

1735
01:20:23,000 --> 01:20:29,373
He looked just like my type.

1736
01:20:29,560 --> 01:20:32,294
When the guys led their picks out
by the hand,

1737
01:20:32,318 --> 01:20:33,896
Ji Hwan was standing right in front of me,

1738
01:20:34,300 --> 01:20:36,653
so I tried to strike up a conversation.

1739
01:20:37,027 --> 01:20:40,219
He barely even glanced my way, though,

1740
01:20:40,913 --> 01:20:44,546
so I figured I should at least
get a chance to talk to him.

1741
01:20:45,165 --> 01:20:49,024
(Women's first-impression picks:
Yu Ra chose Ji Hwan.)

1742
01:20:49,411 --> 01:20:50,664
We're on a time limit.

1743
01:20:52,448 --> 01:20:53,949
I wish we had a little more time.

1744
01:20:55,592 --> 01:20:57,485
- Shall we make a toast?
- This calls for a drink.

1745
01:20:57,858 --> 01:20:59,025
Dong Su, do you have a drink?

1746
01:20:59,050 --> 01:21:01,090
I don't. I'll take a beer, please.

1747
01:21:02,138 --> 01:21:03,238
Got it, one beer.

1748
01:21:04,185 --> 01:21:07,125
After writing the note,
I started having second thoughts.

1749
01:21:07,612 --> 01:21:10,144
Dong Su had picked me,

1750
01:21:10,185 --> 01:21:12,178
so I felt a little bad.

1751
01:21:12,632 --> 01:21:16,038
I hesitated for a while
with the note in my hand.

1752
01:21:16,244 --> 01:21:21,324
Still, Ji Hwan was the one I wanted
to get to know based on first impressions.

1753
01:21:22,729 --> 01:21:27,362
(Meanwhile, Ye In and Min Seo
still haven't written theirs)

1754
01:21:31,121 --> 01:21:34,080
(Min Seo finishes first.)

1755
01:21:34,241 --> 01:21:36,094
- Do you have some in your glass?
- Yeah.

1756
01:21:41,117 --> 01:21:42,830
(Handing over the note)

1757
01:21:44,191 --> 01:21:48,487
(Women's first-impression picks:
Jwa Hyeon chose In Joong.)

1758
01:21:48,815 --> 01:21:52,301
It didn't take me long to decide.

1759
01:21:53,121 --> 01:21:56,341
I thought In Joong seemed cool...

1760
01:21:56,728 --> 01:22:00,114
because he broke the ice
and kept the mood light.

1761
01:22:00,141 --> 01:22:03,721
That made me want to talk to him.

1762
01:22:03,808 --> 01:22:06,028
He mentioned he can't eat spicy food,

1763
01:22:06,053 --> 01:22:09,454
so I wrote, "No spicy food.
Let's go grab something good to eat."

1764
01:22:10,121 --> 01:22:11,247
That's thoughtful.

1765
01:22:11,272 --> 01:22:12,455
- She's cute.
- She really is.

1766
01:22:12,480 --> 01:22:14,374
"No spicy food.
Let's go grab something good to eat."

1767
01:22:15,026 --> 01:22:16,920
(Ye In finally finishes her note.)

1768
01:22:17,715 --> 01:22:21,181
(She keeps hesitating
even after sealing the envelope.)

1769
01:22:26,108 --> 01:22:29,141
(After much deliberation,
she heads downstairs.)

1770
01:22:35,554 --> 01:22:37,001
What were you guys drinking?

1771
01:22:37,239 --> 01:22:38,740
These are both really good.

1772
01:22:38,794 --> 01:22:41,288
- Really?
- Yeah, thanks.

1773
01:22:41,374 --> 01:22:42,681
Funny how it's just the four of us here.

1774
01:22:42,721 --> 01:22:43,659
Right?

1775
01:22:44,500 --> 01:22:47,029
I need to give you this.

1776
01:22:48,981 --> 01:22:51,333
I need to give you this.

1777
01:22:54,785 --> 01:22:59,864
(Women's first-impression picks:
Min Seo chose Ji Hwan.)

1778
01:23:00,218 --> 01:23:01,478
Oh, wow!

1779
01:23:01,711 --> 01:23:04,685
- Why is Ji Hwan so popular?
- At least those two aren't siblings.

1780
01:23:04,798 --> 01:23:06,837
Nobody's matching up.

1781
01:23:06,862 --> 01:23:07,737
Oh, no.

1782
01:23:12,006 --> 01:23:14,273
I wanted to give my note to Ji Hwan,

1783
01:23:14,513 --> 01:23:17,992
but he had walked out
holding Ye In's hand,

1784
01:23:18,017 --> 01:23:21,232
so my pride was a little hurt.

1785
01:23:23,870 --> 01:23:26,717
Sitting right across from the two guys
who'd picked Ye In...

1786
01:23:27,963 --> 01:23:30,309
really stung,

1787
01:23:30,461 --> 01:23:32,407
but I kept waiting for the right moment...

1788
01:23:32,950 --> 01:23:34,950
so I wouldn't have any regrets.

1789
01:23:36,252 --> 01:23:39,349
Eventually, I just thought, "Whatever,"
and handed it to him.

1790
01:23:39,410 --> 01:23:43,556
I knew I'd regret it later
if I didn't go for Ji Hwan,

1791
01:23:43,877 --> 01:23:45,809
so I gave it to him.

1792
01:23:45,834 --> 01:23:48,296
(Women's first-impression picks:
Yu Ra chose Ji Hwan.)

1793
01:23:51,156 --> 01:23:53,496
(One minute left to hand out
the first-impression notes.)

1794
01:23:53,790 --> 01:23:54,603
Are you tired?

1795
01:23:55,362 --> 01:23:58,589
(Ye In is the only one
who hasn't given hers out yet.)

1796
01:24:00,343 --> 01:24:03,616
(Fidgeting)

1797
01:24:03,849 --> 01:24:06,342
- This is a big moment.
- This is huge.

1798
01:24:06,367 --> 01:24:08,148
I think she'll pick Ji Hwan.

1799
01:24:08,882 --> 01:24:09,589
I think so too.

1800
01:24:09,622 --> 01:24:11,102
I bet she gives it to In Joong.

1801
01:24:11,202 --> 01:24:12,209
I think she'll go with In Joong too.

1802
01:24:12,282 --> 01:24:13,228
- Really?
- Yeah, me too.

1803
01:24:13,489 --> 01:24:16,135
We might all go for a jog
tomorrow morning.

1804
01:24:16,175 --> 01:24:19,655
It took me forever to write mine too.

1805
01:24:19,914 --> 01:24:25,962
I knew it was
between In Joong and Ji Hwan,

1806
01:24:26,035 --> 01:24:27,342
but I hadn't made up my mind.

1807
01:24:27,373 --> 01:24:29,208
So I just wrote,
"Let's grab something good to eat."

1808
01:24:31,182 --> 01:24:35,021
That way, she could change her mind
at the last second.

1809
01:24:35,142 --> 01:24:36,462
Smart move.

1810
01:24:36,582 --> 01:24:40,135
- Even she wasn't sure how she felt.
- So she left the name off.

1811
01:24:40,160 --> 01:24:46,301
And that let her play it strategically
after seeing who the other girls picked.

1812
01:24:46,362 --> 01:24:47,475
Ye In is sharp.

1813
01:24:47,888 --> 01:24:48,784
She's clever.

1814
01:24:49,682 --> 01:24:52,448
We might all go for a jog
tomorrow morning.

1815
01:24:55,593 --> 01:24:57,299
(Fidgeting)

1816
01:24:57,673 --> 01:24:59,399
- I think she'll pick Ji Hwan.
- Ji Hwan.

1817
01:24:59,553 --> 01:25:01,219
In Joong!

1818
01:25:04,816 --> 01:25:06,768
They just called the one-minute warning.

1819
01:25:09,602 --> 01:25:15,229
(Women's first-impression picks:
Ye In chose In Joong.)

1820
01:25:16,071 --> 01:25:17,326
Even after writing the note,

1821
01:25:17,358 --> 01:25:19,176
I still couldn't decide who to give it to.

1822
01:25:19,322 --> 01:25:21,709
Then I heard there was
only one minute left.

1823
01:25:21,734 --> 01:25:26,469
In Joong struck me as someone
who takes the initiative,

1824
01:25:26,509 --> 01:25:28,109
so I gave it to him.

1825
01:25:28,928 --> 01:25:29,741
I was thrilled.

1826
01:25:30,241 --> 01:25:32,467
I didn't see that coming from Ye In.

1827
01:25:32,501 --> 01:25:34,015
I was sure she'd give it to Ji Hwan.

1828
01:25:34,533 --> 01:25:36,326
I wasn't expecting her to pick me at all,

1829
01:25:36,351 --> 01:25:37,966
so when she suddenly handed me the note,

1830
01:25:38,735 --> 01:25:42,240
at first I wondered if she'd given it
to the wrong person.

1831
01:25:42,440 --> 01:25:46,034
Ye In is the one I have my eye on.

1832
01:25:46,319 --> 01:25:49,346
I was hoping the note
from the person I'd been watching...

1833
01:25:49,979 --> 01:25:52,086
would come to me,

1834
01:25:52,126 --> 01:25:57,299
so seeing her hand it to In Joong
right in front of me...

1835
01:25:57,592 --> 01:25:59,152
really made my heart sink.

1836
01:26:04,906 --> 01:26:07,853
(I'd love to talk more.
Let's go grab something good to eat.)

1837
01:26:08,074 --> 01:26:09,554
This makes things interesting.

1838
01:26:09,594 --> 01:26:11,474
To be fair, if I were Ye In,

1839
01:26:11,498 --> 01:26:13,233
I wouldn't give my note
to Ji Hwan either...

1840
01:26:13,258 --> 01:26:15,224
after two other women had
already given him theirs.

1841
01:26:15,249 --> 01:26:19,060
She hasn't really settled on anyone yet.

1842
01:26:19,085 --> 01:26:23,712
And nobody wants to be one of three.

1843
01:26:24,583 --> 01:26:28,696
Ji Hwan mentioned earlier
that he's competitive.

1844
01:26:28,721 --> 01:26:30,863
Maybe Ye In was trying to trigger
his competitive streak.

1845
01:26:30,888 --> 01:26:31,664
Exactly.

1846
01:26:32,302 --> 01:26:33,777
- Shall we clean up?
- Sure.

1847
01:26:33,884 --> 01:26:34,577
Sounds good.

1848
01:26:34,637 --> 01:26:35,743
(All the women have made their picks.)

1849
01:26:36,024 --> 01:26:38,097
(The men's room on the third floor)

1850
01:26:38,684 --> 01:26:41,657
(Silence hangs between the two men.)

1851
01:26:45,188 --> 01:26:46,968
I'm feeling a little down.

1852
01:26:47,435 --> 01:26:48,495
What happened?

1853
01:26:49,414 --> 01:26:50,672
Did you get a note?

1854
01:26:51,068 --> 01:26:52,654
- What about you?
- I didn't get one.

1855
01:26:52,679 --> 01:26:53,614
Me neither.

1856
01:26:53,914 --> 01:26:54,934
(Laughing)

1857
01:26:55,275 --> 01:26:56,361
(Laughing)

1858
01:26:57,095 --> 01:26:58,661
I was bummed I didn't get a note.

1859
01:26:58,808 --> 01:27:01,048
Dong Su said he didn't get one either.

1860
01:27:01,175 --> 01:27:03,627
I realized I needed to step up my game.

1861
01:27:04,564 --> 01:27:06,744
Yu Ra.

1862
01:27:08,270 --> 01:27:10,850
She gave hers to Ji Hwan.

1863
01:27:12,277 --> 01:27:14,550
I thought I'd be fine with it.

1864
01:27:14,603 --> 01:27:17,236
But watching it happen
right in front of me...

1865
01:27:19,166 --> 01:27:21,606
really hit me hard.

1866
01:27:23,552 --> 01:27:26,612
(Speechless)

1867
01:27:27,092 --> 01:27:28,619
It threw me off.

1868
01:27:29,319 --> 01:27:30,832
I thought I was pretty tough mentally,

1869
01:27:31,472 --> 01:27:32,539
but that shook me.

1870
01:27:33,746 --> 01:27:35,250
I knew it the second she handed it over.

1871
01:27:35,706 --> 01:27:37,572
Seeing her give it to Ji Hwan...

1872
01:27:38,052 --> 01:27:39,519
Of course, I knew it was possible,

1873
01:27:39,606 --> 01:27:41,857
but watching it unfold
right in front of me...

1874
01:27:42,466 --> 01:27:44,292
brought on a feeling
I'd never felt before.

1875
01:27:45,825 --> 01:27:47,524
It stung.

1876
01:27:48,698 --> 01:27:49,898
It should've been me.

1877
01:27:51,452 --> 01:27:52,538
Min Seo?

1878
01:27:54,119 --> 01:27:56,018
I don't know who she gave hers to.

1879
01:27:56,052 --> 01:27:56,944
You don't?

1880
01:27:58,117 --> 01:27:59,323
It's only first impressions.

1881
01:27:59,350 --> 01:28:01,170
True. It's just the beginning.

1882
01:28:01,871 --> 01:28:03,231
Anything can happen.

1883
01:28:07,251 --> 01:28:11,297
What do you like about Min Seo?

1884
01:28:12,317 --> 01:28:14,230
She has a cute side to her.

1885
01:28:14,255 --> 01:28:15,404
Oh, Min Seo?

1886
01:28:16,644 --> 01:28:18,490
She's also a great listener.

1887
01:28:18,517 --> 01:28:19,577
I see.

1888
01:28:20,397 --> 01:28:21,957
She seems really kind-hearted.

1889
01:28:22,091 --> 01:28:23,717
Sweet-natured?

1890
01:28:24,571 --> 01:28:25,801
Yeah, she gives off that vibe.

1891
01:28:27,886 --> 01:28:31,380
When I first walked in,

1892
01:28:32,450 --> 01:28:36,263
everyone was so tall,

1893
01:28:36,311 --> 01:28:37,385
handsome,

1894
01:28:38,131 --> 01:28:39,505
Everyone is good-looking.

1895
01:28:39,545 --> 01:28:40,751
and in great shape.

1896
01:28:41,884 --> 01:28:43,057
You're right up there too.

1897
01:28:43,105 --> 01:28:44,191
Look at your build.

1898
01:28:45,113 --> 01:28:46,426
You're way more built than I am.

1899
01:28:46,971 --> 01:28:50,137
(The two guys who got zero notes
try to cheer each other up.)

1900
01:28:51,744 --> 01:28:53,070
Want to play gonggi?

1901
01:28:53,104 --> 01:28:54,198
Gonggi?

1902
01:28:54,724 --> 01:28:56,624
(The game of gonggi begins.)

1903
01:28:58,900 --> 01:28:59,901
You're really good at this.

1904
01:29:01,705 --> 01:29:02,437
See?

1905
01:29:03,196 --> 01:29:06,090
(The doorbell rings.)

1906
01:29:07,177 --> 01:29:08,344
At this hour?

1907
01:29:08,411 --> 01:29:10,698
Something's outside.

1908
01:29:12,544 --> 01:29:13,710
- Is there anything inside?
- Yeah, there is.

1909
01:29:13,751 --> 01:29:15,218
Could it be about tomorrow?

1910
01:29:15,891 --> 01:29:17,878
Like, what time do we have to wake up?

1911
01:29:20,671 --> 01:29:25,544
"The Love Hideout is now open."

1912
01:29:29,713 --> 01:29:31,419
- The Love Hideout!
- The Love Hideout!

1913
01:29:31,466 --> 01:29:32,520
Right now?

1914
01:29:32,546 --> 01:29:34,219
Could it be like that hideout
in the basement last season?

1915
01:29:34,253 --> 01:29:35,320
The piano room.

1916
01:29:35,360 --> 01:29:36,920
"The Love Hideout?"

1917
01:29:37,386 --> 01:29:38,840
"At the Love Hideout,"

1918
01:29:38,864 --> 01:29:43,278
"you can spend the night alone
with whoever you choose."

1919
01:29:44,145 --> 01:29:45,954
(Spend the night alone)

1920
01:29:46,258 --> 01:29:49,025
The second I heard "alone,"
my mind went blank.

1921
01:29:49,431 --> 01:29:50,824
Already?

1922
01:29:50,932 --> 01:29:53,119
That would be so awkward.

1923
01:29:53,238 --> 01:29:55,111
What? No way.

1924
01:29:55,165 --> 01:29:56,732
It's only day one,

1925
01:29:56,757 --> 01:29:59,585
and things were already heating up.

1926
01:29:59,794 --> 01:30:01,862
"Head out to the yard right now..."

1927
01:30:01,863 --> 01:30:03,964
"and ring the Love Hideout's doorbell."

1928
01:30:04,299 --> 01:30:07,901
"Only the fastest person gets the chance."

1929
01:30:08,336 --> 01:30:09,669
The fastest person?

1930
01:30:09,670 --> 01:30:10,504
Just one?

1931
01:30:10,505 --> 01:30:11,539
First come, first served.

1932
01:30:11,540 --> 01:30:13,640
This could get physical.

1933
01:30:13,875 --> 01:30:16,577
- Wait, what?
- What is that?

1934
01:30:16,978 --> 01:30:18,845
(Everyone is thrown.)

1935
01:30:18,846 --> 01:30:21,215
Go out to the yard and ring the doorbell?

1936
01:30:21,216 --> 01:30:23,483
Where's the Love Hideout, though?

1937
01:30:23,484 --> 01:30:24,484
I'm heading out.

1938
01:30:24,485 --> 01:30:25,919
Someone tell us where it is.

1939
01:30:29,958 --> 01:30:30,958
He's fast.

1940
01:30:30,959 --> 01:30:31,992
Love Hideout?

1941
01:30:33,161 --> 01:30:34,728
(In Joong, first out to the garden)

1942
01:30:34,729 --> 01:30:35,662
I just took off running.

1943
01:30:35,663 --> 01:30:38,098
I made it out first,
and everyone else followed.

1944
01:30:38,167 --> 01:30:39,768
And they're all kind of slow.

1945
01:30:40,502 --> 01:30:42,336
I was like, "I have to get this."

1946
01:30:42,337 --> 01:30:43,737
I'm super competitive.

1947
01:30:43,872 --> 01:30:46,040
And since it meant alone time with Ye In,

1948
01:30:46,107 --> 01:30:47,474
it had to be mine.

1949
01:30:52,747 --> 01:30:55,282
(The Love Hideout is open.)

1950
01:30:57,152 --> 01:30:58,953
Oh, that must be it.

1951
01:30:59,087 --> 01:31:00,387
There's a separate cottage.

1952
01:31:00,823 --> 01:31:01,923
That's kind of dangerous.

1953
01:31:08,563 --> 01:31:10,330
(Love Hideout)

1954
01:31:12,334 --> 01:31:15,569
(The Love Hideout is
at the end of the garden.)

1955
01:31:17,706 --> 01:31:21,075
(They have to cross the whole garden.)

1956
01:31:24,879 --> 01:31:27,280
(Who will ring
the Love Hideout's doorbell?)

1957
01:31:32,754 --> 01:31:35,689
Only the first one there gets in?

1958
01:31:35,890 --> 01:31:38,791
In Joong bolted out first.

1959
01:31:38,792 --> 01:31:41,328
So I chased after him,
and it was so much fun.

1960
01:31:41,329 --> 01:31:42,729
I don't think this is it.

1961
01:31:43,732 --> 01:31:44,865
He hasn't found it yet.

1962
01:31:45,133 --> 01:31:46,100
He still hasn't found it?

1963
01:31:46,101 --> 01:31:47,068
(Everyone joins the open run.)

1964
01:31:47,069 --> 01:31:48,268
Guess not.

1965
01:31:48,737 --> 01:31:49,436
Still nothing?

1966
01:31:49,437 --> 01:31:50,604
Nope, it's not over there.

1967
01:31:50,605 --> 01:31:52,038
- The Love Hideout?
- Did you find it?

1968
01:31:52,039 --> 01:31:52,940
Nope.

1969
01:31:52,941 --> 01:31:55,543
They said there's a doorbell.

1970
01:31:55,544 --> 01:31:58,179
So whoever finds it first gets in.

1971
01:31:58,513 --> 01:31:59,847
Maybe it's inside?

1972
01:31:59,848 --> 01:32:01,615
(Ye In heads inside.)

1973
01:32:02,017 --> 01:32:03,283
I don't think it's in here.

1974
01:32:04,687 --> 01:32:05,753
I thought it might be inside.

1975
01:32:05,954 --> 01:32:07,922
So I searched every inch of the house.

1976
01:32:08,456 --> 01:32:09,990
I don't think it's here.

1977
01:32:10,358 --> 01:32:13,527
I'm dying to know
where the Love Hideout is.

1978
01:32:13,528 --> 01:32:16,530
(The invite is out,
but no one is showing up.)

1979
01:32:16,531 --> 01:32:19,333
I checked the grounds and the pool.

1980
01:32:19,334 --> 01:32:20,667
Even the backyard.

1981
01:32:20,668 --> 01:32:22,936
(Checking every corner)

1982
01:32:22,937 --> 01:32:25,105
They said there's a doorbell
for whoever gets there first.

1983
01:32:25,106 --> 01:32:26,974
So I started pressing lamps and lights.

1984
01:32:26,975 --> 01:32:27,975
Just in case one rang.

1985
01:32:27,976 --> 01:32:28,976
Is it this?

1986
01:32:30,812 --> 01:32:32,346
I literally looked everywhere.

1987
01:32:32,948 --> 01:32:35,650
(Lingering at the garden gate)

1988
01:32:35,651 --> 01:32:38,486
(So close, yet so far.)

1989
01:32:38,487 --> 01:32:40,288
If there's no path, I'll just make one.

1990
01:32:41,323 --> 01:32:42,657
Do we need to go farther out?

1991
01:32:53,635 --> 01:32:56,905
I figured that path wasn't there
for no reason.

1992
01:32:56,906 --> 01:32:58,639
So I kept following it.

1993
01:32:58,640 --> 01:33:00,541
(She found the sign.)

1994
01:33:00,542 --> 01:33:01,809
(Love Hideout)

1995
01:33:01,810 --> 01:33:04,445
- She found it!
- She found the Love Hideout.

1996
01:33:04,446 --> 01:33:06,013
Go, Yu Ra.

1997
01:33:06,114 --> 01:33:07,581
Who did she give her note to?

1998
01:33:07,582 --> 01:33:08,582
Ji Hwan.

1999
01:33:20,328 --> 01:33:22,163
(Dong Su finds the Love Hideout too.)

2000
01:33:22,164 --> 01:33:23,330
Is this the Love Hideout?

2001
01:33:33,942 --> 01:33:36,577
(The Love Hideout's doorbell
rings for the first time.)

2002
01:33:36,578 --> 01:33:38,846
I honestly...

2003
01:33:39,514 --> 01:33:42,583
strutted up like a total hero...

2004
01:33:43,051 --> 01:33:43,984
and rang the bell.

2005
01:33:47,689 --> 01:33:48,689
Did you ring it?

2006
01:33:49,958 --> 01:33:51,892
I thought I was first,
when out of nowhere...

2007
01:33:51,893 --> 01:33:52,960
she just pops out.

2008
01:33:53,295 --> 01:33:55,362
"Oh, I'm not first."

2009
01:33:55,363 --> 01:33:56,229
Yay!

2010
01:33:57,766 --> 01:33:58,766
Did you find it?

2011
01:33:59,734 --> 01:34:00,901
Oh, there's a sign.

2012
01:34:01,169 --> 01:34:02,102
Yeah.

2013
01:34:02,103 --> 01:34:03,504
Did Yu Ra ring it?

2014
01:34:03,505 --> 01:34:04,571
Yu Ra rang it.

2015
01:34:05,140 --> 01:34:06,107
It says Love Hideout.

2016
01:34:06,108 --> 01:34:08,743
I looked really hard too. Such a bummer.

2017
01:34:09,344 --> 01:34:11,243
I wanted to talk to Ye In.

2018
01:34:11,244 --> 01:34:12,246
So I was pretty bummed.

2019
01:34:12,414 --> 01:34:14,081
(Four guys heading back, defeated)

2020
01:34:14,082 --> 01:34:16,149
- I even went all the way back there.
- Same here.

2021
01:34:16,285 --> 01:34:17,351
At least now we know where it is.

2022
01:34:17,485 --> 01:34:18,351
Did you find it?

2023
01:34:18,653 --> 01:34:20,386
Yu Ra rang it.

2024
01:34:20,387 --> 01:34:21,789
- Where did she find it?
- Where was it?

2025
01:34:21,790 --> 01:34:23,389
- Down there.
- It was over there.

2026
01:34:23,390 --> 01:34:24,424
It's that white house.

2027
01:34:24,693 --> 01:34:26,993
I guess the fastest one really wins.

2028
01:34:26,994 --> 01:34:29,563
Day one is so wild.

2029
01:34:29,564 --> 01:34:31,031
That one? The white one?

2030
01:34:31,032 --> 01:34:32,332
Yeah, that white building.

2031
01:34:35,003 --> 01:34:35,936
A whole night.

2032
01:34:37,004 --> 01:34:38,806
Do we get the tea tomorrow?

2033
01:34:38,807 --> 01:34:39,907
I'm dying to know.

2034
01:34:40,208 --> 01:34:41,174
Right?

2035
01:34:44,145 --> 01:34:46,913
(Tonight's Love Hideout
passcode is 1111*.)

2036
01:35:05,633 --> 01:35:10,203
(A little space just for two)

2037
01:35:23,785 --> 01:35:25,519
There was a welcome guide.

2038
01:35:25,653 --> 01:35:28,054
I thought it was the same
as the main house one.

2039
01:35:28,055 --> 01:35:30,590
So I skimmed through it.

2040
01:35:30,725 --> 01:35:32,359
And at the bottom it said...

2041
01:35:33,495 --> 01:35:35,629
"No early check-outs allowed."

2042
01:35:35,630 --> 01:35:37,864
That's the first line that caught my eye.

2043
01:35:44,305 --> 01:35:45,672
Check-out is at 10 a.m.

2044
01:35:46,007 --> 01:35:47,107
My gosh, until then?

2045
01:35:47,108 --> 01:35:48,976
Isn't that the best?

2046
01:35:48,977 --> 01:35:50,744
So on the very day they meet,

2047
01:35:50,745 --> 01:35:52,980
she has to spend the night under one roof
with a total stranger.

2048
01:35:52,981 --> 01:35:54,848
How is that even okay?

2049
01:35:55,450 --> 01:35:57,784
What happened to the producers
over the past two years?

2050
01:35:58,386 --> 01:36:01,388
I think they spent the whole time
studying dopamine.

2051
01:36:01,389 --> 01:36:03,333
- Opened a dopamine lab.
- A full-blown research lab.

2052
01:36:03,358 --> 01:36:04,358
Yeah.

2053
01:36:06,428 --> 01:36:08,328
(Heading upstairs)

2054
01:36:10,298 --> 01:36:11,632
Oh, man.

2055
01:36:11,633 --> 01:36:12,733
I'm in trouble.

2056
01:36:20,141 --> 01:36:22,809
(Spare bedding)

2057
01:36:23,011 --> 01:36:24,879
Why did you even leave spare bedding?

2058
01:36:25,180 --> 01:36:26,213
Totally unnecessary.

2059
01:36:26,614 --> 01:36:28,616
So they're sharing the bed, then?

2060
01:36:29,195 --> 01:36:29,917
I guess so.

2061
01:36:32,086 --> 01:36:33,453
I went up to the second floor...

2062
01:36:33,454 --> 01:36:35,722
and was shocked to see
there was only one bed.

2063
01:36:35,990 --> 01:36:39,492
Spending the night here
with a guy I pick...

2064
01:36:39,493 --> 01:36:41,194
is a little awkward.

2065
01:36:42,029 --> 01:36:43,363
I'm in so much trouble.

2066
01:36:43,364 --> 01:36:44,864
This is so wrong.

2067
01:36:45,500 --> 01:36:48,368
My brother is going to find out...

2068
01:36:48,369 --> 01:36:52,472
I spent the night alone
with a guy in the Hideout.

2069
01:36:52,473 --> 01:36:53,974
When we run into each other,

2070
01:36:55,076 --> 01:36:56,878
I feel like I'll get a death glare.

2071
01:36:58,846 --> 01:37:00,480
Who is Yu Ra's brother again?

2072
01:37:00,615 --> 01:37:01,748
In Joong.

2073
01:37:02,350 --> 01:37:04,418
Now she kind of looks like Jin Sung.

2074
01:37:04,419 --> 01:37:05,419
Come on.

2075
01:37:06,921 --> 01:37:09,456
- Yeah.
- Their eyes are identical.

2076
01:37:14,862 --> 01:37:17,096
(Call and invite the person you want...)

2077
01:37:17,097 --> 01:37:19,699
(to spend tonight with
at the Love Hideout.)

2078
01:37:25,139 --> 01:37:27,374
I was weighing who to call.

2079
01:37:27,375 --> 01:37:31,077
And knowing I couldn't leave
until 10 in the morning,

2080
01:37:31,078 --> 01:37:32,579
it was a really tough decision.

2081
01:37:37,585 --> 01:37:39,686
It felt like I agonized over it forever.

2082
01:37:45,727 --> 01:37:48,362
(After a long debate,
she picks up the phone.)

2083
01:37:56,537 --> 01:38:00,907
(Who will Yu Ra invite
to the Love Hideout?)

2084
01:38:08,716 --> 01:38:09,582
What's that?

2085
01:38:09,583 --> 01:38:10,950
(The house phone rings.)

2086
01:38:11,085 --> 01:38:11,951
What's that?

2087
01:38:13,655 --> 01:38:14,488
It's ringing.

2088
01:38:14,889 --> 01:38:16,990
Ji Hwan must be so flustered.

2089
01:38:17,324 --> 01:38:18,758
- Should I get it?
- Yeah.

2090
01:38:23,164 --> 01:38:24,598
Hello?

2091
01:38:25,234 --> 01:38:26,867
- Hello.
- Yes.

2092
01:38:27,902 --> 01:38:29,369
- Could you...
- Yes?

2093
01:38:33,007 --> 01:38:35,075
put Dong Su on?

2094
01:38:35,343 --> 01:38:37,344
Could you put Dong Su on?

2095
01:38:38,346 --> 01:38:39,746
- Why?
- Dong Su?

2096
01:38:42,150 --> 01:38:43,083
Dong Su?

2097
01:38:44,018 --> 01:38:45,086
For real?

2098
01:38:45,087 --> 01:38:47,153
- What is going on?
- She's putting Dong Su...

2099
01:38:47,154 --> 01:38:48,888
on an emotional roller coaster.

2100
01:38:49,390 --> 01:38:50,623
Not Ji Hwan?

2101
01:38:51,225 --> 01:38:55,628
Could you put Dong Su on?

2102
01:38:55,930 --> 01:38:56,963
Oh, sure. Got it.

2103
01:38:57,432 --> 01:38:58,832
- Thank you.
- Yep.

2104
01:38:59,067 --> 01:39:00,401
Oh, sure. Got it.

2105
01:39:00,402 --> 01:39:01,502
Thank you.

2106
01:39:06,641 --> 01:39:08,842
One-on-one, the person...

2107
01:39:08,843 --> 01:39:11,878
I'd have the most fun with is Dong Su.

2108
01:39:12,413 --> 01:39:15,115
And when I went upstairs earlier,

2109
01:39:15,116 --> 01:39:17,016
the second I locked eyes with that guitar,

2110
01:39:17,017 --> 01:39:18,418
I knew it had to be Dong Su.

2111
01:39:18,553 --> 01:39:20,354
(Earlier while drinking)

2112
01:39:20,355 --> 01:39:22,089
- I play the guitar.
- Are you any good?

2113
01:39:22,323 --> 01:39:23,791
Good enough to have fun.

2114
01:39:25,727 --> 01:39:28,762
He mentioned he loves singing
while playing guitar.

2115
01:39:28,897 --> 01:39:29,830
Dong Su.

2116
01:39:30,264 --> 01:39:31,130
Dong Su.

2117
01:39:32,367 --> 01:39:33,800
Head on over...

2118
01:39:34,702 --> 01:39:35,802
to the Love Hideout.

2119
01:39:38,506 --> 01:39:39,606
It felt great.

2120
01:39:39,607 --> 01:39:41,107
I didn't think it'd be me.

2121
01:39:41,108 --> 01:39:44,044
I figured she was curious about Ji Hwan.

2122
01:39:44,045 --> 01:39:46,146
Her note went to Ji Hwan, after all.

2123
01:39:46,147 --> 01:39:49,516
So I wanted to go ask her
why she picked me.

2124
01:39:50,385 --> 01:39:51,452
Have fun.

2125
01:39:51,453 --> 01:39:52,453
Have a good night.

2126
01:39:53,054 --> 01:39:54,054
See you tomorrow.

2127
01:39:54,823 --> 01:39:55,956
See ya.

2128
01:39:55,957 --> 01:39:57,792
I guess we won't see you again
until tomorrow.

2129
01:39:58,393 --> 01:39:59,526
This is wild.

2130
01:39:59,732 --> 01:40:00,952
I thought she'd pick Ji Hwan.

2131
01:40:00,965 --> 01:40:03,680
Since Yu Ra gave Ji Hwan her note.

2132
01:40:03,721 --> 01:40:05,233
I was really surprised.

2133
01:40:05,361 --> 01:40:06,733
I never expected her to choose Dong Su.

2134
01:40:06,761 --> 01:40:09,101
I was hoping she'd pick me.

2135
01:40:09,194 --> 01:40:11,134
I'd even gotten a note from her,

2136
01:40:11,467 --> 01:40:14,174
so I was expecting her call.

2137
01:40:14,414 --> 01:40:18,047
I got the vibe that Min Seo was
interested in Dong Su,

2138
01:40:18,094 --> 01:40:21,115
so I was glad Dong Su went with Yu Ra.

2139
01:40:21,314 --> 01:40:23,017
I was happy I got to stay with Min Seo.

2140
01:40:23,518 --> 01:40:24,759
This is fun.

2141
01:40:26,172 --> 01:40:28,222
Things are already getting complicated.

2142
01:40:28,822 --> 01:40:31,119
- It's only been one day.
- This is fun.

2143
01:40:31,926 --> 01:40:33,732
It feels like three days packed into one.

2144
01:40:33,733 --> 01:40:34,695
Totally.

2145
01:40:39,193 --> 01:40:41,519
(He heads to the Love Hideout.)

2146
01:40:57,518 --> 01:40:59,624
I was smiling the whole way over,

2147
01:40:59,745 --> 01:41:00,821
but I was nervous too.

2148
01:41:00,951 --> 01:41:02,323
I felt like I needed to act cool,

2149
01:41:02,351 --> 01:41:03,891
and look my best.

2150
01:41:24,856 --> 01:41:27,503
(The two finally meet.)

2151
01:41:27,736 --> 01:41:28,449
Oh.

2152
01:41:29,422 --> 01:41:31,152
- Hey.
- Hey.

2153
01:41:35,654 --> 01:41:36,623
This is a whole different house.

2154
01:41:36,624 --> 01:41:38,641
(Yu Ra and Dong Su complete their check-in
at the Love Hideout.)

2155
01:41:38,759 --> 01:41:40,461
Head upstairs for a second.

2156
01:41:40,561 --> 01:41:42,663
There's a reason I asked you here.

2157
01:41:42,804 --> 01:41:44,565
- A reason you asked me here?
- Yeah.

2158
01:41:52,963 --> 01:41:53,808
Seriously?

2159
01:41:54,030 --> 01:41:54,976
What do you think?

2160
01:41:57,990 --> 01:41:59,168
(He spots a guitar.)

2161
01:41:59,170 --> 01:42:00,648
- This?
- Do you like it?

2162
01:42:02,416 --> 01:42:03,951
It's even in tune.

2163
01:42:04,819 --> 01:42:06,153
When I walked in, I saw a guitar.

2164
01:42:06,360 --> 01:42:08,456
We'd talked about playing guitar earlier.

2165
01:42:08,500 --> 01:42:09,824
She was hesitating at first,

2166
01:42:09,954 --> 01:42:11,974
but I think seeing the guitar
reminded her of me,

2167
01:42:11,975 --> 01:42:13,694
so she ended up picking me.

2168
01:42:16,092 --> 01:42:18,018
(They find the welcome guide.)

2169
01:42:18,933 --> 01:42:20,768
"Anything that happens here..."

2170
01:42:20,858 --> 01:42:23,337
"must stay between the two of you."

2171
01:42:23,571 --> 01:42:26,474
"You must speak casually to each other
instead of using formal speech."

2172
01:42:26,707 --> 01:42:28,409
"Focus only on each other."

2173
01:42:29,110 --> 01:42:30,578
So we have to speak casually now.

2174
01:42:32,513 --> 01:42:33,514
Should we?

2175
01:42:34,148 --> 01:42:35,116
Should we?

2176
01:42:35,270 --> 01:42:36,017
Sure.

2177
01:42:38,747 --> 01:42:41,088
How did it go? Who got the call?

2178
01:42:42,650 --> 01:42:43,457
In Joong.

2179
01:42:44,025 --> 01:42:45,793
It sounded like In Joong's voice.

2180
01:42:46,494 --> 01:42:47,662
Were you the one who called?

2181
01:42:47,741 --> 01:42:48,896
Yeah, I used this.

2182
01:42:49,572 --> 01:42:50,564
I see.

2183
01:42:51,399 --> 01:42:52,632
I didn't think it'd be me.

2184
01:42:52,825 --> 01:42:53,501
Huh?

2185
01:42:53,599 --> 01:42:54,602
Never thought it'd be me.

2186
01:42:55,036 --> 01:42:55,903
What do you mean?

2187
01:42:58,973 --> 01:43:00,306
The guy you were going to call.

2188
01:43:00,441 --> 01:43:02,737
Really? Why'd you think that?

2189
01:43:05,823 --> 01:43:06,814
Because of the note.

2190
01:43:07,203 --> 01:43:08,649
- The note.
- Yeah.

2191
01:43:10,681 --> 01:43:13,888
But you can use that anytime.

2192
01:43:15,315 --> 01:43:16,850
It doesn't have to be right now.

2193
01:43:17,558 --> 01:43:18,826
So were you disappointed?

2194
01:43:19,667 --> 01:43:20,467
A little.

2195
01:43:21,312 --> 01:43:22,112
A lot.

2196
01:43:23,064 --> 01:43:24,398
You're not hiding it at all.

2197
01:43:24,800 --> 01:43:28,592
She saved her date with Ji Hwan,
and then gave me a shot,

2198
01:43:28,594 --> 01:43:30,594
so I felt like her second choice.

2199
01:43:30,620 --> 01:43:32,239
It didn't feel great.

2200
01:43:32,813 --> 01:43:33,980
And earlier,

2201
01:43:34,474 --> 01:43:37,845
when we switched seats,
you didn't look at me once.

2202
01:43:39,146 --> 01:43:41,048
You didn't, right?

2203
01:43:44,658 --> 01:43:46,220
(Dinner and drinks)

2204
01:43:46,954 --> 01:43:48,689
(Avoiding eye contact while answering)

2205
01:43:49,405 --> 01:43:52,205
(Dong Su didn't make eye contact.)

2206
01:43:54,012 --> 01:43:55,262
I guess it was obvious.

2207
01:43:55,596 --> 01:43:56,964
I wasn't looking at Yu Ra,

2208
01:43:56,985 --> 01:43:58,599
and my hurt feelings must have shown.

2209
01:43:58,892 --> 01:43:59,834
Is there anything to drink?

2210
01:43:59,836 --> 01:44:00,785
(He's parched.)

2211
01:44:00,998 --> 01:44:02,740
- Can you drink?
- Just a little.

2212
01:44:03,804 --> 01:44:05,171
What time do we have to check out?

2213
01:44:05,552 --> 01:44:06,373
Ten.

2214
01:44:06,874 --> 01:44:08,242
We're trapped in here.

2215
01:44:08,465 --> 01:44:09,610
- Huh?
- We can't leave.

2216
01:44:09,944 --> 01:44:11,879
Am I trapped with you,
or just trapped here?

2217
01:44:14,613 --> 01:44:15,449
Both, I guess.

2218
01:44:16,029 --> 01:44:16,917
Both?

2219
01:44:17,946 --> 01:44:20,054
I really thought I'd found
the Love Hideout first.

2220
01:44:21,646 --> 01:44:24,391
And then you just popped out like that.

2221
01:44:26,594 --> 01:44:28,229
- So were you bummed?
- Yeah.

2222
01:44:29,063 --> 01:44:30,698
"Oppa," you were...

2223
01:44:33,400 --> 01:44:35,400
I just called you "oppa" so naturally.

2224
01:44:36,771 --> 01:44:39,473
If you'd gotten here first,
who would you have picked?

2225
01:44:39,740 --> 01:44:41,475
If I'd gotten here first?

2226
01:44:42,563 --> 01:44:43,344
You.

2227
01:44:45,223 --> 01:44:47,223
Why? You said you were upset earlier.

2228
01:44:48,349 --> 01:44:49,416
Being upset and...

2229
01:44:51,735 --> 01:44:54,555
wanting to spend time with someone
are two different things.

2230
01:44:58,616 --> 01:44:59,859
This is so entertaining.

2231
01:44:59,860 --> 01:45:02,007
- Dong Su is no ordinary guy.
- This is fun.

2232
01:45:02,009 --> 01:45:03,531
His name might sound old-school,

2233
01:45:04,936 --> 01:45:06,166
but he's anything but.

2234
01:45:07,542 --> 01:45:09,937
He's a total flirt.

2235
01:45:11,360 --> 01:45:13,274
He's got a whole different side to him.

2236
01:45:14,575 --> 01:45:15,609
Being upset and...

2237
01:45:17,945 --> 01:45:20,748
wanting to spend time with someone
are two different things.

2238
01:45:24,852 --> 01:45:26,420
He said, "you."

2239
01:45:27,038 --> 01:45:28,622
That's what he said.

2240
01:45:28,658 --> 01:45:30,024
It made me shy.

2241
01:45:31,058 --> 01:45:33,058
I guess I was meant to come
to the Love Hideout.

2242
01:45:34,376 --> 01:45:37,464
My heart was set on picking Yu Ra.

2243
01:45:37,569 --> 01:45:39,569
And Yu Ra called me too,

2244
01:45:39,583 --> 01:45:41,135
so that place was meant to be our house.

2245
01:45:42,929 --> 01:45:44,194
- "Our house?"
- "Our house?"

2246
01:45:44,234 --> 01:45:46,340
Are they already buying a place together?

2247
01:45:46,354 --> 01:45:48,242
- Are they buying a place already?
- "Our house?"

2248
01:45:48,294 --> 01:45:50,978
- They do seem to have a similar vibe.
- Exactly.

2249
01:45:51,180 --> 01:45:53,180
They already look like a couple.

2250
01:45:53,260 --> 01:45:55,652
(The Sibling House)

2251
01:45:57,305 --> 01:45:58,252
Can you see anything?

2252
01:45:58,612 --> 01:46:01,055
No, just the big lights.

2253
01:46:02,225 --> 01:46:04,885
(He even tries making binoculars
with his fingers.)

2254
01:46:05,072 --> 01:46:06,430
That place looks like a fortress.

2255
01:46:07,695 --> 01:46:10,664
I could see the Love Hideout clearly.

2256
01:46:11,031 --> 01:46:14,435
Everyone was saying they'd sprint over
if there were another mission.

2257
01:46:14,735 --> 01:46:16,426
Hearing all about it tomorrow
is going to be so fun.

2258
01:46:16,450 --> 01:46:17,670
I have no idea what to expect.

2259
01:46:17,910 --> 01:46:19,373
I'm so curious.

2260
01:46:19,403 --> 01:46:21,775
I'm sure it's completely different
from this house.

2261
01:46:21,916 --> 01:46:25,512
They'll probably have way more time
to talk and hang out.

2262
01:46:25,762 --> 01:46:26,583
This is so fun.

2263
01:46:27,623 --> 01:46:30,618
So much unexpected stuff
has happened on day one.

2264
01:46:30,816 --> 01:46:34,150
(The first day was full of surprises.)

2265
01:46:34,256 --> 01:46:36,506
(The Love Hideout)

2266
01:46:41,228 --> 01:46:42,529
Should I bring the guitar?

2267
01:46:43,966 --> 01:46:45,432
I feel like I'm putting pressure on you.

2268
01:46:45,900 --> 01:46:47,334
Because at first, oppa...

2269
01:46:48,091 --> 01:46:49,503
Why do I keep calling you "oppa"?

2270
01:46:49,837 --> 01:46:50,871
You see me as an older brother, right?

2271
01:46:50,904 --> 01:46:52,373
Then what should I call you?

2272
01:46:52,873 --> 01:46:54,077
Dong Su?

2273
01:46:54,531 --> 01:46:56,243
Just call me whatever feels natural.

2274
01:46:58,031 --> 01:47:00,014
- "Just call me whatever feels natural."
- "Just call me whatever feels natural."

2275
01:47:00,191 --> 01:47:01,750
What's with this guy?

2276
01:47:01,752 --> 01:47:03,124
This is so exciting.

2277
01:47:03,125 --> 01:47:04,118
What's with him?

2278
01:47:04,152 --> 01:47:05,719
I live for this kind of stuff.

2279
01:47:05,772 --> 01:47:07,588
Just call me whatever feels natural.

2280
01:47:10,392 --> 01:47:13,727
It feels like I'm peeking in
through the window.

2281
01:47:13,729 --> 01:47:14,962
Right?

2282
01:47:16,389 --> 01:47:17,231
Are you warm?

2283
01:47:17,649 --> 01:47:19,322
(It's so hot.)

2284
01:47:21,149 --> 01:47:23,835
Yu Ra slipped into calling me
older brother.

2285
01:47:24,756 --> 01:47:26,973
It felt like hearing something
I'd been waiting for.

2286
01:47:27,009 --> 01:47:31,278
From the second I saw her,
I figured she was younger than me.

2287
01:47:31,382 --> 01:47:34,149
I just couldn't bring myself to call him
by his first name right away.

2288
01:47:34,189 --> 01:47:38,519
And he has that mature, older-guy vibe.

2289
01:47:39,094 --> 01:47:44,024
I think speaking casually really
helped us break the ice.

2290
01:47:44,107 --> 01:47:46,501
(The two head upstairs.)

2291
01:47:46,554 --> 01:47:49,065
(They find a Polaroid camera.)

2292
01:47:49,179 --> 01:47:51,565
- Should I pose like this?
- With the guitar?

2293
01:47:52,292 --> 01:47:54,200
- Are you going to hold it like that?
- How's this?

2294
01:47:56,552 --> 01:47:57,304
I'll take it.

2295
01:47:57,305 --> 01:47:58,704
One, two, three.

2296
01:47:59,011 --> 01:47:59,974
You look like a model.

2297
01:48:00,452 --> 01:48:01,809
Why can't I do it?

2298
01:48:02,012 --> 01:48:02,977
Because I'm older.

2299
01:48:04,765 --> 01:48:06,765
We can write a little message on it too.

2300
01:48:06,892 --> 01:48:08,114
Aren't you going to write one?

2301
01:48:09,009 --> 01:48:09,850
By the way...

2302
01:48:10,882 --> 01:48:11,952
I will.

2303
01:48:14,149 --> 01:48:15,022
Should I take one?

2304
01:48:15,435 --> 01:48:16,256
Together?

2305
01:48:22,782 --> 01:48:23,797
The film is...

2306
01:48:26,556 --> 01:48:28,669
Your accent really comes out
when you get comfortable.

2307
01:48:28,775 --> 01:48:29,870
- Me?
- Yeah.

2308
01:48:30,149 --> 01:48:31,138
I don't have an accent.

2309
01:48:31,335 --> 01:48:32,573
It's nighttime now.

2310
01:48:32,806 --> 01:48:33,941
It's really late.

2311
01:48:33,945 --> 01:48:35,275
(On the first day,
they had a secret of their own.)

2312
01:48:35,943 --> 01:48:37,544
I'm suddenly wide awake.

2313
01:48:37,742 --> 01:48:38,779
All of a sudden?

2314
01:48:39,696 --> 01:48:42,683
It's crazy that I'm showing
this side of myself so soon.

2315
01:48:43,229 --> 01:48:44,425
Should we turn off the lights?

2316
01:48:44,449 --> 01:48:46,220
Go on up. I'll turn them off and head up.

2317
01:48:48,202 --> 01:48:50,714
(The two get ready for bed.)

2318
01:48:50,840 --> 01:48:52,726
This feels so surreal.

2319
01:48:53,460 --> 01:48:55,896
It didn't really sink in earlier.

2320
01:48:56,447 --> 01:48:58,899
Being here like this feels
totally different.

2321
01:49:00,000 --> 01:49:01,568
It feels like a dream right now.

2322
01:49:01,645 --> 01:49:02,736
- A dream?
- Yeah.

2323
01:49:06,798 --> 01:49:09,118
- They really look like a couple.
- Totally.

2324
01:49:09,143 --> 01:49:11,094
Just this morning,
they were in separate houses.

2325
01:49:11,118 --> 01:49:12,112
I know.

2326
01:49:12,205 --> 01:49:14,089
Until this morning,
those two were strangers.

2327
01:49:14,091 --> 01:49:15,548
- That's right.
- Complete strangers.

2328
01:49:15,663 --> 01:49:16,683
No way.

2329
01:49:16,925 --> 01:49:18,519
My Sibling's Romance has awakened.

2330
01:49:18,819 --> 01:49:20,087
They are possessed by demons.

2331
01:49:21,726 --> 01:49:22,511
At this point...

2332
01:49:22,535 --> 01:49:24,358
"What have we been missing all this time?"

2333
01:49:25,325 --> 01:49:26,495
Will we be able to sleep?

2334
01:49:26,527 --> 01:49:27,961
Are you tired? Getting sleepy?

2335
01:49:29,359 --> 01:49:30,497
How could we possibly be sleepy?

2336
01:49:32,699 --> 01:49:35,269
I feel a little different
than I did earlier.

2337
01:49:35,546 --> 01:49:36,670
What's different?

2338
01:49:38,238 --> 01:49:39,373
Unbelievable.

2339
01:49:40,808 --> 01:49:42,550
- Can I talk like this?
- Sure.

2340
01:49:43,584 --> 01:49:45,111
I'm so self-conscious about my bare face.

2341
01:49:45,364 --> 01:49:46,080
Oh.

2342
01:49:46,880 --> 01:49:47,915
My eyesight is terrible.

2343
01:49:48,749 --> 01:49:49,950
I took my contacts out.

2344
01:49:51,130 --> 01:49:52,055
- Really?
- Yeah.

2345
01:49:52,962 --> 01:49:54,588
Okay, I'll take your word for it.

2346
01:50:01,039 --> 01:50:03,129
Let me know if you're uncomfortable.
I can sleep on the floor.

2347
01:50:03,534 --> 01:50:04,549
No, it's fine.

2348
01:50:07,609 --> 01:50:09,763
There was a mattress topper
next to the bed too,

2349
01:50:09,787 --> 01:50:12,989
but I just ignored it
and climbed into bed.

2350
01:50:13,468 --> 01:50:16,790
I figured since I was already there,
I might as well sleep on it.

2351
01:50:16,815 --> 01:50:18,251
Though it was super awkward.

2352
01:50:20,582 --> 01:50:21,353
This is wild.

2353
01:50:22,662 --> 01:50:23,489
It feels surreal.

2354
01:50:33,249 --> 01:50:35,167
Hey, since you're already in there!

2355
01:50:35,242 --> 01:50:36,697
If their parents saw this...

2356
01:50:37,349 --> 01:50:38,166
Wouldn't they?

2357
01:50:38,190 --> 01:50:40,549
Our parents became parents
the same way, didn't they?

2358
01:50:42,163 --> 01:50:43,308
That's the truth.

2359
01:50:43,429 --> 01:50:44,471
Should I turn off the lights?

2360
01:50:44,909 --> 01:50:45,655
Yeah.

2361
01:50:49,629 --> 01:50:50,129
What?

2362
01:50:51,193 --> 01:50:51,850
Nothing.

2363
01:50:52,871 --> 01:50:53,719
Can't sleep?

2364
01:50:53,959 --> 01:50:54,459
Huh?

2365
01:50:54,599 --> 01:50:55,588
Can't sleep?

2366
01:50:56,355 --> 01:50:57,189
Just a little.

2367
01:50:58,434 --> 01:50:59,459
Goodnight.

2368
01:51:00,073 --> 01:51:00,893
Goodnight.

2369
01:51:02,629 --> 01:51:03,863
Aren't you going to roll off?

2370
01:51:04,069 --> 01:51:04,630
Me?

2371
01:51:04,889 --> 01:51:06,364
I have tons of room over here.

2372
01:51:06,365 --> 01:51:07,433
- You have plenty of space?
- Yeah.

2373
01:51:11,109 --> 01:51:12,239
I have a question.

2374
01:51:12,565 --> 01:51:13,305
What is it?

2375
01:51:14,182 --> 01:51:17,343
So, we've met twice now.

2376
01:51:17,615 --> 01:51:18,310
Yeah.

2377
01:51:19,745 --> 01:51:20,713
How are you feeling?

2378
01:51:21,107 --> 01:51:23,415
About going to the hut...

2379
01:51:27,189 --> 01:51:28,487
It suddenly got warm.

2380
01:51:28,806 --> 01:51:29,555
Are you hot?

2381
01:51:30,299 --> 01:51:31,791
- Why?
- Did something happen?

2382
01:51:31,819 --> 01:51:32,890
I can't see anything.

2383
01:51:32,915 --> 01:51:35,428
Turn on the infrared!

2384
01:51:35,453 --> 01:51:36,762
We can't see.

2385
01:51:36,912 --> 01:51:38,164
I can't see a thing.

2386
01:51:38,239 --> 01:51:41,067
Why are they making it so dark
and driving us crazy?

2387
01:51:41,901 --> 01:51:43,574
I can't see anything. What happened?

2388
01:51:43,599 --> 01:51:44,299
I can't see.

2389
01:51:44,300 --> 01:51:46,614
Technology is so advanced these days.
Turn on the infrared!

2390
01:51:46,639 --> 01:51:49,014
That's what I'm saying.
Why aren't they using night vision?

2391
01:51:49,039 --> 01:51:50,776
I can't see. What's going on?

2392
01:51:52,012 --> 01:51:53,312
It suddenly got warm.

2393
01:51:53,599 --> 01:51:54,280
Are you hot?

2394
01:51:55,059 --> 01:51:56,990
- You can turn down the AC.
- No, I'm good.

2395
01:51:57,419 --> 01:51:59,873
Because you picked me,

2396
01:52:00,634 --> 01:52:02,939
I genuinely felt really grateful.

2397
01:52:03,919 --> 01:52:06,880
And you're someone
I'd already talked to once before.

2398
01:52:06,905 --> 01:52:07,593
Right.

2399
01:52:09,819 --> 01:52:10,730
This is so nice.

2400
01:52:11,412 --> 01:52:13,432
I'm glad we found this hideout.

2401
01:52:15,029 --> 01:52:16,202
Should I play the guitar for you?

2402
01:52:16,752 --> 01:52:17,537
Right now?

2403
01:52:17,605 --> 01:52:19,171
Could you play it as a wake-up song
tomorrow instead?

2404
01:52:19,212 --> 01:52:21,107
- A wake-up song?
- Yeah, like an alarm.

2405
01:52:23,149 --> 01:52:26,677
(Early dawn, before the sun comes up)

2406
01:52:28,676 --> 01:52:30,676
(Yu Ra tossing and turning)

2407
01:52:34,217 --> 01:52:35,021
What's wrong?

2408
01:52:39,786 --> 01:52:40,593
A bug...

2409
01:52:42,179 --> 01:52:43,129
Is there a bug?

2410
01:52:44,309 --> 01:52:46,339
No, I don't know where it went.

2411
01:52:47,839 --> 01:52:48,919
It startled me.

2412
01:52:48,968 --> 01:52:49,969
You scared me.

2413
01:52:53,144 --> 01:52:55,439
(Trying to go back to sleep)

2414
01:52:57,592 --> 01:52:59,345
(Spotting the bug from earlier)

2415
01:53:01,945 --> 01:53:02,682
There it is.

2416
01:53:02,843 --> 01:53:05,047
(Springing into action
at a single word from Yu Ra)

2417
01:53:05,079 --> 01:53:06,752
There's a spider on the wall.

2418
01:53:06,777 --> 01:53:07,777
(Tissues at the ready)

2419
01:53:08,045 --> 01:53:09,088
Wow.

2420
01:53:09,811 --> 01:53:11,774
(Catching the bug without hesitation)

2421
01:53:11,799 --> 01:53:12,959
None left, right?

2422
01:53:13,209 --> 01:53:14,236
(Bolts upright)

2423
01:53:14,678 --> 01:53:15,555
Is there another one?

2424
01:53:15,784 --> 01:53:16,831
(Laughing)

2425
01:53:17,479 --> 01:53:18,798
Are you Cesco?

2426
01:53:19,292 --> 01:53:21,512
(Dongsco, who never sleeps)

2427
01:53:21,912 --> 01:53:22,932
All clear now, right?

2428
01:53:23,559 --> 01:53:25,159
He went, "What's wrong?"
and woke right up.

2429
01:53:25,405 --> 01:53:26,272
"Is there a bug?"

2430
01:53:26,699 --> 01:53:29,019
Dong Su worked so hard to catch it for me.

2431
01:53:29,419 --> 01:53:31,139
I called him Cesco.

2432
01:53:31,342 --> 01:53:33,221
He handled it so easily.

2433
01:53:33,246 --> 01:53:34,914
He wasn't scared at all.

2434
01:53:34,939 --> 01:53:36,549
It made my heart flutter a little.

2435
01:53:36,574 --> 01:53:38,951
I think we got a lot closer
thanks to that bug.

2436
01:53:41,541 --> 01:53:44,347
(Dongsco's thoughtfulness)

2437
01:53:44,545 --> 01:53:46,165
This could become a cute nickname for him.

2438
01:53:46,190 --> 01:53:47,526
Just between the two of them.

2439
01:53:47,659 --> 01:53:49,254
- Cesco.
- Like Dongsco.

2440
01:53:49,279 --> 01:53:53,139
Wait, after all this, could anything
still happen with Ji Hwan?

2441
01:53:53,164 --> 01:53:54,822
If Yu Ra is clever enough...

2442
01:53:54,846 --> 01:53:57,603
to split her date passes
into two separate dates...

2443
01:53:57,819 --> 01:53:58,319
Right.

2444
01:53:58,344 --> 01:54:00,806
- She won't give her heart away easily.
- I think she can handle it.

2445
01:54:04,898 --> 01:54:07,497
(Morning breaks at the Love Hideout.)

2446
01:54:15,149 --> 01:54:16,355
The weather is amazing.

2447
01:54:17,069 --> 01:54:21,010
(Their first morning together)

2448
01:54:22,353 --> 01:54:24,366
(Dong Su makes the bed.)

2449
01:54:26,139 --> 01:54:28,754
(Even tidying up the room neatly)

2450
01:54:29,799 --> 01:54:31,004
What do you want to eat?

2451
01:54:31,398 --> 01:54:32,271
Just Greek yogurt?

2452
01:54:32,698 --> 01:54:33,806
With eggs on the side.

2453
01:54:34,139 --> 01:54:34,774
Eggs?

2454
01:54:34,799 --> 01:54:36,457
(Scrambled eggs made just for Yu Ra)

2455
01:54:38,079 --> 01:54:40,112
We're having a miracle morning, aren't we?

2456
01:54:41,025 --> 01:54:42,954
I honestly have no idea
how this will taste.

2457
01:54:42,979 --> 01:54:44,383
Just how clueless are you?

2458
01:54:45,141 --> 01:54:46,619
I bet it'll taste great.

2459
01:54:47,039 --> 01:54:47,987
Thanks for the food.

2460
01:54:48,532 --> 01:54:50,021
- Dig in.
- I wonder how good it'll be.

2461
01:54:59,102 --> 01:55:00,032
It's delicious.

2462
01:55:00,702 --> 01:55:02,301
Your eyes are really brown.

2463
01:55:04,748 --> 01:55:05,771
I'm wearing contacts.

2464
01:55:06,229 --> 01:55:07,506
- No way, you're lying.
- I'm serious.

2465
01:55:08,839 --> 01:55:10,376
You're not wearing contacts right now?

2466
01:55:10,401 --> 01:55:12,178
Then you can't see me?

2467
01:55:12,599 --> 01:55:13,746
I got LASIK.

2468
01:55:13,869 --> 01:55:14,613
What?

2469
01:55:16,289 --> 01:55:17,116
You're lying.

2470
01:55:17,669 --> 01:55:19,218
These are LASIK eyes.

2471
01:55:19,243 --> 01:55:21,854
Yesterday you told me
you had bad eyesight.

2472
01:55:22,149 --> 01:55:23,456
I pretended I couldn't see.

2473
01:55:25,789 --> 01:55:28,060
Doesn't seem like much
of a difference, or is there?

2474
01:55:30,869 --> 01:55:31,730
Thank you.

2475
01:55:32,222 --> 01:55:33,202
This feels nice.

2476
01:55:35,862 --> 01:55:37,303
Though I did have this thought.

2477
01:55:37,795 --> 01:55:39,878
It would've been even better
if we'd come here...

2478
01:55:39,902 --> 01:55:41,140
after getting a bit closer first.

2479
01:55:41,701 --> 01:55:42,374
True.

2480
01:55:45,515 --> 01:55:46,845
We still have plenty of time.

2481
01:55:47,516 --> 01:55:48,514
It's only been two days.

2482
01:55:49,048 --> 01:55:52,337
That whole Cesco moment
helped break the ice a bit,

2483
01:55:52,361 --> 01:55:54,386
so the morning felt
a lot more comfortable.

2484
01:56:00,058 --> 01:56:01,687
This looks like a music video right now.

2485
01:56:01,712 --> 01:56:03,958
Honestly, Dong Su's gaze is a little...

2486
01:56:03,982 --> 01:56:05,335
He's fallen hard, hasn't he?

2487
01:56:05,470 --> 01:56:07,266
- Those are the eyes of someone in love.
- Totally.

2488
01:56:08,159 --> 01:56:09,068
What time is it?

2489
01:56:09,705 --> 01:56:10,645
Twenty-five past.

2490
01:56:11,079 --> 01:56:11,737
Already?

2491
01:56:12,258 --> 01:56:13,818
Time flies so fast.

2492
01:56:13,843 --> 01:56:15,103
(Check-out time is 10 a.m.)

2493
01:56:15,999 --> 01:56:19,011
Doesn't the air feel kind of humid?

2494
01:56:19,632 --> 01:56:21,213
Still, the weather is gorgeous.

2495
01:56:22,485 --> 01:56:23,649
It's nice because the sky is clear.

2496
01:56:30,516 --> 01:56:33,974
The weather was amazing,
with a gentle breeze blowing.

2497
01:56:33,998 --> 01:56:38,141
The vibe back then felt exciting and nice.

2498
01:56:38,166 --> 01:56:41,369
Do you prefer someone
in a similar line of work to yours?

2499
01:56:41,394 --> 01:56:44,136
Or someone
with a completely different job?

2500
01:56:44,969 --> 01:56:45,938
Completely different.

2501
01:56:46,009 --> 01:56:47,329
Completely different? Why?

2502
01:56:47,839 --> 01:56:49,763
I just want to experience
the charm of someone...

2503
01:56:49,787 --> 01:56:51,877
who does something completely different.

2504
01:56:52,815 --> 01:56:56,555
The exact opposite of what I'm used to.

2505
01:56:56,580 --> 01:56:57,749
The complete opposite?

2506
01:56:57,895 --> 01:56:58,818
That's tough.

2507
01:57:00,255 --> 01:57:01,989
I'm curious about what you do.

2508
01:57:02,455 --> 01:57:04,589
I feel like I'll see you differently
once I find out.

2509
01:57:04,683 --> 01:57:05,391
Right.

2510
01:57:06,755 --> 01:57:08,661
I think that definitely changes things.

2511
01:57:09,522 --> 01:57:11,397
When we go back,
we have to speak formally again.

2512
01:57:12,362 --> 01:57:13,499
It's back to "Mr. Dong Su."

2513
01:57:13,649 --> 01:57:15,548
I might accidentally slip
and call you "Yu Ra."

2514
01:57:16,289 --> 01:57:17,002
You can't!

2515
01:57:17,702 --> 01:57:19,939
Switching back to formal speech
is going to feel a bit...

2516
01:57:20,428 --> 01:57:23,622
Or on the flip side, I'll just start
speaking casually to everyone else too.

2517
01:57:23,654 --> 01:57:25,169
Like, "Hey, Jin Sung."

2518
01:57:25,190 --> 01:57:25,690
"Ye In."

2519
01:57:25,849 --> 01:57:27,079
Jin Sung would be totally thrown off.

2520
01:57:27,197 --> 01:57:27,947
Right?

2521
01:57:34,638 --> 01:57:38,208
(The phone rings at the Love Hideout.)

2522
01:57:40,462 --> 01:57:41,727
Hello?

2523
01:57:46,309 --> 01:57:46,932
Yes?

2524
01:57:48,195 --> 01:57:48,868
Pardon?

2525
01:57:52,592 --> 01:57:54,239
Yes, would you like me to put him on?

2526
01:57:57,819 --> 01:57:58,477
Yes.

2527
01:58:00,004 --> 01:58:00,579
Yes.

2528
01:58:02,605 --> 01:58:03,845
Mr. Dong Su.

2529
01:58:04,859 --> 01:58:05,512
Yes?

2530
01:58:06,065 --> 01:58:07,679
What is this phone call?

2531
01:58:07,798 --> 01:58:09,721
- Who's calling for "Mr. Dong Su"?
- What's this call about?

2532
01:58:09,746 --> 01:58:11,790
It feels like an investigative news show.

2533
01:58:12,218 --> 01:58:13,192
Mr. Dong Su.

2534
01:58:14,479 --> 01:58:14,979
Yes?

2535
01:58:15,552 --> 01:58:17,129
How are you liking the Love Hideout?

2536
01:58:17,679 --> 01:58:18,998
It's really great.

2537
01:58:19,825 --> 01:58:20,799
It's me.

2538
01:58:22,519 --> 01:58:23,135
Pardon?

2539
01:58:23,679 --> 01:58:24,603
It's me!

2540
01:58:29,789 --> 01:58:30,743
Oh.

2541
01:58:31,792 --> 01:58:32,477
Yes.

2542
01:58:33,859 --> 01:58:35,180
How are things going for you?

2543
01:58:37,535 --> 01:58:40,997
(Who is the person calling Dong Su?)

2544
01:58:41,171 --> 01:58:42,703
- His younger sister! Who is it?
- Who is she?

2545
01:58:42,728 --> 01:58:45,157
- Sounds like Min Seo's voice.
- She has long hair.

2546
01:58:45,182 --> 01:58:46,422
It's Min Seo.

2547
01:58:46,535 --> 01:58:48,260
Isn't Min Seo matched with Jin Sung?

2548
01:58:48,555 --> 01:58:50,547
Jwa Hyeon. It's one of the two.

2549
01:58:50,572 --> 01:58:52,625
Because her hair is brown,
comes down to here,

2550
01:58:52,649 --> 01:58:53,532
and she has long nails.

2551
01:58:53,669 --> 01:58:55,134
Wait, it wasn't Ye In?

2552
01:58:55,229 --> 01:58:56,969
Everything just got scrambled for us.

2553
01:58:56,994 --> 01:58:57,894
I know, right?

2554
01:58:58,269 --> 01:58:58,971
All our guesses...

2555
01:58:59,011 --> 01:59:02,103
(Who is the person calling Dong Su?)

2556
01:59:02,422 --> 01:59:04,892
A free-spirited little kid?

2557
01:59:04,917 --> 01:59:06,057
She's a total baby.

2558
01:59:06,355 --> 01:59:07,980
Like a kid playing out on the lawn.

2559
01:59:08,005 --> 01:59:09,925
She was so pretty back then.

2560
01:59:10,579 --> 01:59:11,969
She was prettier back then.

2561
01:59:11,994 --> 01:59:12,885
Unbelievable.

2562
01:59:13,948 --> 01:59:15,446
It's Jwa Hyeon!

2563
01:59:15,769 --> 01:59:18,784
No, it's not! You startled me.

2564
01:59:18,809 --> 01:59:19,658
Who is it, then?

2565
01:59:20,035 --> 01:59:21,093
Unbelievable.

2566
01:59:22,089 --> 01:59:24,296
Saying, "Why did you grow up
so much? It's gross."

2567
01:59:24,522 --> 01:59:26,302
We tease each other a lot.

2568
01:59:26,334 --> 01:59:27,266
Are we close?

2569
01:59:27,562 --> 01:59:29,468
We joked around and hung out
almost like friends.

2570
01:59:29,828 --> 01:59:31,748
He constantly gets on my nerves.

2571
01:59:31,773 --> 01:59:33,939
I think everything about me
is great right now.

2572
01:59:34,819 --> 01:59:37,229
As for my looks,
I'm super happy with them.

2573
01:59:37,254 --> 01:59:38,964
- Like, "It's all me"?
- Definitely not.

2574
01:59:38,989 --> 01:59:41,129
Aside from my height,
I'm satisfied with myself.

2575
01:59:41,172 --> 01:59:42,046
(Laughing)

2576
01:59:42,071 --> 01:59:45,089
If he were the type to listen
when I nag him, I'd do it,

2577
01:59:45,227 --> 01:59:46,577
but since he never listens at all...

2578
01:59:46,755 --> 01:59:48,653
He's definitely not the soft type.

2579
01:59:48,678 --> 01:59:49,521
More on the tough side?

2580
01:59:49,825 --> 01:59:52,091
He's pretty empathetic, though.

2581
01:59:52,116 --> 01:59:53,105
- Right.
- For a guy, anyway.

2582
01:59:53,130 --> 01:59:54,809
That's just the kind of guy I am.

2583
02:00:00,049 --> 02:00:04,455
(Revealing Dong Su's sibling)

2584
02:00:08,399 --> 02:00:12,211
Since she started school,
she's only ever danced.

2585
02:00:13,529 --> 02:00:15,001
When I was in college,

2586
02:00:15,025 --> 02:00:17,674
our parents moved
to the countryside first.

2587
02:00:17,699 --> 02:00:20,119
I drove her to and from high school
every single day,

2588
02:00:20,144 --> 02:00:21,186
back when I was a college student.

2589
02:00:21,211 --> 02:00:24,511
I took care of her a lot,
morning and night.

2590
02:00:24,672 --> 02:00:28,160
My parents and I doted on her.

2591
02:00:29,032 --> 02:00:29,962
Like a princess.

2592
02:00:31,712 --> 02:00:33,612
Now that I work alongside my parents,

2593
02:00:33,812 --> 02:00:35,592
I think they rely on me a lot.

2594
02:00:35,866 --> 02:00:38,036
But all their affection went to her.

2595
02:00:39,012 --> 02:00:40,806
Did I feel left out?
No, I didn't resent it at all.

2596
02:00:42,199 --> 02:00:43,542
Even to me, she's pretty.

2597
02:00:43,879 --> 02:00:45,677
"Do whatever you want to do."

2598
02:00:46,799 --> 02:00:48,747
He's a really great older brother.

2599
02:00:48,845 --> 02:00:51,062
Doesn't she look a bit like Min Seo?

2600
02:00:51,087 --> 02:00:52,183
I think it's Jwa Hyeon.

2601
02:01:03,669 --> 02:01:05,029
When she was in school,

2602
02:01:05,054 --> 02:01:07,199
our financial situation wasn't great.

2603
02:01:07,382 --> 02:01:09,382
What my dad was thinking at the time was,

2604
02:01:09,588 --> 02:01:12,004
even if the three of us
were out working in the dirt,

2605
02:01:12,175 --> 02:01:14,540
he didn't want her living like that.

2606
02:01:15,982 --> 02:01:18,543
And even though our
parents were a bit far away,

2607
02:01:18,690 --> 02:01:20,879
I felt like I was right there for her.

2608
02:01:25,925 --> 02:01:28,987
I went to almost all of her performances.

2609
02:01:29,012 --> 02:01:29,888
I went quite a bit.

2610
02:01:30,112 --> 02:01:33,926
And she spent over ten years
dancing on stage.

2611
02:01:34,298 --> 02:01:36,528
Whenever she sets her mind on something,
she always sees it through.

2612
02:01:36,826 --> 02:01:39,398
That stubbornness and drive
to follow through...

2613
02:01:39,423 --> 02:01:40,699
I thought that was so cool.

2614
02:01:41,031 --> 02:01:43,835
When she danced in that monochrome,
skin-toned outfit.

2615
02:01:59,646 --> 02:02:01,687
All of my natural flair
went straight to her.

2616
02:02:04,666 --> 02:02:07,359
My dad always says he wants
to hear his baby girl's voice.

2617
02:02:07,384 --> 02:02:08,894
He goes, "Oh, Seo!"

2618
02:02:10,179 --> 02:02:11,440
- Seo.
- Huh?

2619
02:02:11,455 --> 02:02:12,353
(Kim Dong Su's younger sister,)

2620
02:02:12,378 --> 02:02:13,138
Seo.

2621
02:02:13,326 --> 02:02:15,768
Whatever you do,
I'll always have your back.

2622
02:02:15,793 --> 02:02:17,514
(Kim Min Seo)

2623
02:02:17,539 --> 02:02:18,725
Since I'm the youngest daughter,

2624
02:02:18,749 --> 02:02:21,640
I try hard not to let my parents
or my brother down.

2625
02:02:23,899 --> 02:02:24,659
Wrong!

2626
02:02:25,319 --> 02:02:27,279
How could we get every single one wrong?

2627
02:02:27,304 --> 02:02:28,113
Wrong.

2628
02:02:28,139 --> 02:02:29,481
None of us got it right.

2629
02:02:30,591 --> 02:02:32,088
I honestly had no clue.

2630
02:02:32,519 --> 02:02:35,499
Now that I look closely,
they look identical.

2631
02:02:35,958 --> 02:02:39,084
I loved dancing
ever since I was really little,

2632
02:02:39,108 --> 02:02:41,882
so our parents had me learn
belly dancing...

2633
02:02:41,906 --> 02:02:44,427
and traditional Korean dance
starting at age seven.

2634
02:02:44,451 --> 02:02:47,821
I got injured a lot,
and it took a huge toll on my body,

2635
02:02:47,845 --> 02:02:50,335
so once I got to college,
rather than performing myself,

2636
02:02:50,360 --> 02:02:54,630
teaching caught my interest
and seemed more fun,

2637
02:02:54,655 --> 02:02:56,180
so I went down that path.

2638
02:02:56,570 --> 02:02:59,160
My brother has the kind of personality
where he really likes to show off,

2639
02:02:59,184 --> 02:03:03,937
whereas I'm very introverted
and not the affectionate, cutesy type.

2640
02:03:03,961 --> 02:03:06,999
My brother is actually
the more affectionate, cutesy one.

2641
02:03:07,024 --> 02:03:08,186
Especially with our mom.

2642
02:03:08,211 --> 02:03:10,419
He'll go, "Mom, can you give me
some allowance?"

2643
02:03:10,505 --> 02:03:12,024
How is that cutesy?

2644
02:03:12,049 --> 02:03:14,193
That's Daegu-style charm right there.

2645
02:03:14,485 --> 02:03:17,630
Seeing him out in the countryside
with our dad, near our family,

2646
02:03:17,654 --> 02:03:20,594
helping out with the work like that,
is really admirable.

2647
02:03:20,619 --> 02:03:23,135
They've been doing that
since our grandfather's generation.

2648
02:03:23,732 --> 02:03:26,494
Since my dad wanted to work alongside me,

2649
02:03:26,518 --> 02:03:28,273
we farm during the busy seasons,

2650
02:03:28,297 --> 02:03:30,772
and we handle both the cattle
and the crops together.

2651
02:03:31,063 --> 02:03:32,811
Come on, hurry up!

2652
02:03:35,285 --> 02:03:37,420
I see him
in a totally different light now.

2653
02:03:37,445 --> 02:03:40,953
I thought he was a prickly city guy,
but he's not.

2654
02:03:41,245 --> 02:03:43,334
His charm is suddenly
coming out in full force.

2655
02:03:43,359 --> 02:03:46,346
Ever since I was little,
I loved operating machines,

2656
02:03:46,503 --> 02:03:49,015
so I always thought,
"I'm going to do that when I grow up."

2657
02:03:49,039 --> 02:03:50,216
When he was young,

2658
02:03:50,240 --> 02:03:53,734
he loved playing with excavators
and toys like that.

2659
02:03:53,759 --> 02:03:56,879
At his age, he probably wants to dress up
and go out to have fun,

2660
02:03:56,903 --> 02:03:59,371
yet he holds back and works so hard.

2661
02:04:08,969 --> 02:04:10,943
(Heart complete)

2662
02:04:11,239 --> 02:04:13,609
The elderly folks in the countryside
adore my brother.

2663
02:04:13,634 --> 02:04:15,020
They say he's so polite.

2664
02:04:15,375 --> 02:04:18,156
On top of that,
he always puts his family first.

2665
02:04:18,408 --> 02:04:19,958
I rely on Min Seo quite a bit.

2666
02:04:20,076 --> 02:04:21,414
Because more often than not,

2667
02:04:21,438 --> 02:04:23,395
Min Seo's judgment turns out to be
better than mine.

2668
02:04:30,869 --> 02:04:32,358
We're heading out to eat.

2669
02:04:32,383 --> 02:04:34,306
Let's go.

2670
02:04:34,930 --> 02:04:37,009
Off we go, finally.

2671
02:04:37,262 --> 02:04:38,410
How long did you two date?

2672
02:04:38,784 --> 02:04:39,784
A little over three years.

2673
02:04:39,809 --> 02:04:42,002
It was my first serious relationship,

2674
02:04:42,026 --> 02:04:44,920
and we ended up breaking up
over trust issues.

2675
02:04:44,944 --> 02:04:46,589
He knows all about
what happened back then.

2676
02:04:46,675 --> 02:04:48,213
I was riding the bus,

2677
02:04:48,237 --> 02:04:50,522
and I heard a sound coming from behind me.

2678
02:04:50,889 --> 02:04:52,591
She was looking out the window, crying.

2679
02:04:52,709 --> 02:04:54,289
It was so funny to me.

2680
02:04:55,068 --> 02:04:57,495
The heartbreak lasted about a week or two.

2681
02:04:58,049 --> 02:05:00,640
She'd be eating spicy stir-fried octopus
and suddenly burst into tears.

2682
02:05:00,665 --> 02:05:02,667
We were eating octopus,
and that song suddenly came on.

2683
02:05:03,089 --> 02:05:05,429
I think it hit her harder
because it was her first relationship.

2684
02:05:05,475 --> 02:05:07,739
I wondered how she ever ended
up dating a guy like that.

2685
02:05:07,888 --> 02:05:10,108
A guy I didn't approve of.

2686
02:05:10,529 --> 02:05:15,029
I prefer someone laid-back
who I can take things slow with,

2687
02:05:15,053 --> 02:05:16,949
whereas my brother moves pretty fast.

2688
02:05:17,134 --> 02:05:20,919
When my brother dates,
he goes all-in and gets super invested.

2689
02:05:21,302 --> 02:05:23,221
When I fall for someone, I fall hard.

2690
02:05:23,308 --> 02:05:25,856
My brother hasn't been
in a serious relationship...

2691
02:05:25,880 --> 02:05:26,880
in quite a while,

2692
02:05:26,904 --> 02:05:29,961
so I hope he meets someone good,
dates for a long time, and settles down.

2693
02:05:30,075 --> 02:05:31,930
I hope she gets along well with my sister.

2694
02:05:31,955 --> 02:05:35,035
Since my sister is pretty,
I hope she's attractive and sharp too.

2695
02:05:35,060 --> 02:05:36,001
A bit tall.

2696
02:05:36,101 --> 02:05:37,667
And I hope she works out a little.

2697
02:05:37,728 --> 02:05:39,271
If she acts all soft...

2698
02:05:40,422 --> 02:05:41,475
(Shaking head)

2699
02:05:41,689 --> 02:05:43,041
I'll go, "Watch how you behave!"

2700
02:05:43,468 --> 02:05:45,677
"I'm always watching you."
Something like that.

2701
02:05:47,849 --> 02:05:49,809
You're so big you're blocking the view!

2702
02:05:49,943 --> 02:05:52,129
- Can you do it with me on your back?
- Sure.

2703
02:05:53,229 --> 02:05:54,803
This feels so refreshing.

2704
02:05:55,429 --> 02:05:57,289
Sitting isn't as easy as it looks.

2705
02:06:08,802 --> 02:06:11,570
My brother is like a dad
and a friend rolled into one.

2706
02:06:11,888 --> 02:06:15,574
Taking care of me in place of Mom and Dad
is the biggest part of who he is to me.

2707
02:06:20,426 --> 02:06:21,580
This is delicious.

2708
02:06:24,382 --> 02:06:26,978
(Kim Dong Su)

2709
02:06:27,219 --> 02:06:29,329
(Kim Min Seo)

2710
02:06:29,594 --> 02:06:31,681
(Kim Bong Ja)

2711
02:06:39,459 --> 02:06:41,599
- He has total big-brother energy.
- Truly.

2712
02:06:41,865 --> 02:06:42,859
What's funny is,

2713
02:06:42,883 --> 02:06:46,438
Dong Su is so different around women
than he is around his family.

2714
02:06:46,463 --> 02:06:49,079
He's a much more wholesome,
down-to-earth guy.

2715
02:06:49,099 --> 02:06:51,843
He feels so genuine and dependable.

2716
02:06:51,999 --> 02:06:55,939
Watching this, I'm actually so touched
I feel like I might tear up.

2717
02:06:55,964 --> 02:06:56,975
Which part?

2718
02:06:57,342 --> 02:06:58,583
What part?

2719
02:06:59,415 --> 02:07:02,187
- It's understandable to get choked up.
- Why are you laughing?

2720
02:07:02,852 --> 02:07:05,657
Because I'm an only child,
so I don't know what that's like.

2721
02:07:05,682 --> 02:07:09,415
Seeing an older brother take care
of his sister so warmly,

2722
02:07:09,439 --> 02:07:14,340
and watching their banter,
just looks so wonderful.

2723
02:07:14,364 --> 02:07:19,003
I couldn't help thinking
how proud their parents must feel.

2724
02:07:19,173 --> 02:07:21,599
(The same morning)

2725
02:07:23,999 --> 02:07:24,910
You got a text.

2726
02:07:25,122 --> 02:07:26,499
(Shh! It's a secret message!)

2727
02:07:26,523 --> 02:07:29,396
(You can call your sibling
who went to the Love Hideout.)

2728
02:07:29,771 --> 02:07:33,306
As soon as I got that text,
my heart started racing,

2729
02:07:33,330 --> 02:07:35,871
and I thought, "I need to hurry upstairs."

2730
02:07:37,125 --> 02:07:39,023
I'll be right back
after making a quick call.

2731
02:07:39,065 --> 02:07:40,154
(Getting anxious)

2732
02:07:40,179 --> 02:07:41,526
Please handle cleaning up for me.

2733
02:07:42,827 --> 02:07:44,369
(Laughing)

2734
02:07:46,638 --> 02:07:50,498
I went straight upstairs
and called my brother.

2735
02:08:01,395 --> 02:08:03,275
(Dong Su's happy morning)

2736
02:08:04,709 --> 02:08:05,629
Hello?

2737
02:08:05,929 --> 02:08:07,509
Is Dong Su there by any chance?

2738
02:08:08,708 --> 02:08:09,320
Pardon?

2739
02:08:10,089 --> 02:08:11,529
Is Dong Su next to you right now?

2740
02:08:11,554 --> 02:08:13,091
- Yes, would you like me to put him on?
- Yes.

2741
02:08:13,769 --> 02:08:17,250
When I called, Yu Ra answered the phone,

2742
02:08:17,274 --> 02:08:19,183
so to keep her
from figuring out who I was,

2743
02:08:19,207 --> 02:08:21,967
I whispered breathily
and asked her to put my brother on.

2744
02:08:22,082 --> 02:08:22,768
Yes.

2745
02:08:23,462 --> 02:08:24,769
- Hello?
- Yes.

2746
02:08:25,349 --> 02:08:26,338
Mr. Dong Su.

2747
02:08:27,415 --> 02:08:28,039
Yes?

2748
02:08:29,769 --> 02:08:30,642
It's me.

2749
02:08:32,448 --> 02:08:32,928
Pardon?

2750
02:08:33,596 --> 02:08:35,280
It's me, Min Seo.

2751
02:08:36,595 --> 02:08:38,149
It's me, Min Seo.

2752
02:08:39,635 --> 02:08:40,686
Oh...

2753
02:08:41,708 --> 02:08:42,220
Yes.

2754
02:08:42,621 --> 02:08:44,090
Out of nowhere, she goes, "It's me."

2755
02:08:44,115 --> 02:08:45,156
It felt super awkward.

2756
02:08:45,181 --> 02:08:47,180
Yu Ra was sitting right there
looking super curious,

2757
02:08:47,204 --> 02:08:49,121
while I was on the phone.

2758
02:08:50,655 --> 02:08:55,303
Our check-out was at 10 a.m.,
and the call came five minutes before,

2759
02:08:55,328 --> 02:08:58,536
so he kept glancing at me,
totally flustered.

2760
02:09:00,575 --> 02:09:04,397
So why did you stay out overnight,

2761
02:09:05,277 --> 02:09:08,013
coming from someone who always
tells me to sleep at home?

2762
02:09:08,382 --> 02:09:09,080
Yes.

2763
02:09:09,916 --> 02:09:11,349
Could you give me a quick rundown...

2764
02:09:11,374 --> 02:09:13,852
of everything that happened
from yesterday until now?

2765
02:09:13,877 --> 02:09:15,210
I'm dying of curiosity.

2766
02:09:15,326 --> 02:09:18,308
We only have five minutes left
together here,

2767
02:09:18,332 --> 02:09:19,912
and it feels
like you're kind of interrupting.

2768
02:09:20,209 --> 02:09:21,871
Spend those five minutes on me instead.

2769
02:09:21,896 --> 02:09:23,589
- Oh, is that how it is?
- Yes.

2770
02:09:24,795 --> 02:09:29,309
Anyway, is she your type?

2771
02:09:29,515 --> 02:09:32,506
Since you were together yesterday,
you must have talked a lot.

2772
02:09:32,530 --> 02:09:33,304
Yes.

2773
02:09:33,509 --> 02:09:37,129
So did your interest in her go up?
Or is it just so-so?

2774
02:09:37,661 --> 02:09:38,843
Or did it go down?

2775
02:09:40,315 --> 02:09:41,780
She's right here with me right now.

2776
02:09:45,694 --> 02:09:48,349
(What a predicament.)

2777
02:09:49,749 --> 02:09:52,657
You just said you're out of time,
so hurry up and tell me!

2778
02:09:55,522 --> 02:09:57,462
I had no idea who was calling.

2779
02:09:57,499 --> 02:10:01,389
It felt like he was giving a briefing
on how things went at the hideout.

2780
02:10:01,414 --> 02:10:02,500
Who could that have been?

2781
02:10:03,309 --> 02:10:05,003
Could it be his sibling?

2782
02:10:05,122 --> 02:10:07,064
Are you heading back
to the house in five minutes?

2783
02:10:07,089 --> 02:10:08,006
Yes, that's right.

2784
02:10:11,625 --> 02:10:12,505
Hurry back.

2785
02:10:13,798 --> 02:10:14,879
Good work out there.

2786
02:10:15,138 --> 02:10:15,780
Yes.

2787
02:10:17,419 --> 02:10:19,106
I asked him a ton of questions,

2788
02:10:19,131 --> 02:10:22,014
but since he was sitting
right there with Yu Ra,

2789
02:10:22,038 --> 02:10:25,457
what he could actually say
was pretty limited.

2790
02:10:25,482 --> 02:10:28,593
So I kept it to simple questions.

2791
02:10:28,618 --> 02:10:31,452
(Wrapping up a short yet long phone call)

2792
02:10:33,954 --> 02:10:36,066
Was that an interview?

2793
02:10:40,081 --> 02:10:40,725
Look at him.

2794
02:10:40,749 --> 02:10:42,140
What is that reaction?

2795
02:10:42,371 --> 02:10:43,841
His eyes suddenly went all soft.

2796
02:10:44,089 --> 02:10:46,444
Knowing the context makes it even funnier.

2797
02:10:47,109 --> 02:10:49,881
Totally ruined the mood, seriously.
Completely killed the vibe.

2798
02:10:50,905 --> 02:10:55,306
You were annoyed that we only
had five minutes left together.

2799
02:10:55,728 --> 02:10:57,049
- Do you know who it was?
- No idea.

2800
02:10:57,395 --> 02:10:58,156
I don't know either.

2801
02:10:58,539 --> 02:10:59,491
I don't know.

2802
02:11:00,174 --> 02:11:01,267
(Gasps, covering mouth)

2803
02:11:01,292 --> 02:11:02,085
I have no idea.

2804
02:11:02,989 --> 02:11:05,063
Were they curious
about what happened here?

2805
02:11:05,348 --> 02:11:06,408
Seems like it.

2806
02:11:06,595 --> 02:11:08,324
(Reading the room)

2807
02:11:08,349 --> 02:11:09,709
Only one minute left now.

2808
02:11:09,942 --> 02:11:10,869
How was it for you?

2809
02:11:11,789 --> 02:11:13,772
Me? It was better than I expected.

2810
02:11:14,089 --> 02:11:15,407
- Really?
- The morning was.

2811
02:11:16,108 --> 02:11:18,610
I feel like we definitely got a lot closer
after coming here.

2812
02:11:18,920 --> 02:11:19,578
Right?

2813
02:11:19,716 --> 02:11:21,046
I feel the same way.

2814
02:11:22,142 --> 02:11:24,549
The two of us grew closer.

2815
02:11:24,942 --> 02:11:27,407
We got closer, though this closeness...

2816
02:11:27,431 --> 02:11:30,844
could just mean getting comfortable
with each other as friends,

2817
02:11:30,868 --> 02:11:32,645
or getting closer romantically.

2818
02:11:32,669 --> 02:11:35,493
I'm confused myself, and I think
Yu Ra probably feels the same way.

2819
02:11:35,518 --> 02:11:39,752
We talked a lot,
so we definitely got closer,

2820
02:11:39,776 --> 02:11:41,821
but given my personality,

2821
02:11:41,845 --> 02:11:45,925
there are still things
I'd like to learn about him.

2822
02:11:45,949 --> 02:11:48,949
And beyond how he is inside the hideout,

2823
02:11:48,950 --> 02:11:51,729
whether on a date
or just back at the house,

2824
02:11:51,753 --> 02:11:54,222
I want to see more sides of him,

2825
02:11:54,246 --> 02:11:56,748
so I think we still have a ways to go
in getting to know each other.

2826
02:11:56,928 --> 02:11:59,148
Everything that happened here
stays just between us.

2827
02:11:59,322 --> 02:12:00,085
Sounds good to me.

2828
02:12:19,837 --> 02:12:20,847
(Ding-dong)

2829
02:12:20,872 --> 02:12:21,873
- It's here.
- Hey.

2830
02:12:22,119 --> 02:12:24,030
"Your first date is an activity date..."

2831
02:12:24,054 --> 02:12:26,659
"where you can fully enjoy
the summer of Jeju Island."

2832
02:12:26,752 --> 02:12:28,952
"Your choices remain a secret
until departure."

2833
02:12:29,085 --> 02:12:30,909
It's impossible to predict.

2834
02:12:31,105 --> 02:12:33,151
Who is it? Who could it be?

2835
02:12:33,565 --> 02:12:35,356
(Their first time alone together)

2836
02:12:36,186 --> 02:12:37,656
This is so nice.

2837
02:12:38,179 --> 02:12:39,624
I think my heart was fluttering.

2838
02:12:40,619 --> 02:12:42,399
She really feels like a girlfriend.

2839
02:12:42,571 --> 02:12:44,262
I wanted to try this with you too.

2840
02:12:44,406 --> 02:12:46,064
I feel like we've gotten super close.

2841
02:12:46,445 --> 02:12:48,360
Will we get to spend time like this again?

2842
02:12:48,859 --> 02:12:52,536
I think today will be a turning point.

2843
02:12:52,759 --> 02:12:54,239
I came back feeling
so refreshed and recharged.

2844
02:12:54,264 --> 02:12:56,107
You really took on the MC role out there.

2845
02:12:56,565 --> 02:12:59,177
They came back with hearts in their eyes.

2846
02:13:02,280 --> 02:13:04,030
(Day 2 in the house:
Who made your heart flutter?)

2847
02:13:04,059 --> 02:13:05,462
Just like this, right away?

2848
02:13:05,487 --> 02:13:06,117
Right away?

2849
02:13:06,851 --> 02:13:09,479
(Sending their hearts
for the very first time since moving in)

2850
02:13:09,639 --> 02:13:11,556
Should I send mine to her? Will I get one?

2851
02:13:11,581 --> 02:13:13,621
How much bolder do I need to be?

2852
02:13:14,412 --> 02:13:16,612
"Everyone's photo albums have arrived."

2853
02:13:16,799 --> 02:13:19,030
"What kind of work does Jin Sung do?"

2854
02:13:19,073 --> 02:13:21,153
(Everyone's professions are revealed.)

2855
02:13:22,279 --> 02:13:23,468
Even our jobs?

2856
